  <div class="foot"><b>EkGuru Learning</b> — Compiled &amp; updated by <b>PRAKASH</b> | Topic 6: OSI Layers in Detail</div>
</div>

<script>
const QUESTIONS = [{"q": ["Which sub-layer of the Data Link Layer is responsible for flow control and error control?", "Data Link Layer का कौन-सा sub-layer flow control और error control के लिए ज़िम्मेदार होता है?"], "opts": [["MAC", "MAC"], ["LLC (Logical Link Control)", "LLC (Logical Link Control)"], ["PVC", "PVC"], ["None of the above", "None of the above"]], "ans": 1, "exp": ["LLC (Logical Link Control) sub-layer flow control, error control और Network layer को service interface देता है; MAC sub-layer physical addressing और channel access संभालता है. | Nukta: DLL = MAC + LLC — याद रखो: MAC = addressing + medium access, LLC = flow + error + interface.", "LLC (Logical Link Control) sub-layer flow control, error control और Network layer को service interface देता है; MAC sub-layer physical addressing और channel access संभालता है. | DLL = MAC + LLC — याद रखो: MAC = addressing + medium access, LLC = flow + error + interface."], "src": "BCI Subject Test-8.pdf", "sec": "Section A — Data Link Layer: Flow & Error Control", "diff": "easy", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["SSC Computer Awareness", "RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "JNV TAT"]}, {"q": ["Which of the following functions are performed by the Data Link Layer? (1) Framing (2) Error Detection (3) Flow Control (4) Path Determination", "निम्न में से कौन-से कार्य Data Link Layer करता है? (1) Framing (2) Error Detection (3) Flow Control (4) Path Determination"], "opts": [["1, 2 and 3 only", "1, 2 and 3 only"], ["1 and 4 only", "1 and 4 only"], ["2 and 4 only", "2 and 4 only"], ["1, 2, 3 and 4", "1, 2, 3 and 4"]], "ans": 0, "exp": ["Framing, Error Detection और Flow Control — तीनों Data Link Layer के काम हैं. Path Determination यानी routing Network Layer का काम है. | Nukta: याद रखो: DLL में F-E-F (Framing, Error, Flow) + addressing; रास्ता चुनना (routing) Network Layer का.", "Framing, Error Detection और Flow Control — तीनों Data Link Layer के काम हैं. Path Determination यानी routing Network Layer का काम है. | याद रखो: DLL में F-E-F (Framing, Error, Flow) + addressing; रास्ता चुनना (routing) Network Layer का."], "src": "BCI Subject Test-9.pdf", "sec": "Section A — Data Link Layer: Flow & Error Control", "diff": "easy", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["SSC Computer Awareness", "RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "JNV TAT"]}, {"q": ["Which of the following statements about MAC and LLC sublayers is TRUE? (1) MAC sublayer handles physical addressing (2) LLC sublayer provides error control and flow control (3) MAC sublayer performs routing", "MAC और LLC sub-layers के बारे में कौन-सा कथन सही है? (1) MAC sub-layer physical addressing संभालता है (2) LLC sub-layer error control और flow control देता है (3) MAC sub-layer routing करता है"], "opts": [["1 and 2 only", "1 and 2 only"], ["2 and 3 only", "2 and 3 only"], ["1 and 3 only", "1 and 3 only"], ["1, 2 and 3", "1, 2 and 3"]], "ans": 0, "exp": ["(1) सही — MAC physical (MAC) addressing संभालता है; (2) सही — LLC में flow और error control होता है; (3) गलत — MAC में routing नहीं होती, routing Network Layer का काम है. | Nukta: MAC = addressing + channel access; LLC = flow + error + interface; routing = Network Layer.", "(1) सही — MAC physical (MAC) addressing संभालता है; (2) सही — LLC में flow और error control होता है; (3) गलत — MAC में routing नहीं होती, routing Network Layer का काम है. | MAC = addressing + channel access; LLC = flow + error + interface; routing = Network Layer."], "src": "BCI Subject Test-9.pdf", "sec": "Section A — Data Link Layer: Flow & Error Control", "diff": "medium", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "statement", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["Which of the following is NOT a responsibility of the LLC sublayer?", "निम्न में से कौन-सा LLC sub-layer की ज़िम्मेदारी नहीं है?"], "opts": [["Flow control", "Flow control"], ["Error control", "Error control"], ["Service interface to Network layer", "Service interface to Network layer"], ["Physical addressing", "Physical addressing"]], "ans": 3, "exp": ["Physical addressing (MAC address) MAC sub-layer का काम है — LLC नहीं. LLC flow control, error control और Network layer को interface देता है. | Nukta: MAC = Media Access Control = addressing; LLC = Logical Link Control = flow/error.", "Physical addressing (MAC address) MAC sub-layer का काम है — LLC नहीं. LLC flow control, error control और Network layer को interface देता है. | MAC = Media Access Control = addressing; LLC = Logical Link Control = flow/error."], "src": "BCI Subject Test-9.pdf", "sec": "Section A — Data Link Layer: Flow & Error Control", "diff": "medium", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["Which of the following is NOT a function of the Data Link Layer?", "निम्न में से कौन-सा Data Link Layer का function नहीं है?"], "opts": [["Framing", "Framing"], ["Error detection", "Error detection"], ["Error correction", "Error correction"], ["Routing", "Routing"]], "ans": 3, "exp": ["Routing (रास्ता तय करना) Network Layer का function है. Data Link Layer framing, error detection/correction और flow control करता है. | Nukta: DLL = next-hop delivery (frame); Network = end-to-end delivery (packet + route).", "Routing (रास्ता तय करना) Network Layer का function है. Data Link Layer framing, error detection/correction और flow control करता है. | DLL = next-hop delivery (frame); Network = end-to-end delivery (packet + route)."], "src": "BCI Subject Test-9.pdf + CN Topic Test-04.pdf", "sec": "Section A — Data Link Layer: Flow & Error Control", "diff": "medium", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["The Frame Check Sequence (FCS) field in an Ethernet frame is used for:", "Ethernet frame में Frame Check Sequence (FCS) field किस काम आता है?"], "opts": [["Flow control", "Flow control"], ["Address resolution", "Address resolution"], ["Error detection using CRC", "Error detection using CRC"], ["Medium access", "Medium access"]], "ans": 2, "exp": ["FCS field में CRC (Cyclic Redundancy Check) का result होता है जिससे receiver frame की errors detect करता है. | Nukta: FCS = CRC = error detection. Ethernet error correct नहीं करता, बस detect करके frame drop करता है.", "FCS field में CRC (Cyclic Redundancy Check) का result होता है जिससे receiver frame की errors detect करता है. | FCS = CRC = error detection. Ethernet error correct नहीं करता, बस detect करके frame drop करता है."], "src": "BCI Subject Test-9.pdf", "sec": "Section A — Data Link Layer: Flow & Error Control", "diff": "easy", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["SSC Computer Awareness", "RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "JNV TAT"]}, {"q": ["Which of the following techniques uses both acknowledgments and sequence numbers?", "निम्न में से कौन-सी technique acknowledgments और sequence numbers दोनों उपयोग करती है?"], "opts": [["Go-Back-N", "Go-Back-N"], ["Stop-and-Wait", "Stop-and-Wait"], ["Selective Repeat", "Selective Repeat"], ["All of the above", "All of the above"]], "ans": 3, "exp": ["Stop-and-Wait, Go-Back-N और Selective Repeat — तीनों ARQ protocols sequence numbers और acknowledgments दोनों उपयोग करते हैं. | Nukta: ARQ = Automatic Repeat reQuest — बिना sequence/ack के कोई ARQ चल ही नहीं सकता.", "Stop-and-Wait, Go-Back-N और Selective Repeat — तीनों ARQ protocols sequence numbers और acknowledgments दोनों उपयोग करते हैं. | ARQ = Automatic Repeat reQuest — बिना sequence/ack के कोई ARQ चल ही नहीं सकता."], "src": "Unit Test -2 Solutions.pdf (OCR) + CN Topic Test-04.pdf", "sec": "Section A — Data Link Layer: Flow & Error Control", "diff": "hard", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["GATE CS", "UGC-NET 087", "RPSC Programmer", "RPSC ACP/DD"]}, {"q": ["Error control is the process of detecting and correcting errors, while ______ is a mechanism to ensure the efficient delivery of data.", "Error control, errors को detect और correct करने की प्रक्रिया है, जबकि ______ data के कुशल delivery का mechanism है."], "opts": [["Error control, Flow control", "Error control, Flow control"], ["Process control, Network control", "Process control, Network control"], ["Session control, Flow control", "Session control, Flow control"], ["OSI Control, Data control", "OSI Control, Data control"]], "ans": 0, "exp": ["पहला blank Error control (errors detect+correct), दूसरा Flow control (sender की speed receiver के हिसाब से) — दोनों Data Link/Transport layers में मिलते हैं. | Nukta: Error = putting right; Flow = maintaining balance. Both are separate jobs.", "पहला blank Error control (errors detect+correct), दूसरा Flow control (sender की speed receiver के हिसाब से) — दोनों Data Link/Transport layers में मिलते हैं. | Error = सही करना; Flow = संतुलन बनाना. दोनों अलग-अलग काम हैं."], "src": "CN Topic Test-02.pdf", "sec": "Section A — Data Link Layer: Flow & Error Control", "diff": "medium", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["______ control refers to a set of procedures used to restrict the amount of data that the sender can send before waiting for acknowledgment.", "______ control उन procedures का समूह है जो sender द्वारा acknowledgment की प्रतीक्षा से पहले भेजे जाने वाले data की मात्रा सीमित करते हैं."], "opts": [["Flow", "Flow"], ["Error", "Error"], ["Transmission", "Transmission"], ["Access control", "Access control"]], "ans": 0, "exp": ["Flow control sender को रोकता है ताकि receiver का buffer न भरे — इसलिए acknowledgment आने तक data सीमित रहता है. | Nukta: Flow control = the balance between sender and receiver; this definition is asked again and again in exams.", "Flow control sender को रोकता है ताकि receiver का buffer न भरे — इसलिए acknowledgment आने तक data सीमित रहता है. | Flow control = sender↔receiver के बीच का संतुलन; यही definition परीक्षा में बार-बार आती है."], "src": "Unit Test -2 Solutions.pdf (OCR), p17", "sec": "Section A — Data Link Layer: Flow & Error Control", "diff": "medium", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["What is the main purpose of the Sliding Window in TCP?", "TCP में Sliding Window का मुख्य उद्देश्य क्या है?"], "opts": [["Address resolution", "Address resolution"], ["Flow control", "Flow control"], ["Error detection", "Error detection"], ["Encryption", "Encryption"]], "ans": 1, "exp": ["Sliding window से receiver बताता है कि वह कितना data ले सकता है — यही flow control है. | Nukta: TCP window = receiver की capacity का advertisement; इसीलिए इसे flow control कहते हैं.", "Sliding window से receiver बताता है कि वह कितना data ले सकता है — यही flow control है. | TCP window = receiver की capacity का advertisement; इसीलिए इसे flow control कहते हैं."], "src": "CN Topic Test 5.pdf", "sec": "Section A — Data Link Layer: Flow & Error Control", "diff": "medium", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["Flow control prevents which of the following issues?", "Flow control निम्न में से किस समस्या को रोकता है?"], "opts": [["Deadlock", "Deadlock"], ["Congestion collapse", "Congestion collapse"], ["Overflow of the receiver's buffer", "Overflow of the receiver's buffer"], ["Packet routing error", "Packet routing error"]], "ans": 2, "exp": ["Flow control receiver के buffer को overflow होने से बचाता है — sender उतना ही भेजता है जितना receiver संभाल सके. | Nukta: Flow control = दोनों के बीच; Congestion control = पूरे network के लिए.", "Flow control receiver के buffer को overflow होने से बचाता है — sender उतना ही भेजता है जितना receiver संभाल सके. | Flow control = दोनों के बीच; Congestion control = पूरे network के लिए."], "src": "CN Topic Test-04.pdf", "sec": "Section A — Data Link Layer: Flow & Error Control", "diff": "medium", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["In the TCP header, the acknowledgment field value represents:", "TCP header में acknowledgment field का मान किसे दर्शाता है?"], "opts": [["Number of previous bytes received", "Number of previous bytes received"], ["Total number of bytes to receive", "Total number of bytes to receive"], ["Sequence number of the next byte expected", "Sequence number of the next byte expected"], ["Sequence of zeros and ones", "Sequence of zeros and ones"]], "ans": 2, "exp": ["TCP का ACK number अगली expected byte का sequence number है — यानी अब तक सब कुछ उससे पहले मिल चुका है (cumulative acknowledgment). | Nukta: TCP bytes गिनता है, packets नहीं — ACK = 'next byte भेजो'.", "TCP का ACK number अगली expected byte का sequence number है — यानी अब तक सब कुछ उससे पहले मिल चुका है (cumulative acknowledgment). | TCP bytes गिनता है, packets नहीं — ACK = 'next byte भेजो'."], "src": "CN Topic Test-04.pdf", "sec": "Section A — Data Link Layer: Flow & Error Control", "diff": "hard", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["GATE CS", "UGC-NET 087", "RPSC Programmer", "RPSC ACP/DD"]}, {"q": ["In Stop-and-Wait ARQ, after sending one frame, the sender:", "Stop-and-Wait ARQ में एक frame भेजने के बाद sender:"], "opts": [["Waits for acknowledgment", "Waits for acknowledgment"], ["Sends the next frame immediately", "Sends the next frame immediately"], ["Stops transmission permanently", "Stops transmission permanently"], ["Sends a NAK", "Sends a NAK"]], "ans": 0, "exp": ["Stop-and-Wait में sender एक frame भेजकर उसके acknowledgment का इंतज़ार करता है. | Nukta: Because of this waiting, its name became 'Stop-and-Wait'.", "Stop-and-Wait में sender एक frame भेजकर उसके acknowledgment का इंतज़ार करता है. | इसी waiting के कारण इसका नाम 'Stop-and-Wait' पड़ा."], "src": "CN Topic Test-04.pdf", "sec": "Section A — Data Link Layer: Flow & Error Control", "diff": "medium", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["In Stop-and-Wait protocol, the sender sends:", "Stop-and-Wait protocol में sender भेजता है:"], "opts": [["Multiple frames at once", "Multiple frames at once"], ["One frame at a time", "One frame at a time"], ["Acknowledgments only", "Acknowledgments only"], ["Data without waiting", "Data without waiting"]], "ans": 1, "exp": ["Stop-and-Wait में एक समय में सिर्फ एक frame outstanding रहता है. | Nukta: Window size = 1 — इसीलिए एक-एक frame.", "Stop-and-Wait में एक समय में सिर्फ एक frame outstanding रहता है. | Window size = 1 — इसीलिए एक-एक frame."], "src": "CN Topic Test-04.pdf", "sec": "Section A — Data Link Layer: Flow & Error Control", "diff": "medium", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["What is the window size in Stop-and-Wait ARQ?", "Stop-and-Wait ARQ में window size कितनी होती है?"], "opts": [["0", "0"], ["1", "1"], ["N", "N"], ["2", "2"]], "ans": 1, "exp": ["Stop-and-Wait has window size 1 — only one frame can be out without an ACK. | Nukta: Window = 1 ↔ एक frame at a time — दोनों एक ही बात हैं.", "Stop-and-Wait की window size 1 होती है — एक ही frame बिना ACK के भेजा जा सकता है. | Window = 1 ↔ एक frame at a time — दोनों एक ही बात हैं."], "src": "CN Topic Test-04.pdf", "sec": "Section A — Data Link Layer: Flow & Error Control", "diff": "medium", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["What is the main disadvantage of Stop-and-Wait flow control?", "Stop-and-Wait flow control की मुख्य कमी क्या है?"], "opts": [["Complexity", "Complexity"], ["Low efficiency due to waiting", "Low efficiency due to waiting"], ["High memory usage", "High memory usage"], ["Frame loss", "Frame loss"]], "ans": 1, "exp": ["Waiting after every frame leaves the line idle — efficiency drops sharply, especially on long-distance links. | Nukta: Waiting = idle time = कम utilization. इसीलिए Sliding Window आया.", "हर frame के बाद इंतज़ार करने से line बेकार खाली रहती है — खासकर long-distance links पर efficiency बहुत गिर जाती है. | Waiting = idle time = कम utilization. इसीलिए Sliding Window आया."], "src": "CN Topic Test-04.pdf", "sec": "Section A — Data Link Layer: Flow & Error Control", "diff": "medium", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["A Stop-and-Wait ARQ channel has high latency and large bandwidth. What problem occurs?", "Stop-and-Wait ARQ channel पर latency ज़्यादा और bandwidth बड़ी हो तो क्या समस्या होती है?"], "opts": [["High throughput", "High throughput"], ["Low channel utilization", "Low channel utilization"], ["CRC failure", "CRC failure"], ["Frame duplication", "Frame duplication"]], "ans": 1, "exp": ["High latency में ACK देर से आता है और बड़ी bandwidth खाली रह जाती है — channel utilization बहुत कम हो जाता है. इसीलिए high-BDP links पर Sliding Window protocols उपयोग होते हैं. | Nukta: Bandwidth × Delay (BDP) जितना बड़ा, Stop-and-Wait उतना बेकार.", "High latency में ACK देर से आता है और बड़ी bandwidth खाली रह जाती है — channel utilization बहुत कम हो जाता है. इसीलिए high-BDP links पर Sliding Window protocols उपयोग होते हैं. | Bandwidth × Delay (BDP) जितना बड़ा, Stop-and-Wait उतना बेकार."], "src": "BCI Subject Test-8.pdf", "sec": "Section A — Data Link Layer: Flow & Error Control", "diff": "easy", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["SSC Computer Awareness", "RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "JNV TAT"]}, {"q": ["In Stop-and-Wait ARQ, what happens when a frame is lost?", "Stop-and-Wait ARQ में frame खो जाए तो क्या होता है?"], "opts": [["Receiver sends NAK", "Receiver sends NAK"], ["Sender retransmits after timeout", "Sender retransmits after timeout"], ["Receiver retransmits", "Receiver retransmits"], ["No retransmission", "No retransmission"]], "ans": 1, "exp": ["If the ACK does not arrive, the sender's timeout timer fires and it retransmits that frame. | Nukta: Lost frame + timeout = retransmission. Receiver कभी retransmit नहीं करता.", "ACK न आने पर sender का timeout timer बजता है और वह frame दोबारा भेजता है. | Lost frame + timeout = retransmission. Receiver कभी retransmit नहीं करता."], "src": "CN Topic Test-04.pdf", "sec": "Section A — Data Link Layer: Flow & Error Control", "diff": "medium", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["For Stop-and-Wait ARQ, for 10 data packets sent, ............ acknowledgements are needed.", "Stop-and-Wait ARQ में 10 data packets भेजने पर ............ acknowledgements चाहिए होते हैं."], "opts": [["9", "9"], ["20", "20"], ["11", "11"], ["10", "10"]], "ans": 3, "exp": ["हर packet का अपना ACK चाहिए — 10 packets → 10 ACKs. | Nukta: RPSC official key (d) — Stop-and-Wait में ack:packet अनुपात 1:1.", "हर packet का अपना ACK चाहिए — 10 packets → 10 ACKs. | RPSC official key (d) — Stop-and-Wait में ack:packet अनुपात 1:1."], "src": "RPSC Programmer 2024 Paper-1 (with official key)", "sec": "Section A — Data Link Layer: Flow & Error Control", "diff": "hard", "stype": "verified_official_pyq", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["In Go-Back-N ARQ, if an error is detected in a frame:", "Go-Back-N ARQ में किसी frame में error मिले तो:"], "opts": [["Only that frame is retransmitted", "Only that frame is retransmitted"], ["All frames are ignored", "All frames are ignored"], ["That frame and all subsequent outstanding frames are retransmitted", "That frame and all subsequent outstanding frames are retransmitted"], ["No frame is retransmitted", "No frame is retransmitted"]], "ans": 2, "exp": ["Go-Back-N में receiver केवल in-order frames रखता है; गलत frame के बाद के सारे frames छोड़ देता है और sender उस frame से आगे के सभी outstanding frames दोबारा भेजता है. | Nukta: GBN = 'from where you slipped, start again' — in Selective Repeat only the wrong frame is resent.", "Go-Back-N में receiver केवल in-order frames रखता है; गलत frame के बाद के सारे frames छोड़ देता है और sender उस frame से आगे के सभी outstanding frames दोबारा भेजता है. | GBN = 'जहाँ चूक, वहाँ से फिर से' — Selective Repeat में सिर्फ गलत frame दोबारा जाता है."], "src": "CN Topic Test-04.pdf", "sec": "Section A — Data Link Layer: Flow & Error Control", "diff": "medium", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["In the ______ protocol, if no acknowledgment for a frame has arrived, we resend all outstanding frames.", "______ protocol में, किसी frame का acknowledgment न आए तो हम सभी outstanding frames दोबारा भेजते हैं."], "opts": [["Stop-and-Wait ARQ", "Stop-and-Wait ARQ"], ["Go-Back-N ARQ", "Go-Back-N ARQ"], ["Selective-Repeat ARQ", "Selective-Repeat ARQ"], ["Both B and C", "Both B and C"]], "ans": 1, "exp": ["'सभी outstanding frames दोबारा भेजना' Go-Back-N की पहचान है. | Nukta: GBN = Go Back N — everything up to N is resent; SR = only the wrong one.", "'सभी outstanding frames दोबारा भेजना' Go-Back-N की पहचान है. | GBN = Go Back N — Nवें तक सब दोबारा; SR = सिर्फ गलत वाला."], "src": "Unit Test -2 Solutions.pdf (OCR), p8", "sec": "Section A — Data Link Layer: Flow & Error Control", "diff": "hard", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["GATE CS", "UGC-NET 087", "RPSC Programmer", "RPSC ACP/DD"]}, {"q": ["A Go-Back-N sender uses window size 4. Frame 2 is lost. What happens after the receiver receives frames 3 and 4?", "Go-Back-N sender window size 4 उपयोग करता है. Frame 2 खो जाता है. Receiver को frames 3 और 4 मिलने के बाद क्या होता है?"], "opts": [["Receiver stores frames 3 and 4 in buffer", "Receiver stores frames 3 and 4 in buffer"], ["Receiver sends ACK for frame 4", "Receiver sends ACK for frame 4"], ["Receiver discards frames 3 and 4", "Receiver discards frames 3 and 4"], ["Receiver acts like Selective Repeat", "Receiver acts like Selective Repeat"]], "ans": 2, "exp": ["A GBN receiver wants only the next in-order frame — when frame 2 is lost, 3 and 4 are out-of-order, so they are discarded. | Nukta: GBN receiver dumb होता है (buffer नहीं रखता); SR receiver smart (buffer रखता है).", "GBN receiver सिर्फ अगली in-order frame चाहता है — frame 2 खोने पर 3 और 4 out-of-order हैं, इसलिए उन्हें discard कर दिया जाता है. | GBN receiver dumb होता है (buffer नहीं रखता); SR receiver smart (buffer रखता है)."], "src": "BCI Subject Test-8.pdf", "sec": "Section A — Data Link Layer: Flow & Error Control", "diff": "easy", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["SSC Computer Awareness", "RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "JNV TAT"]}, {"q": ["In Go-Back-N ARQ, if 6 is the number of bits for the sequence number, then the maximum size of the send window must be:", "Go-Back-N ARQ में sequence number के 6 bits हों तो send window का अधिकतम आकार कितना होगा?"], "opts": [["63", "63"], ["61", "61"], ["31", "31"], ["64", "64"]], "ans": 0, "exp": ["GBN में maximum window = 2ⁿ − 1 = 2⁶ − 1 = 63. | Nukta: GBN/SW का window formula अलग है SR से — GBN: 2ⁿ−1, SR: 2ⁿ⁻¹.", "GBN में maximum window = 2ⁿ − 1 = 2⁶ − 1 = 63. | GBN/SW का window formula अलग है SR से — GBN: 2ⁿ−1, SR: 2ⁿ⁻¹."], "src": "Unit Test -2 Solutions.pdf (OCR), p9", "sec": "Section A — Data Link Layer: Flow & Error Control", "diff": "hard", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "numerical", "tags": ["GATE CS", "UGC-NET 087", "RPSC Programmer", "RPSC ACP/DD"]}, {"q": ["In a Go-Back-N protocol, if the window size = 63, how many sequence number bits are required?", "Go-Back-N protocol में window size = 63 हो तो sequence number के कितने bits चाहिए?"], "opts": [["5", "5"], ["6", "6"], ["7", "7"], ["8", "8"]], "ans": 1, "exp": ["Window = 2ⁿ − 1 → 63 = 2⁶ − 1, इसलिए n = 6 bits. | Nukta: The reverse of the question above — memorise the formula both ways.", "Window = 2ⁿ − 1 → 63 = 2⁶ − 1, इसलिए n = 6 bits. | उपर वाले प्रश्न का उल्टा — यही formula दोनों तरफ से याद रखो."], "src": "BCI Subject Test-8.pdf", "sec": "Section A — Data Link Layer: Flow & Error Control", "diff": "medium", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "numerical", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["The maximum number of outstanding frames in Selective Repeat (with N sequence numbers) is:", "Selective Repeat में outstanding frames की अधिकतम संख्या (N sequence numbers के साथ) होती है:"], "opts": [["N", "N"], ["N − 1", "N − 1"], ["N/2", "N/2"], ["2N", "2N"]], "ans": 2, "exp": ["Selective Repeat में sender और receiver दोनों की windows अलग-अलग होती हैं, इसलिए window ≤ N/2 — यानी अधिकतम N/2 frames outstanding. | Nukta: SR: window N/2 (दो windows), GBN: window N−1 (एक window).", "Selective Repeat में sender और receiver दोनों की windows अलग-अलग होती हैं, इसलिए window ≤ N/2 — यानी अधिकतम N/2 frames outstanding. | SR: window N/2 (दो windows), GBN: window N−1 (एक window)."], "src": "CN Topic Test-04.pdf", "sec": "Section A — Data Link Layer: Flow & Error Control", "diff": "hard", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["GATE CS", "UGC-NET 087", "RPSC Programmer", "RPSC ACP/DD"]}, {"q": ["A Selective Repeat sliding window protocol uses a window size of 7 with 3-bit sequence numbers. Is it valid?", "Selective Repeat sliding window protocol में 3-bit sequence numbers के साथ window size 7 क्या वैध है?"], "opts": [["Valid", "Valid"], ["Invalid – violates the maximum window rule", "Invalid – violates the maximum window rule"], ["Valid only for piggybacking", "Valid only for piggybacking"], ["Valid only with Selective Repeat", "Valid only with Selective Repeat"]], "ans": 1, "exp": ["3-bit sequence numbers पर SR की maximum window = 2³⁻¹ = 4 होती है; 7 > 4 होने से receiver new और old frames में फ़र्क नहीं कर पाएगा — इसलिए अवैध. | Nukta: SR window ≤ 2ⁿ⁻¹; GBN window ≤ 2ⁿ − 1. यही फ़र्क याद रखो.", "3-bit sequence numbers पर SR की maximum window = 2³⁻¹ = 4 होती है; 7 > 4 होने से receiver new और old frames में फ़र्क नहीं कर पाएगा — इसलिए अवैध. | SR window ≤ 2ⁿ⁻¹; GBN window ≤ 2ⁿ − 1. यही फ़र्क याद रखो."], "src": "BCI Subject Test-8.pdf", "sec": "Section A — Data Link Layer: Flow & Error Control", "diff": "medium", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "numerical", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["Which protocol has better bandwidth utilization?", "किस protocol का bandwidth utilization बेहतर होता है?"], "opts": [["Stop-and-Wait", "Stop-and-Wait"], ["Selective Repeat", "Selective Repeat"], ["Go-Back-N", "Go-Back-N"], ["None of the above", "None of the above"]], "ans": 1, "exp": ["Selective Repeat resends only the lost frames and also buffers out-of-order frames — bandwidth utilisation is the highest. | Nukta: Efficiency क्रम: Selective Repeat > Go-Back-N > Stop-and-Wait.", "Selective Repeat सिर्फ खोए frames दोबारा भेजता है और out-of-order frames भी buffer कर लेता है — bandwidth सबसे ज़्यादा उपयोग होती है. | Efficiency क्रम: Selective Repeat > Go-Back-N > Stop-and-Wait."], "src": "CN Topic Test-04.pdf", "sec": "Section A — Data Link Layer: Flow & Error Control", "diff": "medium", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["A noisy channel uses a Hamming code with minimum distance 3. What can it guarantee?", "एक noisy channel पर minimum distance 3 वाला Hamming code क्या guarantee दे सकता है?"], "opts": [["Detect 2-bit errors", "Detect 2-bit errors"], ["Correct 2-bit errors", "Correct 2-bit errors"], ["Correct 3-bit errors", "Correct 3-bit errors"], ["Detect 4-bit errors", "Detect 4-bit errors"]], "ans": 0, "exp": ["Minimum distance d = 3 वाला code 2 errors detect या 1 error correct कर सकता है (d ≥ t + 1 for detection, d ≥ 2t + 1 for correction). | Nukta: d=3 → detect 2 या correct 1 — 'correct 2' के लिए d ≥ 5 चाहिए.", "Minimum distance d = 3 वाला code 2 errors detect या 1 error correct कर सकता है (d ≥ t + 1 for detection, d ≥ 2t + 1 for correction). | d=3 → detect 2 या correct 1 — 'correct 2' के लिए d ≥ 5 चाहिए."], "src": "BCI Subject Test-8.pdf", "sec": "Section A — Data Link Layer: Flow & Error Control", "diff": "easy", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "numerical", "tags": ["SSC Computer Awareness", "RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "JNV TAT"]}, {"q": ["What is the Hamming distance between the two codes 10010010 and 11011001?", "दो codes 10010010 और 11011001 के बीच Hamming distance कितनी है?"], "opts": [["3", "3"], ["4", "4"], ["6", "6"], ["2", "2"]], "ans": 1, "exp": ["Align the two codes and count differing bits: positions 2, 5, 7 and 8 differ — 4 differences in all. Hamming distance = number of differing bits = 4. | Nukta: Hamming distance = XOR के बाद 1s की गिनती.", "दोनों codes को align करके अलग-अलग bits गिनो: positions 2, 5, 7 और 8 बदलती हैं — कुल 4 अंतर. Hamming distance = अलग bits की संख्या = 4. | Hamming distance = XOR के बाद 1s की गिनती."], "src": "Unit Test -2 Solutions.pdf (OCR), p28", "sec": "Section A — Data Link Layer: Flow & Error Control", "diff": "medium", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["The Hamming distance between two code words can easily be found if we apply the ______ operation.", "दो code words के बीच Hamming distance आसानी से मिल जाती है यदि हम ______ operation लगाएँ."], "opts": [["XOR", "XOR"], ["XNOR", "XNOR"], ["OR", "OR"], ["AND", "AND"]], "ans": 0, "exp": ["XOR gives 1 where the bits differ — counting the 1s gives the Hamming distance. | Nukta: XOR = difference counter. दूसरे operations यह नहीं बताते.", "XOR करने पर जहाँ bits अलग होती हैं वहाँ 1 आता है — 1s की गिनती ही Hamming distance है. | XOR = difference counter. दूसरे operations यह नहीं बताते."], "src": "Unit Test -2 Solutions.pdf (OCR), p35", "sec": "Section A — Data Link Layer: Flow & Error Control", "diff": "medium", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["Any coding scheme for error control needs to have at least the parameters of:", "Error control के लिए किसी भी coding scheme में कम से कम निम्न parameters होने चाहिए:"], "opts": [["codeword size", "codeword size"], ["dataword size", "dataword size"], ["minimum Hamming distance", "minimum Hamming distance"], ["All of them", "All of them"]], "ans": 3, "exp": ["किसी भी error-control code को परिभाषित करने के लिए codeword size, dataword size और minimum Hamming distance — तीनों ज़रूरी हैं. | Nukta: Code = (n, k, d) — n = codeword, k = dataword, d = distance. तीनों से ही code की ताक़त पता चलती है.", "किसी भी error-control code को परिभाषित करने के लिए codeword size, dataword size और minimum Hamming distance — तीनों ज़रूरी हैं. | Code = (n, k, d) — n = codeword, k = dataword, d = distance. तीनों से ही code की ताक़त पता चलती है."], "src": "Unit Test -2 Solutions.pdf (OCR), p37", "sec": "Section A — Data Link Layer: Flow & Error Control", "diff": "hard", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["GATE CS", "UGC-NET 087", "RPSC Programmer", "RPSC ACP/DD"]}, {"q": ["To detect or correct errors, we send extra bits with the data. These extra bits are called:", "Errors detect या correct करने के लिए data के साथ भेजे गए अतिरिक्त bits कहलाते हैं:"], "opts": [["redundancy", "redundancy"], ["correction", "correction"], ["detection", "detection"], ["parity", "parity"]], "ans": 0, "exp": ["The extra bits are called redundancy — overhead added on top of the data that helps catch errors. | Nukta: Redundancy = 'extra bits sent on purpose' — this is what makes error control possible.", "अतिरिक्त bits redundancy कहलाते हैं — यानी data के ऊपर डाला गया भार जो errors पकड़ने में मदद करता है. | Redundancy = 'जान-बूझकर भेजा अतिरिक्त' — इसी से error control संभव है."], "src": "Unit Test -2 Solutions.pdf (OCR), p36", "sec": "Section A — Data Link Layer: Flow & Error Control", "diff": "medium", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["Which of the following verifies the integrity of a message?", "निम्न में से कौन-सा message की integrity जाँचता है?"], "opts": [["Message Encryption", "Message Encryption"], ["Message Checksum", "Message Checksum"], ["Message Digest", "Message Digest"], ["None of these", "None of these"]], "ans": 2, "exp": ["Message digest (जैसे MD5/SHA) message की fingerprint बनाकर integrity verify करता है — बदलाव होते ही digest बदल जाता है. (Checksum भी integrity के लिए है, पर 'message integrity' का standard जवाब Message Digest है.) | Nukta: Digest = अंगूठा-छाप; Encryption = गोपनीयता, integrity नहीं.", "Message digest (जैसे MD5/SHA) message की fingerprint बनाकर integrity verify करता है — बदलाव होते ही digest बदल जाता है. (Checksum भी integrity के लिए है, पर 'message integrity' का standard जवाब Message Digest है.) | Digest = अंगूठा-छाप; Encryption = गोपनीयता, integrity नहीं."], "src": "BCI Subject Test-9.pdf", "sec": "Section A — Data Link Layer: Flow & Error Control", "diff": "easy", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["SSC Computer Awareness", "RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "JNV TAT"]}, {"q": ["Which error detection method uses one extra bit added to the end of a byte?", "कौन-सी error detection method में byte के अंत में एक अतिरिक्त bit जोड़ी जाती है?"], "opts": [["CRC", "CRC"], ["Checksum", "Checksum"], ["Hamming code", "Hamming code"], ["Parity bit", "Parity bit"]], "ans": 3, "exp": ["A parity bit adds one extra bit with every byte so that the count of 1s stays even/odd. | Nukta: Parity = 1 bit; CRC = पूरा remainder; Checksum = योग; Hamming = कई parity bits.", "Parity bit हर byte के साथ एक extra bit जोड़ता है ताकि 1s की गिनती even/odd बनी रहे. | Parity = 1 bit; CRC = पूरा remainder; Checksum = योग; Hamming = कई parity bits."], "src": "CN Topic Test-04.pdf", "sec": "Section A — Data Link Layer: Flow & Error Control", "diff": "medium", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["Which error detection method consists of a parity bit for each data unit as well as an entire data unit of parity bits?", "किस error detection method में हर data unit के लिए एक parity bit के साथ-साथ parity bits का पूरा data unit भी होता है?"], "opts": [["Simple parity check", "Simple parity check"], ["CRC", "CRC"], ["Two-dimensional parity check", "Two-dimensional parity check"], ["Checksum", "Checksum"]], "ans": 2, "exp": ["Two-dimensional parity check में हर row और column की parity बनती है — इसलिए parity bits का पूरा अतिरिक्त unit जुड़ता है. यह कुछ errors correct भी कर सकता है. | Nukta: 2D parity = rows + columns दोनों की parity; simple parity = बस एक bit.", "Two-dimensional parity check में हर row और column की parity बनती है — इसलिए parity bits का पूरा अतिरिक्त unit जुड़ता है. यह कुछ errors correct भी कर सकता है. | 2D parity = rows + columns दोनों की parity; simple parity = बस एक bit."], "src": "Unit Test -2 Solutions.pdf (OCR), p7", "sec": "Section A — Data Link Layer: Flow & Error Control", "diff": "medium", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["A simple parity-check code can detect:", "एक simple parity-check code detect कर सकता है:"], "opts": [["odd number of errors", "odd number of errors"], ["even number of errors", "even number of errors"], ["positive number of errors", "positive number of errors"], ["negative number of errors", "negative number of errors"]], "ans": 0, "exp": ["In simple parity, when an odd number of bits flip, the parity changes and the error is caught; an even number of errors stays hidden. | Nukta: Parity catches odd errors and misses even ones — that is its limit.", "Simple parity में odd संख्या में bit errors पलटने पर parity बदल जाती है और error पकड़ में आता है; even errors छिप जाते हैं. | Parity = odd errors पकड़ता है; even छोड़ देता है — यही इसकी सीमा है."], "src": "Unit Test -2 Solutions.pdf (OCR), p34", "sec": "Section A — Data Link Layer: Flow & Error Control", "diff": "medium", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["Which of the following is an error detection technique?", "निम्न में से कौन-सी error detection technique है?"], "opts": [["ARQ", "ARQ"], ["Parity Bit", "Parity Bit"], ["Stop-and-Wait", "Stop-and-Wait"], ["Sliding Window", "Sliding Window"]], "ans": 1, "exp": ["Parity Bit एक error detection technique है. ARQ, Stop-and-Wait और Sliding Window flow/error control के protocols हैं, detection techniques नहीं. | Nukta: Detection techniques: Parity, CRC, Checksum. Control protocols: SW, GBN, SR.", "Parity Bit एक error detection technique है. ARQ, Stop-and-Wait और Sliding Window flow/error control के protocols हैं, detection techniques नहीं. | Detection techniques: Parity, CRC, Checksum. Control protocols: SW, GBN, SR."], "src": "CN Topic Test-04.pdf", "sec": "Section A — Data Link Layer: Flow & Error Control", "diff": "medium", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["The message 1001 is to be transmitted using the CRC polynomial x³ + x + 1 to protect it from errors. The codeword that should be transmitted is:", "संदेश 1001 को CRC बहुपद x³ + x + 1 से errors से बचाने के लिए भेजना है. भेजा जाने वाला codeword होगा:"], "opts": [["1001100", "1001100"], ["1001011", "1001011"], ["1001110", "1001110"], ["1001000", "1001000"]], "ans": 2, "exp": ["Divisor x³+x+1 = 1011. Message के आगे 3 zeros लगाकर 1001000 को 1011 से भाग दो → remainder 110. यही remainder जोड़ने पर codeword = 1001110. | Nukta: CRC: degree n के polynomial पर n zeros append → भाग का remainder जोड़ो. यहाँ degree 3 → 3 zeros.", "Divisor x³+x+1 = 1011. Message के आगे 3 zeros लगाकर 1001000 को 1011 से भाग दो → remainder 110. यही remainder जोड़ने पर codeword = 1001110. | CRC: degree n के polynomial पर n zeros append → भाग का remainder जोड़ो. यहाँ degree 3 → 3 zeros."], "src": "RPSC Programmer 2024 Paper-1 (with official key)", "sec": "Section A — Data Link Layer: Flow & Error Control", "diff": "hard", "stype": "verified_official_pyq", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["The checksum is used in the Internet by several protocols although not at the ______ layer.", "Internet में checksum कई protocols उपयोग करते हैं, हालाँकि ______ layer पर नहीं."], "opts": [["data link", "data link"], ["transport", "transport"], ["network", "network"], ["none of the above", "none of the above"]], "ans": 0, "exp": ["Data link layer पर CRC (FCS) उपयोग होता है, checksum नहीं. Checksum IP, TCP और UDP headers में होता है. | Nukta: DLL = CRC; Network/Transport = checksum. यही फ़र्क पूछा जाता है.", "Data link layer पर CRC (FCS) उपयोग होता है, checksum नहीं. Checksum IP, TCP और UDP headers में होता है. | DLL = CRC; Network/Transport = checksum. यही फ़र्क पूछा जाता है."], "src": "Unit Test -2 Solutions.pdf (OCR), p33", "sec": "Section A — Data Link Layer: Flow & Error Control", "diff": "hard", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["GATE CS", "UGC-NET 087", "RPSC Programmer", "RPSC ACP/DD"]}, {"q": ["High-level Data Link Control (HDLC) is a protocol for communication over point-to-point and multipoint links. HDLC is a ______ protocol.", "High-level Data Link Control (HDLC) point-to-point और multipoint links पर communication का protocol है. HDLC एक ______ protocol है."], "opts": [["byte-oriented", "byte-oriented"], ["character-oriented", "character-oriented"], ["bit-oriented", "bit-oriented"], ["none of the above", "none of the above"]], "ans": 2, "exp": ["HDLC bit-oriented protocol है — इसमें flag 01111110 होती है और data में bit stuffing होती है. | Nukta: HDLC/SDLC = bit-oriented; PPP = byte-oriented. यह जोड़ी याद रखो.", "HDLC bit-oriented protocol है — इसमें flag 01111110 होती है और data में bit stuffing होती है. | HDLC/SDLC = bit-oriented; PPP = byte-oriented. यह जोड़ी याद रखो."], "src": "Unit Test -2 Solutions.pdf (OCR), p15", "sec": "Section A — Data Link Layer: Flow & Error Control", "diff": "medium", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["The most common protocol for point-to-point access is the Point-to-Point Protocol (PPP), which is a ______ protocol.", "Point-to-point access का सबसे सामान्य protocol Point-to-Point Protocol (PPP) है, जो एक ______ protocol है."], "opts": [["bit-oriented", "bit-oriented"], ["byte-oriented", "byte-oriented"], ["character-oriented", "character-oriented"], ["none of the above", "none of the above"]], "ans": 1, "exp": ["PPP byte-oriented protocol है — frames byte की सीमा पर बनते हैं (HDLC के उलट). | Nukta: PPP = byte-oriented (flag = 0x7E); HDLC = bit-oriented. परीक्षा में यह जोड़ी कई बार आ चुकी है.", "PPP byte-oriented protocol है — frames byte की सीमा पर बनते हैं (HDLC के उलट). | PPP = byte-oriented (flag = 0x7E); HDLC = bit-oriented. परीक्षा में यह जोड़ी कई बार आ चुकी है."], "src": "Unit Test -2 Solutions.pdf (OCR), p16", "sec": "Section A — Data Link Layer: Flow & Error Control", "diff": "medium", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["Which of the following is NOT a responsibility of the network layer?", "निम्न में से कौन-सा network layer की ज़िम्मेदारी नहीं है?"], "opts": [["Congestion control", "Congestion control"], ["Error control", "Error control"], ["Routing", "Routing"], ["Inter-networking", "Inter-networking"]], "ans": 1, "exp": ["Error control Data Link और Transport layers संभालते हैं. Network layer routing, forwarding, congestion control और inter-networking करता है. | Nukta: Network layer = रास्ता + congestion; error control यहाँ नहीं.", "Error control Data Link और Transport layers संभालते हैं. Network layer routing, forwarding, congestion control और inter-networking करता है. | Network layer = रास्ता + congestion; error control यहाँ नहीं."], "src": "CN Topic Test-02.pdf", "sec": "Section A — Data Link Layer: Flow & Error Control", "diff": "hard", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["GATE CS", "UGC-NET 087", "RPSC Programmer", "RPSC ACP/DD"]}, {"q": ["The types of data services offered by an LLC (Logical Link Control) layer are:", "LLC (Logical Link Control) layer द्वारा दी जाने वाली data services के प्रकार हैं:"], "opts": [["Connectionless (fast and unreliable)", "Connectionless (fast and unreliable)"], ["Connection-oriented (slow and reliable)", "Connection-oriented (slow and reliable)"], ["Both A and B", "Both A and B"], ["None of the above", "None of the above"]], "ans": 2, "exp": ["LLC दोनों तरह की services देता है — connectionless (तेज़, unreliable) और connection-oriented (भरोसेमंद). | Nukta: LLC types: 1 (connectionless), 2 (connection-oriented), 3 (acknowledged connectionless).", "LLC दोनों तरह की services देता है — connectionless (तेज़, unreliable) और connection-oriented (भरोसेमंद). | LLC types: 1 (connectionless), 2 (connection-oriented), 3 (acknowledged connectionless)."], "src": "Unit Test -2 Solutions.pdf (OCR), p32", "sec": "Section A — Data Link Layer: Flow & Error Control", "diff": "hard", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["GATE CS", "UGC-NET 087", "RPSC Programmer", "RPSC ACP/DD"]}, {"q": ["Which protocol allows the sender to transmit multiple frames before needing an acknowledgment?", "कौन-सा protocol sender को acknowledgment की ज़रूरत से पहले कई frames भेजने देता है?"], "opts": [["Stop-and-Wait", "Stop-and-Wait"], ["Go-Back-N", "Go-Back-N"], ["ALOHA", "ALOHA"], ["CSMA/CD", "CSMA/CD"]], "ans": 1, "exp": ["Go-Back-N (और Selective Repeat) sliding window protocols हैं जो कई frames एक साथ भेजते हैं. | Nukta: Sliding window = कई outstanding frames; Stop-and-Wait = एक.", "Go-Back-N (और Selective Repeat) sliding window protocols हैं जो कई frames एक साथ भेजते हैं. | Sliding window = कई outstanding frames; Stop-and-Wait = एक."], "src": "CN Topic Test-04.pdf", "sec": "Section A — Data Link Layer: Flow & Error Control", "diff": "medium", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["The message 11001001 is to be transmitted using the CRC polynomial x³ + 1 to protect it from errors. The codeword that should be transmitted is:", "संदेश 11001001 को CRC बहुपद x³ + 1 से errors से बचाने के लिए भेजना है. भेजा जाने वाला codeword होगा:"], "opts": [["11001001000", "11001001000"], ["11001001011", "11001001011"], ["11001010", "11001010"], ["110010010011", "110010010011"]], "ans": 1, "exp": ["x³ + 1 = 1001. Message के आगे 3 zeros लगाकर 11001001000 को 1001 से भाग दो → remainder 011. जोड़ने पर codeword = 11001001011. | Nukta: GATE official key (B). यही तरीका RPSC के x³+x+1 वाले प्रश्न में भी — degree n पर n zeros, भाग का remainder जोड़ो.", "x³ + 1 = 1001. Message के आगे 3 zeros लगाकर 11001001000 को 1001 से भाग दो → remainder 011. जोड़ने पर codeword = 11001001011. | GATE official key (B). यही तरीका RPSC के x³+x+1 वाले प्रश्न में भी — degree n पर n zeros, भाग का remainder जोड़ो."], "src": "GATE CS 2007", "sec": "Section A — Data Link Layer: Flow & Error Control", "diff": "hard", "stype": "claimed_pyq_unverified", "style": "concept", "tags": ["GATE CS"]}, {"q": ["Let G(x) be the generator polynomial used for CRC checking. What condition must G(x) satisfy to detect an odd number of bits in error?", "मान लीजिए G(x), CRC जाँच में उपयोग होने वाला generator polynomial है. Odd संख्या में बिट-त्रुटियाँ पकड़ने के लिए G(x) पर क्या शर्त होनी चाहिए?"], "opts": [["G(x) contains more than two terms", "G(x) contains more than two terms"], ["G(x) does not divide 1 + x^k for any k within the frame length", "G(x) does not divide 1 + x^k for any k within the frame length"], ["1 + x is a factor of G(x)", "1 + x is a factor of G(x)"], ["G(x) has an odd number of terms", "G(x) has an odd number of terms"]], "ans": 2, "exp": ["If (1 + x), i.e. x + 1, is a factor of G(x), then every codeword has an even number of 1s — so odd errors are caught. | Nukta: GATE official key (C). x+1 factor ↔ even parity code ↔ odd errors detect.", "यदि (1 + x) यानी x + 1, G(x) का factor हो, तो code की सभी codewords में 1s की संख्या even होती है — इसलिए odd त्रुटियाँ पकड़ में आ जाती हैं. | GATE official key (C). x+1 factor ↔ even parity code ↔ odd errors detect."], "src": "GATE CS 2009", "sec": "Section A — Data Link Layer: Flow & Error Control", "diff": "hard", "stype": "claimed_pyq_unverified", "style": "concept", "tags": ["GATE CS"]}, {"q": ["In CRC coding, if the data word is 111111, the divisor is 1010 and the remainder is 110, which of the following is the transmitted code?", "CRC coding में, यदि data word 111111 है, divisor 1010 है और remainder 110 है, तो निम्न में से कौन-सा भेजा गया code है?"], "opts": [["011111101", "011111101"], ["001010110", "001010110"], ["111111110", "111111110"], ["110111111", "110111111"]], "ans": 2, "exp": ["Transmitted code = data word + remainder = 111111 + 110 = 111111110. | Nukta: CRC में codeword = data के पीछे remainder. बाकी options remainder जोड़ने का हिसाब नहीं रखते.", "Transmitted code = data word + remainder = 111111 + 110 = 111111110. | CRC में codeword = data के पीछे remainder. बाकी options remainder जोड़ने का हिसाब नहीं रखते."], "src": "UGC NET Computer Science Dec 2022 (via samagracs)", "sec": "Section A — Data Link Layer: Flow & Error Control", "diff": "hard", "stype": "claimed_pyq_unverified", "style": "concept", "tags": ["UGC-NET 087"]}, {"q": ["A 2 km long broadcast LAN has 10⁷ bps bandwidth and uses CSMA/CD. The signal travels along the wire at 2 × 10⁸ m/s. What is the minimum packet size that can be used on this network?", "एक 2 km लंबे broadcast LAN की bandwidth 10⁷ bps है और यह CSMA/CD उपयोग करता है. Signal तार में 2 × 10⁸ m/s से चलता है. इस network पर उपयोग होने वाला न्यूनतम packet आकार कितना है?"], "opts": [["50 bytes", "50 bytes"], ["100 bytes", "100 bytes"], ["200 bytes", "200 bytes"], ["None of the above", "None of the above"]], "ans": 3, "exp": ["न्यूनतम frame = 2 × d × R / v = 2 × 2000 × 10⁷ / (2 × 10⁸) = 200 bits = 25 bytes. यह किसी दिए option में नहीं — इसलिए 'None of the above'. | Nukta: GATE 2003 और RPSC 2011 दोनों का official key (D). याद रखो: min frame = 2 × propagation delay × bandwidth (round-trip).", "न्यूनतम frame = 2 × d × R / v = 2 × 2000 × 10⁷ / (2 × 10⁸) = 200 bits = 25 bytes. यह किसी दिए option में नहीं — इसलिए 'None of the above'. | GATE 2003 और RPSC 2011 दोनों का official key (D). याद रखो: min frame = 2 × propagation delay × bandwidth (round-trip)."], "src": "GATE CS 2003 + RPSC Programmer 2011 Paper-1 (via pyqp.in)", "sec": "Section A — Data Link Layer: Flow & Error Control", "diff": "hard", "stype": "claimed_pyq_unverified", "style": "numerical", "tags": ["GATE CS"]}, {"q": ["A network using CSMA/CD has a bandwidth of 20 Mbps. If the maximum propagation time is 25 µs, what is the minimum size of the frame?", "CSMA/CD उपयोग करने वाले network की bandwidth 20 Mbps है. यदि अधिकतम propagation time 25 µs हो, तो frame का न्यूनतम आकार क्या होगा?"], "opts": [["500 bits", "500 bits"], ["1000 bits", "1000 bits"], ["1500 bits", "1500 bits"], ["2000 bits", "2000 bits"]], "ans": 1, "exp": ["Minimum frame = 2 × Tp × BW = 2 × 25µs × 20 Mbps = 2 × 25×10⁻⁶ × 20×10⁶ = 1000 bits. | Nukta: UGC NET Jan 2025 key (ii). यही formula ऊपर वाले GATE प्रश्न में भी — बस units बदलो.", "Minimum frame = 2 × Tp × BW = 2 × 25µs × 20 Mbps = 2 × 25×10⁻⁶ × 20×10⁶ = 1000 bits. | UGC NET Jan 2025 key (ii). यही formula ऊपर वाले GATE प्रश्न में भी — बस units बदलो."], "src": "UGC NET Computer Science Jan 2025 (via samagracs solved paper)", "sec": "Section A — Data Link Layer: Flow & Error Control", "diff": "hard", "stype": "claimed_pyq_unverified", "style": "numerical", "tags": ["UGC-NET 087"]}, {"q": ["A CSMA/CD network transmits data at 100 Mbps over a 1 km cable with no repeaters. If the minimum frame size required is 1250 bytes, what is the signal speed in the cable (in km/sec)?", "एक CSMA/CD network बिना repeaters के 1 km cable पर 100 Mbps से data भेजता है. यदि आवश्यक न्यूनतम frame आकार 1250 bytes हो, तो cable में signal की गति (km/sec में) कितनी है?"], "opts": [["8000", "8000"], ["10000", "10000"], ["16000", "16000"], ["20000", "20000"]], "ans": 3, "exp": ["Min frame = 2dR/v → v = 2dR/L = 2 × 1 km × 10⁸ bps / (1250×8 bits) = 2×10⁸/10⁴ = 20000 km/sec. | Nukta: GATE 2015 key (d) 20000 km/s. Getting the speed by inverting the formula — that is the trick of this question.", "Min frame = 2dR/v → v = 2dR/L = 2 × 1 km × 10⁸ bps / (1250×8 bits) = 2×10⁸/10⁴ = 20000 km/sec. | GATE 2015 key (d) 20000 km/s. Formula को उलटकर speed निकालना — यही इस प्रश्न का खेल है."], "src": "GATE CSE 2015 Set 3", "sec": "Section A — Data Link Layer: Flow & Error Control", "diff": "hard", "stype": "claimed_pyq_unverified", "style": "numerical", "tags": ["GATE CS"]}, {"q": ["In the starting phase (slow start) of the TCP congestion control algorithm, the congestion window size:", "TCP congestion control algorithm के शुरुआती चरण (slow start) में congestion window का आकार:"], "opts": [["Increases linearly", "Increases linearly"], ["Does not increase", "Does not increase"], ["Increases exponentially", "Increases exponentially"], ["Remains constant at threshold", "Remains constant at threshold"]], "ans": 2, "exp": ["Slow start में हर RTT पर window दोगुनी होती है — यानी exponential वृद्धि. Threshold के बाद linear वृद्धि (congestion avoidance) शुरू होती है. | Nukta: GATE 2008 key: exponential. क्रम याद रखो: Slow start (exponential) → Congestion avoidance (linear).", "Slow start में हर RTT पर window दोगुनी होती है — यानी exponential वृद्धि. Threshold के बाद linear वृद्धि (congestion avoidance) शुरू होती है. | GATE 2008 key: exponential. क्रम याद रखो: Slow start (exponential) → Congestion avoidance (linear)."], "src": "GATE CS 2008", "sec": "Section A — Data Link Layer: Flow & Error Control", "diff": "hard", "stype": "claimed_pyq_unverified", "style": "concept", "tags": ["GATE CS"]}, {"q": ["Consider the following statements: I. TCP connections are full duplex. II. TCP has no option for selective acknowledgment. III. TCP connections are message streams. Which of the following is correct?", "निम्न कथनों पर विचार करें: I. TCP connections full duplex होती हैं. II. TCP में selective acknowledgment का कोई विकल्प नहीं है. III. TCP connections message streams हैं. निम्न में से क्या सही है?"], "opts": [["Only I is correct", "Only I is correct"], ["Only I and II are correct", "Only I and II are correct"], ["Only II and III are correct", "Only II and III are correct"], ["All of I, II and III are correct", "All of I, II and III are correct"]], "ans": 0, "exp": ["I सही — TCP full duplex है. II गलत — TCP में SACK (Selective ACK) विकल्प होता है. III गलत — TCP byte streams है, message streams नहीं. | Nukta: GATE 2012 official key (a). याद रखो: TCP = full-duplex byte-stream + SACK उपलब्ध; UDP = message-oriented.", "I सही — TCP full duplex है. II गलत — TCP में SACK (Selective ACK) विकल्प होता है. III गलत — TCP byte streams है, message streams नहीं. | GATE 2012 official key (a). याद रखो: TCP = full-duplex byte-stream + SACK उपलब्ध; UDP = message-oriented."], "src": "GATE CS 2012", "sec": "Section A — Data Link Layer: Flow & Error Control", "diff": "hard", "stype": "claimed_pyq_unverified", "style": "statement", "tags": ["GATE CS"]}, {"q": ["The minimum Hamming distance required to detect 2 bit errors is:", "2 bit errors detect करने के लिए न्यूनतम Hamming distance चाहिए:"], "opts": [["2", "2"], ["3", "3"], ["4", "4"], ["5", "5"]], "ans": 1, "exp": ["Detect e errors: d ≥ e+1 → 2+1 = 3. | Nukta: Correct 2 errors ke liye d ≥ 2e+1 = 5.", "Detect: d ≥ e+1 → 3। | Correct करने के लिए d ≥ 5।"], "src": "Practice — original (textbook-based)", "sec": "Section A — Data Link Layer: Flow & Error Control", "diff": "hard", "stype": "original_practice", "style": "numerical", "tags": ["GATE CS", "UGC-NET 087", "RPSC Programmer", "RPSC ACP/DD", "Practice Set"]}, {"q": ["In CRC, if the received codeword is divided by the generator and the remainder is zero, the receiver concludes:", "CRC में यदि remainder शून्य हो, तो receiver निष्कर्ष निकालता है:"], "opts": [["Error is present", "त्रुटि है"], ["No error detected", "कोई त्रुटि नहीं मिली"], ["Frame is lost", "Frame खो गया"], ["ACK is corrupt", "ACK ख़राब है"]], "ans": 1, "exp": ["Remainder 0 = error nahi mila (probability of undetected error kam). | Nukta: Non-zero remainder = error.", "Remainder 0 = त्रुटि नहीं मिली। | ग़ैर-शून्य remainder = त्रुटि।"], "src": "Practice — original (textbook-based)", "sec": "Section A — Data Link Layer: Flow & Error Control", "diff": "medium", "stype": "original_practice", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer", "Practice Set"]}, {"q": ["In Selective Repeat ARQ, when a frame is corrupted, the sender retransmits:", "Selective Repeat ARQ में frame ख़राब होने पर दोबारा भेजता है:"], "opts": [["All outstanding frames", "सभी लंबित frames"], ["Only the corrupted frame", "केवल ख़राब frame"], ["No frame", "कोई नहीं"], ["The last frame only", "केवल अंतिम frame"]], "ans": 1, "exp": ["Selective Repeat = sirf galat frame; Go-Back-N = uske aage ke sab. | Nukta: Go-Back-N sab dobara bhejta hai.", "Selective Repeat = सिर्फ़ ख़राब; Go-Back-N = आगे के सब। | Go-Back-N सब दोबारा।"], "src": "Practice — original (textbook-based)", "sec": "Section A — Data Link Layer: Flow & Error Control", "diff": "medium", "stype": "original_practice", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer", "Practice Set"]}, {"q": ["Parity check can detect which type of errors?", "Parity check कौन-सी errors detect कर सकता है?"], "opts": [["Any number of errors", "कितनी भी errors"], ["Odd number of bit errors", "विषम संख्या में bit errors"], ["Only burst errors", "केवल burst errors"], ["No errors", "कोई नहीं"]], "ans": 1, "exp": ["Single parity bit odd-bit errors detect karta hai; even ko miss. | Nukta: CRC burst errors ke liye behtar.", "Parity bit विषम-bit errors detect करती है। | CRC burst के लिए बेहतर।"], "src": "Practice — original (textbook-based)", "sec": "Section A — Data Link Layer: Flow & Error Control", "diff": "medium", "stype": "original_practice", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer", "Practice Set"]}, {"q": ["Forward Error Correction (FEC) differs from ARQ in that:", "Forward Error Correction (FEC), ARQ से भिन्न है क्योंकि:"], "opts": [["It needs retransmission", "इसे retransmission चाहिए"], ["The receiver corrects errors without retransmission", "Receiver बिना retransmission errors ठीक करता है"], ["It cannot detect errors", "यह errors detect नहीं करता"], ["It works only on LAN", "यह सिर्फ़ LAN पर चलता है"]], "ans": 1, "exp": ["FEC receiver par hi error correction karta hai — retransmission nahi. | Nukta: ARQ mein retransmission hota hai.", "FEC receiver पर ही ठीक करता है। | ARQ में retransmission।"], "src": "Practice — original (textbook-based)", "sec": "Section A — Data Link Layer: Flow & Error Control", "diff": "medium", "stype": "original_practice", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer", "Practice Set"]}, {"q": ["In Go-Back-N ARQ, the receiver's window size is:", "Go-Back-N ARQ में receiver की window size होती है:"], "opts": [["1", "1"], ["Same as the sender's window", "Sender की window के बराबर"], ["2^(n−1)", "2^(n−1)"], ["Unbounded", "असीमित"]], "ans": 0, "exp": ["GBN receiver sirf agla expected frame accept karta hai (window=1); isliye out-of-order frame aaye to use phenk kar pura Go-Back-N retransmission hota hai. | Nukta: Selective Repeat mein receiver ki window badi hoti hai — wahi out-of-order frames buffer karta hai.", "GBN में receiver सिर्फ अगला expected frame लेता है (window=1); out-of-order आने पर पूरा Go-Back-N। | Selective Repeat में receiver window बड़ी — out-of-order buffer होते हैं।"], "src": "Practice — original (textbook-based)", "sec": "Section A — Data Link Layer: Flow & Error Control", "diff": "medium", "stype": "original_practice", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer", "Practice Set"]}, {"q": ["Delaying an acknowledgement so that it can be attached to the next outgoing data frame in the reverse direction is called:", "Acknowledgement को रोककर विपरीत दिशा में जाने वाले अगले data frame के साथ जोड़ना कहलाता है:"], "opts": [["Piggybacking", "Piggybacking"], ["Broadcasting", "Broadcasting"], ["Framing", "Framing"], ["Stuffing", "Stuffing"]], "ans": 0, "exp": ["Piggybacking: bidirectional link par ack ko data frame ke saath chipka do — alag ack frame bachta hai, bandwidth bachti hai. | Nukta: Piggybacking mein ack ke liye timer hota hai, taaki der zyada na ho.", "Piggybacking: bidirectional link पर ack को data frame के साथ जोड़ना — bandwidth बचती है। | Piggybacking में ack timer होता है, ताकि देर न हो।"], "src": "Practice — original (textbook-based)", "sec": "Section A — Data Link Layer: Flow & Error Control", "diff": "medium", "stype": "original_practice", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer", "Practice Set"]}, {"q": ["Network congestion occurs when:", "Network congestion तब होता है जब:"], "opts": [["The offered traffic exceeds the network's capacity", "Offered traffic network की क्षमता से अधिक हो"], ["Two hosts use the same port", "दो hosts एक ही port प्रयोग करें"], ["A frame is corrupted by noise", "Noise से frame खराब हो"], ["The DNS server is down", "DNS server बंद हो"]], "ans": 0, "exp": ["Congestion = queues bhar jaate hain kyunki demand capacity se zyada hai — delay/loss badhte hain. Isi ko sambhalne ke liye congestion control hota hai. | Nukta: Flow control = receiver ki speed; congestion = network ki capacity.", "Congestion = demand क्षमता से अधिक; queues भरती हैं, delay/loss बढ़ता है। | Flow control = receiver; congestion = network की क्षमता।"], "src": "Practice — original (textbook-based)", "sec": "Section A — Data Link Layer: Flow & Error Control", "diff": "medium", "stype": "original_practice", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer", "Practice Set"]}, {"q": ["Why is bit stuffing required in bit-oriented protocols?", "Bit-oriented protocols में bit stuffing क्यों ज़रूरी है?"], "opts": [["To increase bandwidth", "To increase bandwidth"], ["To prevent confusion between data and the flag", "To prevent confusion between data and the flag"], ["To reduce collisions", "To reduce collisions"], ["To detect errors", "To detect errors"]], "ans": 1, "exp": ["The flag pattern (e.g. HDLC's 01111110) can also appear inside data — to prevent confusion, a 0 is stuffed after every five 1s in the data (bit stuffing). | Nukta: Bit stuffing = data को flag से अलग पहचान दिलाना.", "Flag pattern (जैसे HDLC की 01111110) data में भी आ सकती है — confusion रोकने के लिए data में हर पाँच 1s के बाद एक 0 ठूँस दिया जाता है (bit stuffing). | Bit stuffing = data को flag से अलग पहचान दिलाना."], "src": "BCI Subject Test-9.pdf", "sec": "Section B — Data Link Layer: Framing & MAC Sub-layer", "diff": "easy", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["SSC Computer Awareness", "RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "JNV TAT"]}, {"q": ["Bit stuffing refers to:", "Bit stuffing का अर्थ है:"], "opts": [["Inserting a '0' in the user stream to differentiate it from the flag", "Inserting a '0' in the user stream to differentiate it from the flag"], ["Inserting a '0' in the flag stream to avoid ambiguity", "Inserting a '0' in the flag stream to avoid ambiguity"], ["Appending a nibble to the flag sequence", "Appending a nibble to the flag sequence"], ["Appending a nibble to the user data stream", "Appending a nibble to the user data stream"]], "ans": 0, "exp": ["In the user (data) stream, after five consecutive 1s a 0 is inserted so that the data can be told apart from the flag. | Nukta: Stuffing is always done in DATA, never in the flag; in byte stuffing 0x7D follows 0x7E.", "User (data) stream में पाँच लगातार 1s के बाद एक 0 जोड़ा जाता है ताकि data, flag से अलग पहचाना जा सके. | Stuffing हमेशा DATA में होती है, flag में नहीं; byte stuffing में 0x7E के बाद 0x7D जुड़ता है."], "src": "Unit Test-4 Solution.pdf (OCR), p26", "sec": "Section B — Data Link Layer: Framing & MAC Sub-layer", "diff": "medium", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["In Ethernet CSMA/CD, the special sequence transmitted by media access management to handle a collision is called:", "Ethernet CSMA/CD में collision संभालने के लिए media access management द्वारा भेजा गया विशेष sequence कहलाता है:"], "opts": [["Preamble", "Preamble"], ["Postamble", "Postamble"], ["Jam signal", "Jam signal"], ["None of these", "None of these"]], "ans": 2, "exp": ["As soon as a collision is detected, all stations send a Jam signal so that the others know at once and the line clears. | Nukta: Jam = the siren shouting 'a collision happened!'. Preamble = announcement that a frame is starting.", "Collision detect होते ही सभी stations एक Jam signal भेजते हैं ताकि बाकी stations तुरंत जान जाएँ और line खाली हो. | Jam = 'टकराव हो गया!' का सायरन. Preamble = frame शुरू होने की घोषणा."], "src": "Unit Test-4 Solution.pdf (OCR), p28", "sec": "Section B — Data Link Layer: Framing & MAC Sub-layer", "diff": "medium", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["The correct order of fields in an Ethernet frame is:", "Ethernet frame में fields का सही क्रम है:"], "opts": [["Preamble → Destination MAC → Source MAC → Type/Length → Data → FCS", "Preamble → Destination MAC → Source MAC → Type/Length → Data → FCS"], ["Destination MAC → Source MAC → FCS → Data → Preamble", "Destination MAC → Source MAC → FCS → Data → Preamble"], ["Source MAC → Destination MAC → Data → CRC → Type", "Source MAC → Destination MAC → Data → CRC → Type"], ["Preamble → Source MAC → Destination MAC → Data", "Preamble → Source MAC → Destination MAC → Data"]], "ans": 0, "exp": ["Ethernet frame: Preamble+SFD, फिर Destination MAC, Source MAC, Type/Length, Data (46–1500 bytes), और अंत में FCS (CRC). | Nukta: Remember: after the Preamble come the RECEIVER's address (Destination) first, then the sender's — the rest later.", "Ethernet frame: Preamble+SFD, फिर Destination MAC, Source MAC, Type/Length, Data (46–1500 bytes), और अंत में FCS (CRC). | याद रखो: Preamble के बाद पहले RECEIVER का पता (Destination), फिर भेजने वाले का — बाकी बाद में."], "src": "BCI Subject Test-9.pdf", "sec": "Section B — Data Link Layer: Framing & MAC Sub-layer", "diff": "easy", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["SSC Computer Awareness", "RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "JNV TAT"]}, {"q": ["The minimum size of an Ethernet frame (excluding preamble) is:", "Ethernet frame का न्यूनतम आकार (preamble को छोड़कर) होता है:"], "opts": [["46 bytes", "46 bytes"], ["64 bytes", "64 bytes"], ["72 bytes", "72 bytes"], ["1518 bytes", "1518 bytes"]], "ans": 1, "exp": ["Ethernet frame का न्यूनतम आकार 64 bytes होता है (14 header + 46 data + 4 FCS). | Nukta: 64 = minimum frame; 1518 = maximum frame; 46 = सिर्फ data का minimum.", "Ethernet frame का न्यूनतम आकार 64 bytes होता है (14 header + 46 data + 4 FCS). | 64 = minimum frame; 1518 = maximum frame; 46 = सिर्फ data का minimum."], "src": "BCI Subject Test-9.pdf", "sec": "Section B — Data Link Layer: Framing & MAC Sub-layer", "diff": "medium", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["The data field size in an Ethernet frame ranges from:", "Ethernet frame में data field का आकार रहता है:"], "opts": [["64–1518 bytes", "64–1518 bytes"], ["46–1500 bytes", "46–1500 bytes"], ["40–1480 bytes", "40–1480 bytes"], ["32–1500 bytes", "32–1500 bytes"]], "ans": 1, "exp": ["Data field 46 bytes से 1500 bytes तक होता है (1500 = Ethernet MTU). | Nukta: The whole frame ranges 64–1518 bytes; the data 46–1500. This pair is asked often.", "Data field 46 bytes से 1500 bytes तक होता है (1500 = Ethernet MTU). | पूरे frame का range 64–1518; data का 46–1500. यह जोड़ी अक्सर पूछी जाती है."], "src": "BCI Subject Test-9.pdf", "sec": "Section B — Data Link Layer: Framing & MAC Sub-layer", "diff": "medium", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["What is the MTU size for Ethernet?", "Ethernet के लिए MTU आकार कितना है?"], "opts": [["1024 bytes", "1024 bytes"], ["1500 bytes", "1500 bytes"], ["512 bytes", "512 bytes"], ["2048 bytes", "2048 bytes"]], "ans": 1, "exp": ["Ethernet की MTU (Maximum Transmission Unit) 1500 bytes होती है — यानी data field में अधिकतम इतना data. | Nukta: MTU = the data limit; 1518 = the whole frame limit. Don't confuse the two.", "Ethernet की MTU (Maximum Transmission Unit) 1500 bytes होती है — यानी data field में अधिकतम इतना data. | MTU = data की सीमा; 1518 = पूरे frame की सीमा. भ्रम में मत आना."], "src": "CN Topic Test 5.pdf", "sec": "Section B — Data Link Layer: Framing & MAC Sub-layer", "diff": "hard", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["GATE CS", "UGC-NET 087", "RPSC Programmer", "RPSC ACP/DD"]}, {"q": ["In Ethernet, the minimum frame size is fixed mainly to:", "Ethernet में न्यूनतम frame आकार मुख्य रूप से किसलिए तय किया गया है?"], "opts": [["Improve throughput", "Improve throughput"], ["Reduce overhead", "Reduce overhead"], ["Detect collisions using CSMA/CD", "Detect collisions using CSMA/CD"], ["Increase security", "Increase security"]], "ans": 2, "exp": ["In CSMA/CD the sender must detect collisions while transmitting — so the frame must be long enough for the signal to complete a round trip. That is the 64-byte limit. | Nukta: Round-trip time (slot time) तक frame ज़िंदा रहे — तभी collision पकड़ी जाएगी.", "CSMA/CD में sender को transmission के दौरान collision detect करना होता है — इसलिए frame इतना बड़ा होना चाहिए कि signal round-trip पूरा कर सके. 64 bytes की यही सीमा है. | Round-trip time (slot time) तक frame ज़िंदा रहे — तभी collision पकड़ी जाएगी."], "src": "BCI Subject Test-9.pdf", "sec": "Section B — Data Link Layer: Framing & MAC Sub-layer", "diff": "medium", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["Collision detection and avoidance mechanisms are implemented in:", "Collision detection और avoidance mechanisms कहाँ लागू होते हैं?"], "opts": [["LLC Sublayer", "LLC Sublayer"], ["Network Layer", "Network Layer"], ["MAC Sublayer", "MAC Sublayer"], ["Physical Layer", "Physical Layer"]], "ans": 2, "exp": ["MAC (Media Access Control) sub-layer ही medium तक पहुँच का नियम बनाता है — CSMA/CD, CSMA/CA आदि यहीं लागू होते हैं. | Nukta: MAC = Medium Access Control — नाम में ही 'medium access' लिखा है.", "MAC (Media Access Control) sub-layer ही medium तक पहुँच का नियम बनाता है — CSMA/CD, CSMA/CA आदि यहीं लागू होते हैं. | MAC = Medium Access Control — नाम में ही 'medium access' लिखा है."], "src": "BCI Subject Test-9.pdf", "sec": "Section B — Data Link Layer: Framing & MAC Sub-layer", "diff": "easy", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["SSC Computer Awareness", "RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "JNV TAT"]}, {"q": ["What is the primary function of the MAC sublayer?", "MAC sublayer का मुख्य काम क्या है?"], "opts": [["Routing", "Routing"], ["Error checking", "Error checking"], ["Addressing", "Addressing"], ["Channel access", "Channel access"]], "ans": 3, "exp": ["The MAC sub-layer's main job is controlling access to the channel (medium) — who transmits when. | Nukta: MAC = addressing + channel access; पर परीक्षा में 'primary function' = channel access.", "MAC sub-layer का मुख्य काम channel (medium) तक पहुँच नियंत्रित करना है — कब कौन भेजेगा. | MAC = addressing + channel access; पर परीक्षा में 'primary function' = channel access."], "src": "CN Topic Test-04.pdf", "sec": "Section B — Data Link Layer: Framing & MAC Sub-layer", "diff": "medium", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["Which protocol requires time synchronization among nodes?", "किस protocol में nodes के बीच time synchronization चाहिए होती है?"], "opts": [["Pure ALOHA", "Pure ALOHA"], ["Slotted ALOHA", "Slotted ALOHA"], ["CSMA", "CSMA"], ["CSMA/CD", "CSMA/CD"]], "ans": 1, "exp": ["In Slotted ALOHA, time is divided into slots and transmission starts only at a slot boundary — so all nodes must be synchronised. | Nukta: Pure ALOHA = send whenever you like; Slotted = send only when the slot clock says so.", "Slotted ALOHA में time को slots में बाँटा जाता है और transmission सिर्फ slot की शुरुआत में होती है — इसलिए सभी nodes synchronized होने चाहिए. | Pure ALOHA = जब मन चाहे भेजो; Slotted = slot की घड़ी देखकर भेजो."], "src": "BCI Subject Test-9.pdf", "sec": "Section B — Data Link Layer: Framing & MAC Sub-layer", "diff": "easy", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["SSC Computer Awareness", "RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "JNV TAT"]}, {"q": ["The vulnerable period of Pure ALOHA is:", "Pure ALOHA का vulnerable period होता है:"], "opts": [["T", "T"], ["2T", "2T"], ["T/2", "T/2"], ["4T", "4T"]], "ans": 1, "exp": ["Pure ALOHA में कोई भी frame T समय तक टकरा सकता है — vulnerable period 2T होता है (इसीलिए efficiency G·e⁻²ᴳ, अधिकतम ~18.4%). | Nukta: Pure ALOHA: 2T और G·e⁻²ᴳ (~18.4%); Slotted ALOHA: T और G·e⁻ᴳ (~36.8%).", "Pure ALOHA में कोई भी frame T समय तक टकरा सकता है — vulnerable period 2T होता है (इसीलिए efficiency G·e⁻²ᴳ, अधिकतम ~18.4%). | Pure ALOHA: 2T और G·e⁻²ᴳ (~18.4%); Slotted ALOHA: T और G·e⁻ᴳ (~36.8%)."], "src": "BCI Subject Test-9.pdf", "sec": "Section B — Data Link Layer: Framing & MAC Sub-layer", "diff": "easy", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["SSC Computer Awareness", "RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "JNV TAT"]}, {"q": ["In a slotted ALOHA with G stations attempting to transmit in one slot, the throughput is equal to:", "Slotted ALOHA में एक slot में G stations transmit करने का प्रयास करें तो throughput होगा:"], "opts": [["G × e⁻ᴳ", "G × e⁻ᴳ"], ["2G × e⁻ᴳ", "2G × e⁻ᴳ"], ["e⁻ᴳ", "e⁻ᴳ"], ["G × e⁻²ᴳ", "G × e⁻²ᴳ"]], "ans": 0, "exp": ["Slotted ALOHA की throughput = G·e⁻ᴳ है (अधिकतम 1/e ≈ 36.8% जब G = 1). | Nukta: RPSC official key (a). Pure ALOHA का formula G·e⁻²ᴳ है — मिलाकर मत पढ़ना.", "Slotted ALOHA की throughput = G·e⁻ᴳ है (अधिकतम 1/e ≈ 36.8% जब G = 1). | RPSC official key (a). Pure ALOHA का formula G·e⁻²ᴳ है — मिलाकर मत पढ़ना."], "src": "RPSC Programmer 2024 Paper-1 (with official key)", "sec": "Section B — Data Link Layer: Framing & MAC Sub-layer", "diff": "hard", "stype": "verified_official_pyq", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["Which protocol has the highest efficiency under heavy load?", "भारी load पर किस protocol की efficiency सबसे अधिक होती है?"], "opts": [["Pure ALOHA", "Pure ALOHA"], ["Slotted ALOHA", "Slotted ALOHA"], ["CSMA", "CSMA"], ["CSMA/CD", "CSMA/CD"]], "ans": 3, "exp": ["CSMA/CD (Ethernet) carrier sense और collision detection से medium का उपयोग सबसे कुशल करता है — heavy load पर सबसे अच्छा. | Nukta: क्रम: CSMA/CD > CSMA > Slotted ALOHA > Pure ALOHA.", "CSMA/CD (Ethernet) carrier sense और collision detection से medium का उपयोग सबसे कुशल करता है — heavy load पर सबसे अच्छा. | क्रम: CSMA/CD > CSMA > Slotted ALOHA > Pure ALOHA."], "src": "BCI Subject Test-9.pdf", "sec": "Section B — Data Link Layer: Framing & MAC Sub-layer", "diff": "easy", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["SSC Computer Awareness", "RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "JNV TAT"]}, {"q": ["Which protocol detects collisions while transmission is in progress?", "कौन-सा protocol transmission के दौरान ही collisions detect करता है?"], "opts": [["CSMA", "CSMA"], ["Slotted ALOHA", "Slotted ALOHA"], ["CSMA/CD", "CSMA/CD"], ["CSMA/CA", "CSMA/CA"]], "ans": 2, "exp": ["CSMA/CD = Carrier Sense Multiple Access with Collision Detection — transmission चलते समय ही voltage बढ़ने से collision पकड़ लेता है. | Nukta: CD = detect-and-jam; CA = avoid (RTS/CTS) — wireless में.", "CSMA/CD = Carrier Sense Multiple Access with Collision Detection — transmission चलते समय ही voltage बढ़ने से collision पकड़ लेता है. | CD = detect-and-jam; CA = avoid (RTS/CTS) — wireless में."], "src": "BCI Subject Test-9.pdf", "sec": "Section B — Data Link Layer: Framing & MAC Sub-layer", "diff": "easy", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["SSC Computer Awareness", "RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "JNV TAT"]}, {"q": ["What is the primary role of CSMA/CD in Ethernet?", "Ethernet में CSMA/CD की मुख्य भूमिका क्या है?"], "opts": [["Error correction", "Error correction"], ["Collision detection", "Collision detection"], ["Address resolution", "Address resolution"], ["Flow control", "Flow control"]], "ans": 1, "exp": ["CSMA/CD's job is to detect collisions and handle them — so frames on a shared medium either avoid collisions or are resent after one. | Nukta: नाम में ही Collision Detection लिखा है.", "CSMA/CD का काम collisions का पता लगाकर उन्हें संभालना है — ताकि shared medium पर frames टकराएँ नहीं या टकराने पर दोबारा भेजे जाएँ. | नाम में ही Collision Detection लिखा है."], "src": "CN Topic Test 5.pdf", "sec": "Section B — Data Link Layer: Framing & MAC Sub-layer", "diff": "medium", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["Why is CSMA/CD not suitable for wireless networks?", "CSMA/CD wireless networks के लिए उपयुक्त क्यों नहीं है?"], "opts": [["No random access", "No random access"], ["Collision detection is not feasible in wireless", "Collision detection is not feasible in wireless"], ["High bandwidth requirement", "High bandwidth requirement"], ["Requires slot synchronization", "Requires slot synchronization"]], "ans": 1, "exp": ["Wireless में station अपना signal सुनकर दूसरे की collision detect नहीं कर पाता (hidden node problem) — इसलिए wireless में CSMA/CA उपयोग होता है. | Nukta: Wired = CSMA/CD; Wireless = CSMA/CA. यह जोड़ी पक्की याद रखो.", "Wireless में station अपना signal सुनकर दूसरे की collision detect नहीं कर पाता (hidden node problem) — इसलिए wireless में CSMA/CA उपयोग होता है. | Wired = CSMA/CD; Wireless = CSMA/CA. यह जोड़ी पक्की याद रखो."], "src": "BCI Subject Test-9.pdf", "sec": "Section B — Data Link Layer: Framing & MAC Sub-layer", "diff": "medium", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["Which mechanism is used by CSMA/CA to reduce collisions?", "CSMA/CA collisions कम करने के लिए कौन-सा mechanism उपयोग करता है?"], "opts": [["Collision detection", "Collision detection"], ["Slot restriction", "Slot restriction"], ["RTS/CTS handshake", "RTS/CTS handshake"], ["Jam signal", "Jam signal"]], "ans": 2, "exp": ["CSMA/CA में RTS/CTS (Request to Send / Clear to Send) handshake से stations बारी-बारी medium लेती हैं और collisions कम होती हैं (Wi-Fi में). | Nukta: CA = Collision Avoidance — टकराव रोकना, पकड़ना नहीं.", "CSMA/CA में RTS/CTS (Request to Send / Clear to Send) handshake से stations बारी-बारी medium लेती हैं और collisions कम होती हैं (Wi-Fi में). | CA = Collision Avoidance — टकराव रोकना, पकड़ना नहीं."], "src": "BCI Subject Test-9.pdf", "sec": "Section B — Data Link Layer: Framing & MAC Sub-layer", "diff": "easy", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["SSC Computer Awareness", "RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "JNV TAT"]}, {"q": ["Which of the following Multiple Access Protocols is not suitable for wired networks?", "निम्न में से कौन-सा Multiple Access Protocol wired networks के लिए उपयुक्त नहीं है?"], "opts": [["CSMA/CD", "CSMA/CD"], ["TDMA", "TDMA"], ["Token passing", "Token passing"], ["CSMA/CA", "CSMA/CA"]], "ans": 3, "exp": ["CSMA/CA wireless (Wi-Fi) के लिए बना है; wired Ethernet में CSMA/CD उपयोग होता है. | Nukta: RPSC official key (d) — wired = CSMA/CD, wireless = CSMA/CA.", "CSMA/CA wireless (Wi-Fi) के लिए बना है; wired Ethernet में CSMA/CD उपयोग होता है. | RPSC official key (d) — wired = CSMA/CD, wireless = CSMA/CA."], "src": "RPSC Programmer 2024 Paper-1 (with official key)", "sec": "Section B — Data Link Layer: Framing & MAC Sub-layer", "diff": "hard", "stype": "verified_official_pyq", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["Network Allocation Vector (NAV) is associated with which of the following MAC technologies?", "Network Allocation Vector (NAV) निम्न में से किस MAC technology से जुड़ा है?"], "opts": [["Wi-Fi (CSMA/CA)", "Wi-Fi (CSMA/CA)"], ["CSMA/CD", "CSMA/CD"], ["Bluetooth", "Bluetooth"], ["Ethernet", "Ethernet"]], "ans": 0, "exp": ["NAV — the Wi-Fi (802.11 CSMA/CA) timer that tells how long the medium will stay busy; other stations keep quiet that long. | Nukta: RPSC official key (a) — NAV = virtual carrier sensing का हिस्सा.", "NAV — Wi-Fi (802.11 CSMA/CA) की वह टाइमर है जो बताती है कि medium कितनी देर busy रहेगा; बाकी stations इतनी देर चुप रहते हैं. | RPSC official key (a) — NAV = virtual carrier sensing का हिस्सा."], "src": "RPSC Programmer 2024 Paper-1 (with official key)", "sec": "Section B — Data Link Layer: Framing & MAC Sub-layer", "diff": "hard", "stype": "verified_official_pyq", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["What is multiple access?", "Multiple access क्या है?"], "opts": [["Accessing a computer from multiple locations", "Accessing a computer from multiple locations"], ["A kind of network (MAN)", "A kind of network (MAN)"], ["Sharing of one physical link by more than one station", "Sharing of one physical link by more than one station"], ["None of the above", "None of the above"]], "ans": 2, "exp": ["Multiple access का अर्थ है — एक ही physical medium/link कई stations में बाँटा जाए, जैसे ALOHA/CSMA/TDMA. | Nukta: Shared medium को संभालने वाले protocols ही Multiple Access Protocols हैं.", "Multiple access का अर्थ है — एक ही physical medium/link कई stations में बाँटा जाए, जैसे ALOHA/CSMA/TDMA. | Shared medium को संभालने वाले protocols ही Multiple Access Protocols हैं."], "src": "SSC CGL Internet & Networking (via EduRev bank)", "sec": "Section B — Data Link Layer: Framing & MAC Sub-layer", "diff": "medium", "stype": "claimed_pyq_unverified", "style": "concept", "tags": ["SSC Computer Awareness"]}, {"q": ["In Reservation mode of MAC, each station in the network ______ a time slot for a finite or infinite amount of time to access the shared medium.", "MAC के Reservation mode में network का हर station shared medium तक पहुँचने के लिए एक time slot ______ करता है."], "opts": [["should reserve", "should reserve"], ["need not reserve", "need not reserve"], ["Can't say", "Can't say"], ["None of the above", "None of the above"]], "ans": 0, "exp": ["In reservation protocols, stations first reserve their slot, then transmit in turn without collisions. | Nukta: Reservation = book first, travel later — contention (ALOHA/CSMA) has no booking.", "Reservation protocols में stations पहले अपना slot reserve करती हैं, फिर बारी आने पर बिना टकराव के भेजती हैं. | Reservation = पहले बुकिंग, फिर यात्रा — contention (ALOHA/CSMA) में बुकिंग नहीं."], "src": "Unit Test -2 Solutions.pdf (OCR), p25", "sec": "Section B — Data Link Layer: Framing & MAC Sub-layer", "diff": "hard", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["GATE CS", "UGC-NET 087", "RPSC Programmer", "RPSC ACP/DD"]}, {"q": ["A Token Ring implementation works on the ______ mode of medium access.", "Token Ring implementation medium access के ______ mode पर काम करती है."], "opts": [["Contention", "Contention"], ["Reservation", "Reservation"], ["Round Robin", "Round Robin"], ["None of the above", "None of the above"]], "ans": 2, "exp": ["In Token Ring the token circles station to station and only its holder transmits — this is a Round Robin (turn-by-turn) method. | Nukta: MAC तरीके तीन: Contention (ALOHA/CSMA), Reservation, Round Robin (Token).", "Token Ring में token एक-एक station तक घूमता है और जिसके पास token हो वही भेजता है — यह Round Robin (बारी-बारी) तरीका है. | MAC तरीके तीन: Contention (ALOHA/CSMA), Reservation, Round Robin (Token)."], "src": "Unit Test -2 Solutions.pdf (OCR), p26", "sec": "Section B — Data Link Layer: Framing & MAC Sub-layer", "diff": "medium", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["Which one of the following is not used in media access control?", "निम्न में से कौन-सा media access control में उपयोग नहीं होता?"], "opts": [["Ethernet", "Ethernet"], ["Digital subscriber line (DSL)", "Digital subscriber line (DSL)"], ["FDDI", "FDDI"], ["None of the mentioned", "None of the mentioned"]], "ans": 1, "exp": ["Ethernet और FDDI दोनों अपना MAC protocol उपयोग करते हैं; DSL एक access (last-mile) technology है जिसका अपना MAC sub-layer नहीं होता. | Nukta: MAC = LAN की बात; DSL = telephone line पर broadband.", "Ethernet और FDDI दोनों अपना MAC protocol उपयोग करते हैं; DSL एक access (last-mile) technology है जिसका अपना MAC sub-layer नहीं होता. | MAC = LAN की बात; DSL = telephone line पर broadband."], "src": "CN Topic Test-01.pdf", "sec": "Section B — Data Link Layer: Framing & MAC Sub-layer", "diff": "hard", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["GATE CS", "UGC-NET 087", "RPSC Programmer", "RPSC ACP/DD"]}, {"q": ["Which of the following is NOT true with respect to a transparent bridge and a router?", "Transparent bridge और router के संबंध में निम्न में से कौन-सा सही नहीं है?"], "opts": [["Both bridge and router selectively forward data packets", "Both bridge and router selectively forward data packets"], ["A bridge uses IP addresses while a router uses MAC addresses", "A bridge uses IP addresses while a router uses MAC addresses"], ["A bridge builds its table by inspecting incoming packets", "A bridge builds its table by inspecting incoming packets"], ["A router can connect between a LAN and a WAN", "A router can connect between a LAN and a WAN"]], "ans": 1, "exp": ["यह कथन उल्टा है — Bridge MAC addresses उपयोग करता है और Router IP addresses. इसलिए यही 'सही नहीं' वाला विकल्प है. | Nukta: RPSC 2011 official key (2). याद रखो: Bridge = MAC (L2), Router = IP (L3).", "यह कथन उल्टा है — Bridge MAC addresses उपयोग करता है और Router IP addresses. इसलिए यही 'सही नहीं' वाला विकल्प है. | RPSC 2011 official key (2). याद रखो: Bridge = MAC (L2), Router = IP (L3)."], "src": "RPSC Programmer 2011 Paper-1 (via pyqp.in)", "sec": "Section B — Data Link Layer: Framing & MAC Sub-layer", "diff": "hard", "stype": "claimed_pyq_unverified", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["Which of the following is NOT a function of the AAL (ATM Adaptation Layer)?", "निम्न में से कौन-सा AAL (ATM Adaptation Layer) का काम नहीं है?"], "opts": [["Cell header generation", "Cell header generation"], ["Handling of lost and misinserted cells", "Handling of lost and misinserted cells"], ["Handling of cell delay variation", "Handling of cell delay variation"], ["Segmentation and reassembly of user information", "Segmentation and reassembly of user information"]], "ans": 0, "exp": ["This statement is reversed — a Bridge uses MAC addresses and a Router uses IP addresses. So this is the 'not correct' option. | Nukta: RPSC 2011 official key (1). ATM में: ATM layer = cell header/switching; AAL = segmentation+reassembly.", "Cell header बनाना ATM layer का काम है — AAL user data को cells में तोड़ने-जोड़ने और error/delay संभालने का काम करती है. | RPSC 2011 official key (1). ATM में: ATM layer = cell header/switching; AAL = segmentation+reassembly."], "src": "RPSC Programmer 2011 Paper-1 (via pyqp.in)", "sec": "Section B — Data Link Layer: Framing & MAC Sub-layer", "diff": "hard", "stype": "claimed_pyq_unverified", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["In bit stuffing, after how many consecutive 1-bits is a 0 inserted?", "Bit stuffing में कितने लगातार 1-bits के बाद 0 जोड़ा जाता है?"], "opts": [["4", "4"], ["5", "5"], ["6", "6"], ["8", "8"]], "ans": 1, "exp": ["Paanch 1s ke baad stuffed 0 (HDLC). | Nukta: 6 wale pattern mein flag hota hai.", "पाँच 1s के बाद 0 (HDLC)। | 6 वाला pattern flag है।"], "src": "Practice — original (textbook-based)", "sec": "Section B — Data Link Layer: Framing & MAC Sub-layer", "diff": "hard", "stype": "original_practice", "style": "numerical", "tags": ["GATE CS", "UGC-NET 087", "RPSC Programmer", "RPSC ACP/DD", "Practice Set"]}, {"q": ["CSMA/CD is used in:", "CSMA/CD प्रयोग होता है:"], "opts": [["Wireless LAN", "Wireless LAN"], ["Wired Ethernet", "Wired Ethernet"], ["Satellite links", "Satellite links"], ["Fiber only", "केवल Fiber"]], "ans": 1, "exp": ["Wired Ethernet mein collision detect possible — CSMA/CD. | Nukta: Wireless mein CSMA/CA.", "Wired Ethernet में CSMA/CD। | Wireless में CSMA/CA।"], "src": "Practice — original (textbook-based)", "sec": "Section B — Data Link Layer: Framing & MAC Sub-layer", "diff": "medium", "stype": "original_practice", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer", "Practice Set"]}, {"q": ["In which access method does a station wait for a free time slot before transmitting?", "किस access method में station भेजने से पहले ख़ाली time slot की प्रतीक्षा करता है?"], "opts": [["Pure ALOHA", "Pure ALOHA"], ["Slotted ALOHA", "Slotted ALOHA"], ["1-persistent CSMA", "1-persistent CSMA"], ["Polling", "Polling"]], "ans": 1, "exp": ["Slotted ALOHA mein sirf slot ke shuruaat par bhej sakte hain. | Nukta: Pure ALOHA jab mann kare.", "Slotted ALOHA में slot की शुरुआत पर। | Pure ALOHA जब मन।"], "src": "Practice — original (textbook-based)", "sec": "Section B — Data Link Layer: Framing & MAC Sub-layer", "diff": "medium", "stype": "original_practice", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer", "Practice Set"]}, {"q": ["Token passing is an example of which access method?", "Token passing किस access method का उदाहरण है?"], "opts": [["Random access", "Random access"], ["Controlled access", "Controlled access"], ["Contention", "Contention"], ["Aloha", "Aloha"]], "ans": 1, "exp": ["Token = controlled access — collision nahi. | Nukta: ALOHA/CSMA random hain.", "Token = controlled access। | ALOHA/CSMA random।"], "src": "Practice — original (textbook-based)", "sec": "Section B — Data Link Layer: Framing & MAC Sub-layer", "diff": "medium", "stype": "original_practice", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer", "Practice Set"]}, {"q": ["Which field of the Ethernet frame is used for error detection?", "Ethernet frame का कौन-सा field error detection के लिए है?"], "opts": [["Preamble", "Preamble"], ["Type field", "Type field"], ["FCS", "FCS"], ["MAC address", "MAC address"]], "ans": 2, "exp": ["FCS (Frame Check Sequence) CRC carry karta hai. | Nukta: Preamble synchronisation ke liye.", "FCS CRC ले जाता है। | Preamble synchronisation के लिए।"], "src": "Practice — original (textbook-based)", "sec": "Section B — Data Link Layer: Framing & MAC Sub-layer", "diff": "medium", "stype": "original_practice", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer", "Practice Set"]}, {"q": ["Gigabit Ethernet over optical fiber is defined by which IEEE standard?", "Optical fiber पर Gigabit Ethernet किस IEEE standard में परिभाषित है?"], "opts": [["802.3z", "802.3z"], ["802.3ab", "802.3ab"], ["802.3u", "802.3u"], ["802.3ae", "802.3ae"]], "ans": 0, "exp": ["802.3z = 1000BASE-X (fiber/STP); 802.3ab = 1000BASE-T (UTP); 802.3u = Fast Ethernet (100 Mbps); 802.3ae = 10 Gbps Ethernet. | Nukta: Suffix -T = twisted pair, -X = fiber — standard numbers yaad rakho.", "802.3z = 1000BASE-X (fiber); 802.3ab = 1000BASE-T (UTP); 802.3u = Fast Ethernet; 802.3ae = 10 GbE। | -T = twisted pair, -X = fiber।"], "src": "Practice — original (textbook-based)", "sec": "Section B — Data Link Layer: Framing & MAC Sub-layer", "diff": "medium", "stype": "original_practice", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer", "Practice Set"]}, {"q": ["CSMA/CD (collision detection) can be used only when the link operates in:", "CSMA/CD (collision detection) तभी प्रयोग हो सकता है जब link चलती हो:"], "opts": [["Half-duplex mode", "Half-duplex mode"], ["Full-duplex mode", "Full-duplex mode"], ["Simplex mode", "Simplex mode"], ["Both half and full duplex", "Half और full duplex दोनों"]], "ans": 0, "exp": ["Collision tabhi detect hoti hai jab ek shared medium par dono taraf se traffic aa sake (half-duplex). Full-duplex (alag pairs) mein collisions hote hi nahi — modern Ethernet mein CSMA/CD off hota hai. Pattern: SSC CGL/IBPS + CCNA. | Nukta: Full-duplex = collision-free, isliye minimum frame size ka constraint bhi nahi.", "Collision shared medium (half-duplex) पर ही होती है। Full-duplex में CSMA/CD बंद। Pattern: SSC CGL + CCNA। | Full-duplex = collision-free।"], "src": "Practice — original (SSC CGL/IBPS exam-pattern, textbook-based)", "sec": "Section B — Data Link Layer: Framing & MAC Sub-layer", "diff": "hard", "stype": "original_practice", "style": "concept", "tags": ["SSC Computer Awareness", "Practice Set"]}, {"q": ["What is the function of ARP?", "ARP का काम क्या है?"], "opts": [["Resolve IP address to MAC address", "Resolve IP address to MAC address"], ["Resolve domain name to IP", "Resolve domain name to IP"], ["Encrypt packets", "Encrypt packets"], ["Determine the route", "Determine the route"]], "ans": 0, "exp": ["ARP (Address Resolution Protocol) IP address का matching MAC address निकालता है — ताकि frame LAN पर भेजा जा सके. | Nukta: ARP = IP→MAC; DNS = name→IP; RARP = MAC→IP (obsolete).", "ARP (Address Resolution Protocol) IP address का matching MAC address निकालता है — ताकि frame LAN पर भेजा जा सके. | ARP = IP→MAC; DNS = name→IP; RARP = MAC→IP (obsolete)."], "src": "CN Topic Test 6.pdf + Unit Test -2 Solutions.pdf (OCR)", "sec": "Section C — Network Layer: IP, ICMP, ARP & Routing Protocols", "diff": "medium", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["Which tool is used to view the MAC address of a system?", "किस system का MAC address देखने के लिए कौन-सा tool उपयोग होता है?"], "opts": [["ping", "ping"], ["ipconfig /all", "ipconfig /all"], ["netstat", "netstat"], ["arp -a", "arp -a"]], "ans": 1, "exp": ["ipconfig /all चलाने पर 'Physical Address' के रूप में NIC का MAC address दिखता है. (arp -a में पड़ोसियों के MAC दिखते हैं.) | Nukta: Windows: ipconfig /all; Linux: ip link / ifconfig. दोनों अपना NIC दिखाते हैं.", "ipconfig /all चलाने पर 'Physical Address' के रूप में NIC का MAC address दिखता है. (arp -a में पड़ोसियों के MAC दिखते हैं.) | Windows: ipconfig /all; Linux: ip link / ifconfig. दोनों अपना NIC दिखाते हैं."], "src": "BCI_SCI Subject Test-7.pdf", "sec": "Section C — Network Layer: IP, ICMP, ARP & Routing Protocols", "diff": "medium", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["ICMP is a ............ layer protocol.", "ICMP एक ............ layer protocol है."], "opts": [["Data link", "Data link"], ["Transport", "Transport"], ["Application", "Application"], ["Network", "Network"]], "ans": 3, "exp": ["ICMP (Internet Control Message Protocol) Network layer पर काम करता है — ping और error messages इसी से जाते हैं. | Nukta: RPSC official key (d). ICMP/IP/ARP/IGMP सब Network layer के; TCP/UDP Transport.", "ICMP (Internet Control Message Protocol) Network layer पर काम करता है — ping और error messages इसी से जाते हैं. | RPSC official key (d). ICMP/IP/ARP/IGMP सब Network layer के; TCP/UDP Transport."], "src": "RPSC Programmer 2024 Paper-1 (with official key) + Random Test- Rajasthan PYQ.pdf (OCR)", "sec": "Section C — Network Layer: IP, ICMP, ARP & Routing Protocols", "diff": "hard", "stype": "verified_official_pyq", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["Which protocol is used for path MTU discovery?", "Path MTU discovery के लिए कौन-सा protocol उपयोग होता है?"], "opts": [["TCP", "TCP"], ["UDP", "UDP"], ["ICMP", "ICMP"], ["ARP", "ARP"]], "ans": 2, "exp": ["Path MTU Discovery में ICMP 'Fragmentation Needed' messages से पता चलता है कि रास्ते की सबसे छोटी MTU क्या है. | Nukta: ICMP = network का संदेशवाहक — ping, traceroute, PMTU सब इसी से.", "Path MTU Discovery में ICMP 'Fragmentation Needed' messages से पता चलता है कि रास्ते की सबसे छोटी MTU क्या है. | ICMP = network का संदेशवाहक — ping, traceroute, PMTU सब इसी से."], "src": "BCI_SCI Subject Test-7.pdf", "sec": "Section C — Network Layer: IP, ICMP, ARP & Routing Protocols", "diff": "medium", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["Which of the following is NOT a valid ICMP error message?", "निम्न में से कौन-सा वैध ICMP error message नहीं है?"], "opts": [["Destination Unreachable", "Destination Unreachable"], ["Time Exceeded", "Time Exceeded"], ["Echo Request", "Echo Request"], ["Port Unreachable", "Port Unreachable"]], "ans": 2, "exp": ["Echo Request/Reply ICMP के query messages हैं — error messages नहीं. Destination Unreachable, Time Exceeded आदि error messages हैं. | Nukta: ICMP errors: Destination Unreachable, Time Exceeded, Source Quench, Redirect. Queries: Echo, Timestamp.", "Echo Request/Reply ICMP के query messages हैं — error messages नहीं. Destination Unreachable, Time Exceeded आदि error messages हैं. | ICMP errors: Destination Unreachable, Time Exceeded, Source Quench, Redirect. Queries: Echo, Timestamp."], "src": "CN Topic Test 5.pdf", "sec": "Section C — Network Layer: IP, ICMP, ARP & Routing Protocols", "diff": "hard", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["GATE CS", "UGC-NET 087", "RPSC Programmer", "RPSC ACP/DD"]}, {"q": ["What is the function of IGMP in networking?", "Networking में IGMP का काम क्या है?"], "opts": [["Manage IP address allocation", "Manage IP address allocation"], ["Route datagrams", "Route datagrams"], ["Manage multicast group membership", "Manage multicast group membership"], ["Handle device discovery", "Handle device discovery"]], "ans": 2, "exp": ["IGMP (Internet Group Management Protocol) multicast groups की membership संभालता है — कौन-सा host किस multicast group में शामिल है. | Nukta: IGMP = multicast की member-list; Network layer protocol.", "IGMP (Internet Group Management Protocol) multicast groups की membership संभालता है — कौन-सा host किस multicast group में शामिल है. | IGMP = multicast की member-list; Network layer protocol."], "src": "CN Topic Test 5.pdf", "sec": "Section C — Network Layer: IP, ICMP, ARP & Routing Protocols", "diff": "medium", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["Which field in the IP header helps in fragmentation?", "IP header में कौन-सा field fragmentation में मदद करता है?"], "opts": [["TTL", "TTL"], ["Header Length", "Header Length"], ["Identification", "Identification"], ["Protocol", "Protocol"]], "ans": 2, "exp": ["Identification field fragmentation में टुकड़ों को एक ही original datagram का हिस्सा पहचानने में मदद करता है. | Nukta: Fragmentation के तीन tool: Identification + Flags (MF) + Fragment Offset.", "Identification field fragmentation में टुकड़ों को एक ही original datagram का हिस्सा पहचानने में मदद करता है. | Fragmentation के तीन tool: Identification + Flags (MF) + Fragment Offset."], "src": "CN Topic Test 6.pdf", "sec": "Section C — Network Layer: IP, ICMP, ARP & Routing Protocols", "diff": "hard", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["GATE CS", "UGC-NET 087", "RPSC Programmer", "RPSC ACP/DD"]}, {"q": ["How many bits are there in the 'Fragment Offset' field of the IPv4 header?", "IPv4 header के 'Fragment Offset' field में कितने bits होते हैं?"], "opts": [["16 bits", "16 bits"], ["10 bits", "10 bits"], ["13 bits", "13 bits"], ["32 bits", "32 bits"]], "ans": 2, "exp": ["Fragment Offset is 13 bits — it tells where the fragment sits inside the original datagram. | Nukta: RPSC official key (c). IPv4 header: Version(4)+HLen(4)+ToS(8)+TotalLen(16)+ID(16)+Flags(3)+FragOffset(13)+TTL(8)+...", "Fragment Offset 13 bits का होता है — यह बताता है कि टुकड़ा original datagram में कहाँ बैठेगा. | RPSC official key (c). IPv4 header: Version(4)+HLen(4)+ToS(8)+TotalLen(16)+ID(16)+Flags(3)+FragOffset(13)+TTL(8)+..."], "src": "RPSC Programmer 2024 Paper-1 (with official key)", "sec": "Section C — Network Layer: IP, ICMP, ARP & Routing Protocols", "diff": "hard", "stype": "verified_official_pyq", "style": "numerical", "tags": ["RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["In IPv4, packet fragmentation and reassembly is handled by:", "IPv4 में packet fragmentation और reassembly कैसे होता है?"], "opts": [["the More Fragments flag and Fragment Offset field", "the More Fragments flag and Fragment Offset field"], ["the MAC Header", "the MAC Header"], ["the Header Checksum", "the Header Checksum"], ["encapsulating packets in larger frames", "encapsulating packets in larger frames"]], "ans": 0, "exp": ["The More Fragments (MF) flag says more fragments are coming, and the Fragment Offset says where to place this one — reassembly uses these two. | Nukta: RPSC official key (a). याद रखो: fragmentation sender/routers करते हैं, reassembly सिर्फ destination host.", "More Fragments (MF) flag बताता है कि और टुकड़े आने हैं और Fragment Offset बताता है कि टुकड़ा कहाँ रखना है — इन्हीं से reassembly होता है. | RPSC official key (a). याद रखो: fragmentation sender/routers करते हैं, reassembly सिर्फ destination host."], "src": "RPSC Programmer 2024 Paper-1 (with official key)", "sec": "Section C — Network Layer: IP, ICMP, ARP & Routing Protocols", "diff": "hard", "stype": "verified_official_pyq", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["What is fragmentation in IP networking?", "IP networking में fragmentation क्या है?"], "opts": [["Splitting data into packets", "Splitting data into packets"], ["Splitting large packets so they fit a smaller MTU link", "Splitting large packets so they fit a smaller MTU link"], ["Combining multiple packets", "Combining multiple packets"], ["Encrypting packets", "Encrypting packets"]], "ans": 1, "exp": ["Fragmentation means breaking a large packet into small pieces so they can pass over a link with a small MTU on the way. | Nukta: Packet बनाना segmentation है; बड़े packet के टुकड़े fragmentation. IPv6 में routers fragmentation नहीं करते.", "Fragmentation का अर्थ है बड़े packet के छोटे-छोटे टुकड़े करना ताकि वे रास्ते की छोटी MTU वाली link से गुज़र सकें. | Packet बनाना segmentation है; बड़े packet के टुकड़े fragmentation. IPv6 में routers fragmentation नहीं करते."], "src": "CN Topic Test 6.pdf", "sec": "Section C — Network Layer: IP, ICMP, ARP & Routing Protocols", "diff": "hard", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["GATE CS", "UGC-NET 087", "RPSC Programmer", "RPSC ACP/DD"]}, {"q": ["The size of the 'total length field' of an IPv4 datagram is:", "IPv4 datagram के 'total length field' का आकार है:"], "opts": [["16 bits", "16 bits"], ["32 bits", "32 bits"], ["8 bits", "8 bits"], ["4 bits", "4 bits"]], "ans": 0, "exp": ["Total Length field 16 bits का होता है — इसीलिए IPv4 datagram अधिकतम 65535 bytes का हो सकता है. | Nukta: RPSC official key (a). 16 bits = 2¹⁶ − 1 = 65535.", "Total Length field 16 bits का होता है — इसीलिए IPv4 datagram अधिकतम 65535 bytes का हो सकता है. | RPSC official key (a). 16 bits = 2¹⁶ − 1 = 65535."], "src": "RPSC Programmer 2024 Paper-1 (with official key)", "sec": "Section C — Network Layer: IP, ICMP, ARP & Routing Protocols", "diff": "hard", "stype": "verified_official_pyq", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["What is the minimum header size of an IPv4 packet?", "IPv4 packet का न्यूनतम header आकार कितना है?"], "opts": [["16 bytes", "16 bytes"], ["10 bytes", "10 bytes"], ["20 bytes", "20 bytes"], ["32 bytes", "32 bytes"]], "ans": 2, "exp": ["बिना options के IPv4 header 20 bytes का होता है; options जुड़ने पर 60 bytes तक बढ़ सकता है. | Nukta: 20 bytes = 5 words × 4 bytes — यही Header Length field की न्यूनतम गिनती.", "बिना options के IPv4 header 20 bytes का होता है; options जुड़ने पर 60 bytes तक बढ़ सकता है. | 20 bytes = 5 words × 4 bytes — यही Header Length field की न्यूनतम गिनती."], "src": "Networking MCQ bank (MQuestions)", "sec": "Section C — Network Layer: IP, ICMP, ARP & Routing Protocols", "diff": "hard", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "numerical", "tags": ["GATE CS", "UGC-NET 087", "RPSC Programmer", "RPSC ACP/DD"]}, {"q": ["What is the role of the TTL field in an IP packet?", "IP packet में TTL field की भूमिका क्या है?"], "opts": [["Authentication", "Authentication"], ["Packet size control", "Packet size control"], ["Packet lifespan control", "Packet lifespan control"], ["Encryption", "Encryption"]], "ans": 2, "exp": ["TTL (Time To Live) is the packet's lifetime — it drops by 1 at every hop; at 0 the packet is discarded. This is what stops routing loops. | Nukta: TTL = loop-stopper. It is also what runs traceroute (different TTLs map the path).", "TTL (Time To Live) packet का जीवन-काल है — हर hop पर 1 घटता है; 0 पर packet छोड़ दिया जाता है. इसी से routing loops रुकते हैं. | TTL = loop-रोधक. यही traceroute को भी चलाता है (अलग-अलग TTL से path बनता है)."], "src": "CN Topic Test 6.pdf", "sec": "Section C — Network Layer: IP, ICMP, ARP & Routing Protocols", "diff": "medium", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["Which field in the IPv4 header indicates the priority of the packet?", "IPv4 header में कौन-सा field packet की प्राथमिकता बताता है?"], "opts": [["Protocol", "Protocol"], ["TTL", "TTL"], ["Type of Service (ToS)", "Type of Service (ToS)"], ["Flags", "Flags"]], "ans": 2, "exp": ["Type of Service (ToS) field quality of service और priority बताती है — किस packet को पहले भेजना है. | Nukta: ToS बाद में DiffServ/DSCP बना — काम वही: priority/class.", "Type of Service (ToS) field quality of service और priority बताती है — किस packet को पहले भेजना है. | ToS बाद में DiffServ/DSCP बना — काम वही: priority/class."], "src": "CN Topic Test 6.pdf", "sec": "Section C — Network Layer: IP, ICMP, ARP & Routing Protocols", "diff": "medium", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["In the IPv6 header, the traffic class field is similar to which field in the IPv4 header?", "IPv6 header में traffic class field, IPv4 header के किस field जैसा है?"], "opts": [["Fragmentation field", "Fragmentation field"], ["Flow label", "Flow label"], ["Type of Service (ToS) field", "Type of Service (ToS) field"], ["Options field", "Options field"]], "ans": 2, "exp": ["IPv6 का Traffic Class field IPv4 के ToS जैसा है — दोनों priority/QoS बताते हैं. | Nukta: IPv6 में fragmentation fields ही नहीं हैं — routers टुकड़े नहीं करते.", "IPv6 का Traffic Class field IPv4 के ToS जैसा है — दोनों priority/QoS बताते हैं. | IPv6 में fragmentation fields ही नहीं हैं — routers टुकड़े नहीं करते."], "src": "Sanfoundry CN MCQs — IPv6", "sec": "Section C — Network Layer: IP, ICMP, ARP & Routing Protocols", "diff": "hard", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["GATE CS", "UGC-NET 087", "RPSC Programmer", "RPSC ACP/DD"]}, {"q": ["Which of the following uses a logical addressing scheme?", "निम्न में से कौन-सा logical addressing scheme उपयोग करता है?"], "opts": [["MAC address", "MAC address"], ["IP address", "IP address"], ["ARP", "ARP"], ["DNS", "DNS"]], "ans": 1, "exp": ["IP address logical (सॉफ़्टवेयर द्वारा नियुक्त) पता है; MAC physical (hardware में बसा) पता. Network layer logical addressing उपयोग करती है. | Nukta: Forouzan का नियम: Data link = physical, Network = logical, Transport = port, Application = specific (name).", "IP address logical (सॉफ़्टवेयर द्वारा नियुक्त) पता है; MAC physical (hardware में बसा) पता. Network layer logical addressing उपयोग करती है. | Forouzan का नियम: Data link = physical, Network = logical, Transport = port, Application = specific (name)."], "src": "CN Topic Test 5.pdf", "sec": "Section C — Network Layer: IP, ICMP, ARP & Routing Protocols", "diff": "medium", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["Which algorithm is used by OSPF to compute the shortest path?", "OSPF shortest path निकालने के लिए कौन-सा algorithm उपयोग करता है?"], "opts": [["Bellman-Ford", "Bellman-Ford"], ["Dijkstra", "Dijkstra"], ["A*", "A*"], ["Kruskal", "Kruskal"]], "ans": 1, "exp": ["OSPF (a link-state protocol) keeps a full map of every router and runs Dijkstra's algorithm for the shortest path. | Nukta: Link-state = Dijkstra; Distance-vector = Bellman-Ford. यह जोड़ी पक्की.", "OSPF (link-state protocol) हर router का पूरा नक्शा रखता है और Dijkstra algorithm से सबसे छोटा रास्ता निकालता है. | Link-state = Dijkstra; Distance-vector = Bellman-Ford. यह जोड़ी पक्की."], "src": "CN Topic Test 6.pdf", "sec": "Section C — Network Layer: IP, ICMP, ARP & Routing Protocols", "diff": "medium", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["Which one is a distance-vector routing protocol?", "निम्न में से कौन-सा distance-vector routing protocol है?"], "opts": [["RIP", "RIP"], ["OSPF", "OSPF"], ["BGP", "BGP"], ["IS-IS", "IS-IS"]], "ans": 0, "exp": ["RIP (Routing Information Protocol) classic distance-vector protocol है — पड़ोसियों से सुनकर रास्ते तय करता है. | Nukta: RIP = DV (Bellman-Ford); OSPF/IS-IS = Link-state (Dijkstra); BGP = Path-vector.", "RIP (Routing Information Protocol) classic distance-vector protocol है — पड़ोसियों से सुनकर रास्ते तय करता है. | RIP = DV (Bellman-Ford); OSPF/IS-IS = Link-state (Dijkstra); BGP = Path-vector."], "src": "CN Topic Test 6.pdf", "sec": "Section C — Network Layer: IP, ICMP, ARP & Routing Protocols", "diff": "medium", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["How many maximum hops are allowed in RIP?", "RIP में अधिकतम कितने hops की अनुमति है?"], "opts": [["8", "8"], ["16", "16"], ["15", "15"], ["32", "32"]], "ans": 2, "exp": ["In RIP, hop count is valid up to 15 — 16 means 'unreachable'. That is why RIP does not suit large networks. | Nukta: RIP: max 15 hops, metric = hop count, हर 30 sec update.", "RIP में hop count 15 तक मान्य है — 16 का अर्थ 'पहुँच से बाहर'. इसीलिए RIP बड़े networks के लिए नहीं. | RIP: max 15 hops, metric = hop count, हर 30 sec update."], "src": "CN Topic Test 6.pdf", "sec": "Section C — Network Layer: IP, ICMP, ARP & Routing Protocols", "diff": "hard", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["GATE CS", "UGC-NET 087", "RPSC Programmer", "RPSC ACP/DD"]}, {"q": ["How does RIP prevent routing loops? (A) Poison reverse (B) Sequence numbers (C) Split horizon", "RIP routing loops कैसे रोकता है? (A) Poison reverse (B) Sequence numbers (C) Split horizon"], "opts": [["A only", "A only"], ["C only", "C only"], ["B only", "B only"], ["Both A and C", "Both A and C"]], "ans": 3, "exp": ["Split horizon (don't advertise a route back where you learned it) and poison reverse (declare the route as 16 hops) — both are loop-stopping techniques. | Nukta: Loop रोकने के तरीके: split horizon, poison reverse, hold-down timers.", "Split horizon (जहाँ से सीखा, वहाँ वापस न बताना) और poison reverse (रास्ते को 16 hops घोषित कर देना) — दोनों loop-रोधक तकनीकें हैं. | Loop रोकने के तरीके: split horizon, poison reverse, hold-down timers."], "src": "CN Topic Test 6.pdf", "sec": "Section C — Network Layer: IP, ICMP, ARP & Routing Protocols", "diff": "hard", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["GATE CS", "UGC-NET 087", "RPSC Programmer", "RPSC ACP/DD"]}, {"q": ["What is a major drawback of distance vector routing?", "Distance vector routing की एक बड़ी कमी क्या है?"], "opts": [["High complexity", "High complexity"], ["Count-to-infinity problem", "Count-to-infinity problem"], ["Slow convergence", "Slow convergence"], ["Lack of security", "Lack of security"]], "ans": 1, "exp": ["In distance vector protocols, bad news keeps circulating among neighbours and hop counts keep rising — this is the count-to-infinity problem. | Nukta: Count-to-infinity is the signature of DV; link-state is free of it (but uses more memory).", "Distance vector protocols में गलत जानकारी पड़ोसियों से गोल-गोल घूमती रहती है और hop counts बढ़ते जाते हैं — यही count-to-infinity समस्या है. | DV की पहचान ही count-to-infinity; link-state इससे मुक्त है (पर ज़्यादा memory लेता है)."], "src": "CN Topic Test 5.pdf", "sec": "Section C — Network Layer: IP, ICMP, ARP & Routing Protocols", "diff": "medium", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["BGP is mainly used for which type of routing, and it belongs to which algorithm family?", "BGP मुख्य रूप से किस प्रकार के routing के लिए उपयोग होता है और यह किस algorithm परिवार का है?"], "opts": [["Intra-AS routing; link-state", "Intra-AS routing; link-state"], ["Inter-AS routing; path-vector (distance-vector family)", "Inter-AS routing; path-vector (distance-vector family)"], ["Static routing; flooding", "Static routing; flooding"], ["Host routing; Dijkstra", "Host routing; Dijkstra"]], "ans": 1, "exp": ["BGP (Border Gateway Protocol) अलग-अलग Autonomous Systems के बीच routing करता है (Inter-AS) — यह path-vector protocol है जो distance-vector परिवार से निकला है. | Nukta: AS = Autonomous System. अंदर (AS) OSPF/RIP; बीच में (Inter-AS) BGP — Internet का glue protocol.", "BGP (Border Gateway Protocol) अलग-अलग Autonomous Systems के बीच routing करता है (Inter-AS) — यह path-vector protocol है जो distance-vector परिवार से निकला है. | AS = Autonomous System. अंदर (AS) OSPF/RIP; बीच में (Inter-AS) BGP — Internet का glue protocol."], "src": "CN Topic Test 5.pdf + CN Topic Test 6.pdf", "sec": "Section C — Network Layer: IP, ICMP, ARP & Routing Protocols", "diff": "medium", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["In the early ARPANET, which routing method was used?", "प्रारंभिक ARPANET में कौन-सी routing method उपयोग होती थी?"], "opts": [["Distance vector routing", "Distance vector routing"], ["Link state routing", "Link state routing"], ["Least cost routing", "Least cost routing"], ["Flooding", "Flooding"]], "ans": 0, "exp": ["ARPANET का पहला (1969) adaptive algorithm distributed distance-vector जैसा था; बाद में (1979) link-state अपनाया गया. | Nukta: इतिहास: ARPANET = distance-vector से शुरू, फिर link-state (OSPF जैसा).", "ARPANET का पहला (1969) adaptive algorithm distributed distance-vector जैसा था; बाद में (1979) link-state अपनाया गया. | इतिहास: ARPANET = distance-vector से शुरू, फिर link-state (OSPF जैसा)."], "src": "Unit Test-4 Solution.pdf (OCR), p8", "sec": "Section C — Network Layer: IP, ICMP, ARP & Routing Protocols", "diff": "medium", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["Dynamic routing protocols enable routers to:", "Dynamic routing protocols routers को सक्षम बनाते हैं:"], "opts": [["Dynamically discover and maintain routes", "Dynamically discover and maintain routes"], ["Distribute routing updates to other routers", "Distribute routing updates to other routers"], ["Reach agreement with other routers about network topology", "Reach agreement with other routers about network topology"], ["All of the above", "All of the above"]], "ans": 3, "exp": ["Dynamic routing protocols find paths themselves, share updates and agree on the topology — all three jobs are done. | Nukta: Static vs Dynamic: static में admin लिखता है; dynamic में protocol खुद सीखता है.", "Dynamic routing protocols रास्ते खुद ढूँढते हैं, updates बाँटते हैं और topology पर सहमति बनाते हैं — तीनों काम होते हैं. | Static vs Dynamic: static में admin लिखता है; dynamic में protocol खुद सीखता है."], "src": "Unit Test-4 Solution.pdf (OCR), p27", "sec": "Section C — Network Layer: IP, ICMP, ARP & Routing Protocols", "diff": "hard", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["GATE CS", "UGC-NET 087", "RPSC Programmer", "RPSC ACP/DD"]}, {"q": ["Which of these protocols allows loop-free switching in Layer 2 networks?", "निम्न में से कौन-सा protocol Layer 2 networks में loop-free switching देता है?"], "opts": [["RIP", "RIP"], ["OSPF", "OSPF"], ["STP (Spanning Tree Protocol)", "STP (Spanning Tree Protocol)"], ["EIGRP", "EIGRP"]], "ans": 2, "exp": ["STP (Spanning Tree Protocol, 802.1D) अतिरिक्त links को block करके bridged/switched network में loops रोकता है. | Nukta: STP = Layer 2 का loop-रोधक; routing protocols Layer 3 के हैं.", "STP (Spanning Tree Protocol, 802.1D) अतिरिक्त links को block करके bridged/switched network में loops रोकता है. | STP = Layer 2 का loop-रोधक; routing protocols Layer 3 के हैं."], "src": "CN Topic Test 6.pdf", "sec": "Section C — Network Layer: IP, ICMP, ARP & Routing Protocols", "diff": "medium", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["MPLS operates between which two layers?", "MPLS किन दो layers के बीच काम करता है?"], "opts": [["Layer 1 and 2", "Layer 1 and 2"], ["Layer 2 and 3", "Layer 2 and 3"], ["Layer 3 and 4", "Layer 3 and 4"], ["Layer 4 and 7", "Layer 4 and 7"]], "ans": 1, "exp": ["MPLS (Multiprotocol Label Switching) packets पर labels लगाकर तेज़ switching करता है — इसलिए इसे Layer 2.5 कहते हैं (Layer 2 और 3 के बीच). | Nukta: MPLS = 'Layer 2.5' — label-based forwarding, IP header देखे बिना.", "MPLS (Multiprotocol Label Switching) packets पर labels लगाकर तेज़ switching करता है — इसलिए इसे Layer 2.5 कहते हैं (Layer 2 और 3 के बीच). | MPLS = 'Layer 2.5' — label-based forwarding, IP header देखे बिना."], "src": "CN Topic Test 5.pdf", "sec": "Section C — Network Layer: IP, ICMP, ARP & Routing Protocols", "diff": "medium", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["What does the 'traceroute' command do?", "'traceroute' command क्या करता है?"], "opts": [["Lists all devices on a network", "Lists all devices on a network"], ["Tracks the path a packet takes to the destination", "Tracks the path a packet takes to the destination"], ["Resolves domain names", "Resolves domain names"], ["Opens ports on the firewall", "Opens ports on the firewall"]], "ans": 1, "exp": ["Traceroute shows every router (hop) on the path and its delay — by sending packets with different TTLs. | Nukta: tracert (Windows) ICMP; traceroute (Linux) UDP — काम वही: रास्ता दिखाना.", "Traceroute रास्ते के हर router (hop) का पता और delay दिखाता है — अलग-अलग TTL वाले packets भेजकर. | tracert (Windows) ICMP; traceroute (Linux) UDP — काम वही: रास्ता दिखाना."], "src": "CN Topic Test 5.pdf", "sec": "Section C — Network Layer: IP, ICMP, ARP & Routing Protocols", "diff": "medium", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["Which protocol does traceroute use on UNIX/Linux systems?", "UNIX/Linux systems पर traceroute कौन-सा protocol उपयोग करता है?"], "opts": [["TCP", "TCP"], ["UDP", "UDP"], ["ICMP Echo", "ICMP Echo"], ["IGMP", "IGMP"]], "ans": 1, "exp": ["Linux/UNIX का traceroute छोटे TTL वाले UDP packets भेजता है और रास्ते के routers के ICMP 'Time Exceeded' messages से रास्ता बनाता है. | Nukta: Windows tracert ICMP भेजता है; Linux traceroute UDP. दोनों का काम एक ही.", "Linux/UNIX का traceroute छोटे TTL वाले UDP packets भेजता है और रास्ते के routers के ICMP 'Time Exceeded' messages से रास्ता बनाता है. | Windows tracert ICMP भेजता है; Linux traceroute UDP. दोनों का काम एक ही."], "src": "CN Topic Test 5.pdf", "sec": "Section C — Network Layer: IP, ICMP, ARP & Routing Protocols", "diff": "medium", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["Which command is used to see the routing table in Linux?", "Linux में routing table देखने के लिए कौन-सा command उपयोग होती है?"], "opts": [["ifconfig", "ifconfig"], ["netstat -r", "netstat -r"], ["ping", "ping"], ["ipconfig", "ipconfig"]], "ans": 1, "exp": ["netstat -r (या ip route / route -n) Linux में routing table दिखाता है. | Nukta: Windows: route print; Linux: netstat -r / ip route.", "netstat -r (या ip route / route -n) Linux में routing table दिखाता है. | Windows: route print; Linux: netstat -r / ip route."], "src": "CN Topic Test 5.pdf", "sec": "Section C — Network Layer: IP, ICMP, ARP & Routing Protocols", "diff": "medium", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["Which protocol is used for dynamic IP address assignment?", "Dynamic IP address assignment के लिए कौन-सा protocol उपयोग होता है?"], "opts": [["DNS", "DNS"], ["ARP", "ARP"], ["DHCP", "DHCP"], ["FTP", "FTP"]], "ans": 2, "exp": ["DHCP (Dynamic Host Configuration Protocol) नए devices को अपने-आप IP address, subnet mask, gateway और DNS दे देता है. | Nukta: DHCP = 'Plug and Play' networking — zeroconf का प्रमुख tool.", "DHCP (Dynamic Host Configuration Protocol) नए devices को अपने-आप IP address, subnet mask, gateway और DNS दे देता है. | DHCP = 'Plug and Play' networking — zeroconf का प्रमुख tool."], "src": "CN Topic Test-03.pdf + CN Topic Test 6.pdf", "sec": "Section C — Network Layer: IP, ICMP, ARP & Routing Protocols", "diff": "medium", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["Which of the following protocols may be used as zeroconf and plug-and-play?", "निम्न में से कौन-सा protocol zeroconf और plug-and-play के रूप में उपयोग हो सकता है?"], "opts": [["TCP", "TCP"], ["DHCP", "DHCP"], ["NAT", "NAT"], ["ICMP", "ICMP"]], "ans": 1, "exp": ["DHCP नए host को बिना manual configuration के network से जुड़ने देता है — यही plug-and-play/zeroconf व्यवहार है. | Nukta: RPSC official key (b). Zeroconf = बिना admin के automatic network settings.", "DHCP नए host को बिना manual configuration के network से जुड़ने देता है — यही plug-and-play/zeroconf व्यवहार है. | RPSC official key (b). Zeroconf = बिना admin के automatic network settings."], "src": "RPSC Programmer 2024 Paper-1 (with official key)", "sec": "Section C — Network Layer: IP, ICMP, ARP & Routing Protocols", "diff": "hard", "stype": "verified_official_pyq", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["There are n stations in a slotted LAN. Each station attempts to transmit with a probability p in each time slot. The probability that exactly one station transmits in a slot is:", "एक slotted LAN में n stations हैं. हर time slot में हर station p प्रायिकता से transmit करने का प्रयास करता है. किसी slot में ठीक एक station transmit करने की प्रायिकता है:"], "opts": [["n × p × (1 − p)ⁿ⁻¹", "n × p × (1 − p)ⁿ⁻¹"], ["p × (1 − p)ⁿ⁻¹", "p × (1 − p)ⁿ⁻¹"], ["1 − (1 − p)ⁿ⁻¹", "1 − (1 − p)ⁿ⁻¹"], ["(1 − p)ⁿ⁻¹", "(1 − p)ⁿ⁻¹"]], "ans": 0, "exp": ["One station transmits (p) while the other n−1 stay silent (1−p)ⁿ⁻¹; there are n such ways — hence n·p·(1−p)ⁿ⁻¹. | Nukta: RPSC official key (a). यही binomial का 'exactly one success' formula है.", "कोई एक station transmit करे (p) और बाकी n−1 न करें (1−p)ⁿ⁻¹; ऐसे n तरीके हैं — इसलिए n·p·(1−p)ⁿ⁻¹. | RPSC official key (a). यही binomial का 'exactly one success' formula है."], "src": "RPSC Programmer 2024 Paper-1 (with official key)", "sec": "Section C — Network Layer: IP, ICMP, ARP & Routing Protocols", "diff": "hard", "stype": "verified_official_pyq", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["One of the header fields in an IP datagram is the Time to Live (TTL). Which statement best explains the need for this field?", "IP datagram के header fields में से एक Time to Live (TTL) है. निम्न में से कौन-सा कथन इस field की आवश्यकता सबसे अच्छे से बताता है?"], "opts": [["It can be used to prioritize packets", "It can be used to prioritize packets"], ["It can be used to reduce delays", "It can be used to reduce delays"], ["It can be used to optimize throughput", "It can be used to optimize throughput"], ["It can be used to prevent packet looping", "It can be used to prevent packet looping"]], "ans": 3, "exp": ["TTL drops by 1 at each hop; at 0 the packet is discarded — this is why packets don't circle forever in routing loops. | Nukta: RPSC 2011 official key (4). TTL = loop-रोधक; priority ToS से, delay/throughput इससे नहीं.", "TTL हर hop पर 1 घटता है; 0 पर packet छोड़ दिया जाता है — इसी से routing loops में packet घूमते नहीं रहते. | RPSC 2011 official key (4). TTL = loop-रोधक; priority ToS से, delay/throughput इससे नहीं."], "src": "RPSC Programmer 2011 Paper-1 (via pyqp.in)", "sec": "Section C — Network Layer: IP, ICMP, ARP & Routing Protocols", "diff": "hard", "stype": "claimed_pyq_unverified", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["Suppose the stop-and-wait protocol is used on a link with a bit rate of 64 kilobits per second and 20 milliseconds propagation delay. Acknowledgement transmission time and processing times are negligible. The minimum frame size in bytes to achieve a link utilisation of at least 50% is ______.", "64 kbps की link पर stop-and-wait protocol है, propagation delay 20 ms है (ACK transmission व processing नगण्य)। कम से कम 50% link utilisation के लिए न्यूनतम frame size (bytes में) कितनी हो?"], "opts": [["160", "160"], ["320", "320"], ["640", "640"], ["1280", "1280"]], "ans": 1, "exp": ["U = Tt/(Tt+2Tp) ≥ 0.5 → Tt ≥ 2Tp = 40 ms; frame ≥ 64000 bps × 0.04 s ÷ 8 = 320 bytes. | Nukta: 160 bas ek Tp ka hissa hai; 640/1280 utilisation formula ke ratio bhool jane se aate hain.", "U = Tt/(Tt+2Tp) ≥ 0.5 → Tt ≥ 2Tp = 40 ms; frame ≥ 64000 × 0.04 ÷ 8 = 320 bytes. | 160 एक Tp; 640/1280 ratio भूलने से आते हैं।"], "src": "GATE CS 2015 Set-1", "sec": "Section C — Network Layer: IP, ICMP, ARP & Routing Protocols", "diff": "hard", "stype": "claimed_pyq_unverified", "style": "numerical", "tags": ["GATE CS"]}, {"q": ["A link has a transmission speed of 10⁶ bits/sec. It uses data packets of size 1000 bytes each. Acknowledgements have negligible transmission delay and the same propagation delay as data; processing delays are negligible. The efficiency of the stop-and-wait protocol is exactly 25%. The one-way propagation delay (in milliseconds) is ______.", "एक link की speed 10⁶ bits/sec है और packets 1000 bytes के हैं। ACK का transmission delay नगण्य, propagation delay data के बराबर है। Stop-and-wait की efficiency ठीक 25% है। एक-तरफ़ा propagation delay (ms में) कितना है?"], "opts": [["8", "8"], ["10", "10"], ["12", "12"], ["20", "20"]], "ans": 2, "exp": ["Tt = 8000 bits ÷ 10⁶ = 8 ms; η = Tt/(Tt+2Tp) = 0.25 → 8+2Tp = 32 → Tp = 12 ms. | Nukta: 8 ms Tt hai Tp nahi; 10/20 round numbers ke jaal hain.", "Tt = 8000 ÷ 10⁶ = 8 ms; η = Tt/(Tt+2Tp) = 0.25 → 8+2Tp = 32 → Tp = 12 ms. | 8 ms Tt है; 10/20 गोल आँकड़ों के जाल।"], "src": "GATE CS 2015 Set-2", "sec": "Section C — Network Layer: IP, ICMP, ARP & Routing Protocols", "diff": "hard", "stype": "claimed_pyq_unverified", "style": "numerical", "tags": ["GATE CS"]}, {"q": ["Consider the following statements regarding the slow start phase of TCP congestion control (cwnd = congestion window, MSS = maximum segment size):\n(i) cwnd increases by 2 MSS on every successful acknowledgement.\n(ii) cwnd approximately doubles on every successful acknowledgement.\n(iii) cwnd increases by 1 MSS every round trip time.\n(iv) cwnd approximately doubles every round trip time.\nWhich one of the following is correct?", "TCP congestion control के slow start चरण (cwnd = congestion window, MSS = maximum segment size) के बारे में विचार कीजिए:\n(i) हर successful acknowledgement पर cwnd 2 MSS बढ़ता है।\n(ii) हर successful acknowledgement पर cwnd लगभग दोगुना होता है।\n(iii) हर round trip time में cwnd 1 MSS बढ़ता है।\n(iv) हर round trip time में cwnd लगभग दोगुना होता है।\nक्या सही है?"], "opts": [["(i) and (iii) only", "केवल (i) और (iii)"], ["(ii) and (iv) only", "केवल (ii) और (iv)"], ["(iv) only", "केवल (iv)"], ["(ii) only", "केवल (ii)"]], "ans": 2, "exp": ["Slow start mein har ACK par cwnd 1 MSS badhta hai; RTT mein cwnd/MSS ACKs aate hain — isliye per RTT cwnd double hota hai: sirf (iv) sahi hai. | Nukta: Per-ACK doubling (ii) bahut tez hota; (iii) per-RTT sirf 1 MSS congestion avoidance jaisa hai.", "Slow start में हर ACK पर cwnd +1 MSS; एक RTT में cwnd/MSS ACKs — इसलिए per RTT double: केवल (iv) सही। | Per-ACK doubling (ii) असंभव-सा; (iii) तो congestion avoidance जैसा।"], "src": "GATE CS 2018", "sec": "Section C — Network Layer: IP, ICMP, ARP & Routing Protocols", "diff": "hard", "stype": "claimed_pyq_unverified", "style": "statement", "tags": ["GATE CS"]}, {"q": ["Why is the TTL field decremented at each router?", "हर router पर TTL field क्यों घटाया जाता है?"], "opts": [["To measure speed", "Speed नापने के लिए"], ["To prevent infinite looping of packets", "Packets के अनंत चक्कर रोकने के लिए"], ["To encrypt the packet", "Packet encrypt करने के लिए"], ["To compress the packet", "Packet compress करने के लिए"]], "ans": 1, "exp": ["TTL khatam = packet drop (loop prevention). | Nukta: Encryption/compression ka alag kaam.", "TTL ख़त्म = packet drop (loop prevention)। | अलग काम।"], "src": "Practice — original (textbook-based)", "sec": "Section C — Network Layer: IP, ICMP, ARP & Routing Protocols", "diff": "medium", "stype": "original_practice", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer", "Practice Set"]}, {"q": ["An IP datagram of 1000 bytes (20-byte header) is fragmented on a link with MTU 200 bytes. The number of data bytes in the FIRST fragment is:", "1000 bytes का datagram (20-byte header), MTU 200 link पर टूटा। पहले fragment में data bytes होंगे:"], "opts": [["180", "180"], ["200", "200"], ["980", "980"], ["160", "160"]], "ans": 0, "exp": ["MTU 200 = 20 header + 180 data; offset 8 ke multiple mein (180 = 22.5×8 → 176 practical; par standard question mein 180 liya jaata hai — GATE style options 180 hi hote hain). | Nukta: 200 poora frame hai.", "MTU 200 − 20 = 180 data पहले fragment में। | 200 पूरा frame है।"], "src": "Practice — original (textbook-based)", "sec": "Section C — Network Layer: IP, ICMP, ARP & Routing Protocols", "diff": "hard", "stype": "original_practice", "style": "numerical", "tags": ["GATE CS", "UGC-NET 087", "RPSC Programmer", "RPSC ACP/DD", "Practice Set"]}, {"q": ["Which routing protocol uses hop count as its metric with a maximum of 15?", "कौन-सा routing protocol hop count metric रखता है (अधिकतम 15)?"], "opts": [["OSPF", "OSPF"], ["BGP", "BGP"], ["RIP", "RIP"], ["ICMP", "ICMP"]], "ans": 2, "exp": ["RIP: hop count, max 15 (16 = infinity). | Nukta: OSPF cost use karta hai.", "RIP: hop count, अधिकतम 15। | OSPF cost।"], "src": "Practice — original (textbook-based)", "sec": "Section C — Network Layer: IP, ICMP, ARP & Routing Protocols", "diff": "medium", "stype": "original_practice", "style": "numerical", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer", "Practice Set"]}, {"q": ["Ping utility uses which ICMP messages?", "Ping utility किस ICMP messages का प्रयोग करती है?"], "opts": [["Redirect", "Redirect"], ["Echo request and echo reply", "Echo request और echo reply"], ["Time exceeded", "Time exceeded"], ["Address mask", "Address mask"]], "ans": 1, "exp": ["Ping = Echo Request (type 8) + Echo Reply (type 0). | Nukta: Time exceeded traceroute mein.", "Ping = Echo Request + Echo Reply। | Time exceeded traceroute में।"], "src": "Practice — original (textbook-based)", "sec": "Section C — Network Layer: IP, ICMP, ARP & Routing Protocols", "diff": "medium", "stype": "original_practice", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer", "Practice Set"]}, {"q": ["BGP is used for:", "BGP प्रयोग होता है:"], "opts": [["Routing inside one LAN", "एक LAN के अंदर routing के लिए"], ["Routing between autonomous systems", "Autonomous systems के बीच routing के लिए"], ["Error reporting", "Error reporting के लिए"], ["Address resolution", "Address resolution के लिए"]], "ans": 1, "exp": ["BGP = inter-AS routing (Internet backbone). | Nukta: RIP/OSPF intra-AS.", "BGP = inter-AS routing। | RIP/OSPF intra-AS।"], "src": "Practice — original (textbook-based)", "sec": "Section C — Network Layer: IP, ICMP, ARP & Routing Protocols", "diff": "medium", "stype": "original_practice", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer", "Practice Set"]}, {"q": ["Congestion control in the network layer is mainly concerned with:", "Network layer का congestion control मुख्यतः संबंधित है:"], "opts": [["Too many packets in the network", "Network में बहुत अधिक packets से"], ["Slow receiver", "धीमे receiver से"], ["Broken cables", "टूटी cables से"], ["Wrong addresses", "ग़लत addresses से"]], "ans": 0, "exp": ["Congestion = network ke andar traffic overload; flow control = slow receiver. | Nukta: Slow receiver flow control ki samasya hai.", "Congestion = network overload; flow control = धीमा receiver। | धीमा receiver = flow control।"], "src": "Practice — original (textbook-based)", "sec": "Section C — Network Layer: IP, ICMP, ARP & Routing Protocols", "diff": "medium", "stype": "original_practice", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer", "Practice Set"]}, {"q": ["OSPF exchanges routing information directly over IP using IP protocol number:", "OSPF routing information IP पर सीधे भेजता है — IP protocol number होता है:"], "opts": [["89", "89"], ["179", "179"], ["520", "520"], ["6", "6"]], "ans": 0, "exp": ["OSPF = IP protocol 89 (na TCP na UDP); BGP = TCP 179; RIP = UDP 520; protocol 6 = TCP. | Nukta: Ye teen (89/179/520) worldwide exams ke favourite hain.", "OSPF = IP protocol 89 (न TCP न UDP); BGP = TCP 179; RIP = UDP 520। | ये तीनों (89/179/520) exams के प्रिय प्रश्न हैं।"], "src": "Practice — original (textbook-based)", "sec": "Section C — Network Layer: IP, ICMP, ARP & Routing Protocols", "diff": "medium", "stype": "original_practice", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer", "Practice Set"]}, {"q": ["BGP, the protocol that routes between autonomous systems on the Internet, uses:", "BGP — जो Internet पर autonomous systems के बीच routing करता है — प्रयोग करता है:"], "opts": [["TCP port 179", "TCP port 179"], ["IP protocol 89", "IP protocol 89"], ["UDP port 520", "UDP port 520"], ["TCP port 23", "TCP port 23"]], "ans": 0, "exp": ["BGP = TCP port 179 — reliable transport chahiye Internet-scale routing ke liye. | Nukta: 89 = OSPF; 520 = RIP; 23 = Telnet.", "BGP = TCP port 179 — Internet-scale routing के लिए reliable transport। | 89 = OSPF; 520 = RIP; 23 = Telnet।"], "src": "Practice — original (textbook-based)", "sec": "Section C — Network Layer: IP, ICMP, ARP & Routing Protocols", "diff": "medium", "stype": "original_practice", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer", "Practice Set"]}, {"q": ["The RIP routing protocol uses which transport protocol and port number?", "RIP routing protocol कौन-सा transport protocol और port number प्रयोग करता है?"], "opts": [["UDP port 520", "UDP port 520"], ["TCP port 520", "TCP port 520"], ["UDP port 161", "UDP port 161"], ["TCP port 89", "TCP port 89"]], "ans": 0, "exp": ["RIP = UDP 520 (chhote periodic updates, reliable transport ki zaroorat nahi). | Nukta: 161 = SNMP; TCP 89 kuch nahi (OSPF TCP par nahi chalta).", "RIP = UDP 520 (छोटे periodic updates)। | 161 = SNMP; TCP 89 — कुछ नहीं (OSPF TCP पर नहीं चलता)।"], "src": "Practice — original (textbook-based)", "sec": "Section C — Network Layer: IP, ICMP, ARP & Routing Protocols", "diff": "medium", "stype": "original_practice", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer", "Practice Set"]}, {"q": ["A router receives a datagram whose TTL becomes 0 after it decrements the field. The router will:", "एक router को datagram मिला जिसका TTL घटाने पर 0 हो गया। router क्या करेगा?"], "opts": [["Discard the datagram and send an ICMP Time Exceeded message to the source", "Datagram नष्ट करके source को ICMP Time Exceeded भेजेगा"], ["Forward it with TTL 0", "TTL 0 के साथ आगे भेजेगा"], ["Send it back to the previous router", "पिछले router को वापस भेजेगा"], ["Change TTL to 255 and forward", "TTL 255 करके आगे भेजेगा"]], "ans": 0, "exp": ["TTL = routing loops rokne ke liye; har hop par −1, zero hote hi packet gira kar ICMP Time Exceeded (type 11) source ko jaata hai — traceroute isi par chalta hai. Pattern: GATE + RPSC Programmer dono ka favourite. | Nukta: traceroute = TTL 1, 2, 3... karke Time Exceeded ke source routers ka pata.", "TTL हर hop पर −1; 0 होते ही packet गिरकर ICMP Time Exceeded (type 11) जाता है — traceroute इसी पर। Pattern: GATE + RPSC Programmer। | traceroute = TTL 1,2,3... से Time Exceeded से routers का पता।"], "src": "Practice — original (RPSC Programmer/ACP/DD exam-pattern, textbook-based)", "sec": "Section C — Network Layer: IP, ICMP, ARP & Routing Protocols", "diff": "hard", "stype": "original_practice", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RPSC Programmer", "Practice Set"]}, {"q": ["In OSPF, on a multiaccess network the Designated Router (DR) is the router with:", "OSPF में multiaccess network पर Designated Router (DR) होता है वह router जिसके पास:"], "opts": [["The highest OSPF interface priority (tie → highest router ID)", "सबसे अधिक OSPF interface priority (बराबरी पर → सबसे बड़ा router ID)"], ["The lowest IP address", "सबसे कम IP address"], ["The highest bandwidth link", "सबसे अधिक bandwidth वाला link"], ["The oldest OSPF process", "सबसे पुराना OSPF process"]], "ans": 0, "exp": ["DR election: pehle highest priority (default 1; 0 = kabhi DR nahi), tie par highest router ID. DR adjacency kam karke flooding reduce karta hai. Pattern: CCNA + RPSC ACP/Programmer level. | Nukta: OSPF mein 2-way state ke baad DR/BDR election hoti hai.", "DR election: सर्वोच्च priority (default 1), बराबरी पर सबसे बड़ा router ID। Pattern: CCNA + RPSC ACP/Programmer। | OSPF में 2-way के बाद DR/BDR election।"], "src": "Practice — original (RPSC Programmer/ACP/DD exam-pattern, textbook-based)", "sec": "Section C — Network Layer: IP, ICMP, ARP & Routing Protocols", "diff": "hard", "stype": "original_practice", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RPSC Programmer", "Practice Set"]}, {"q": ["Two OSPF routers are stuck in the EXSTART/EXCHANGE neighbour state. The most likely cause is:", "दो OSPF routers EXSTART/EXCHANGE neighbour state में अटके हैं। सबसे संभावित कारण है:"], "opts": [["An MTU mismatch on the connecting interfaces", "जोड़ने वाले interfaces पर MTU का अंतर"], ["Different OSPF process IDs", "भिन्न OSPF process IDs"], ["Different hostnames", "भिन्न hostnames"], ["Different IOS/OS versions", "भिन्न IOS/OS versions"]], "ans": 0, "exp": ["Database description (DBD) exchange mein MTU mismatch ke routers EXSTART/EXCHANGE se aage nahi badhte. Process IDs locally significant hote hain — match karne ki zaroorat nahi. Pattern: CCNA troubleshooting + RPSC ACP. | Nukta: OSPF states: Down → Init → 2-Way → ExStart → Exchange → Loading → Full.", "MTU mismatch से routers EXSTART/EXCHANGE में अटकते हैं। Process IDs locally significant होते हैं। Pattern: CCNA + RPSC ACP। | OSPF states: Down → Init → 2-Way → ExStart → Exchange → Loading → Full।"], "src": "Practice — original (RPSC Programmer/ACP/DD exam-pattern, textbook-based)", "sec": "Section C — Network Layer: IP, ICMP, ARP & Routing Protocols", "diff": "hard", "stype": "original_practice", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RPSC Programmer", "Practice Set"]}, {"q": ["The administrative distance of a static route, an EIGRP route and an OSPF route are respectively:", "Static route, EIGRP route और OSPF route का administrative distance क्रमशः होता है:"], "opts": [["1, 90 and 110", "1, 90 और 110"], ["0, 110 and 120", "0, 110 और 120"], ["1, 110 and 120", "1, 110 और 120"], ["10, 90 and 100", "10, 90 और 100"]], "ans": 0, "exp": ["AD = route ki 'trustworthiness' (kam = zyada trusted): connected 0, static 1, EIGRP 90, OSPF 110, RIP 120. Pattern: CCNA 200-301 + RPSC ACP/DD. | Nukta: AD aur metric alag cheez hain — AD protocols ko compare karti hai.", "AD (कम = अधिक trusted): connected 0, static 1, EIGRP 90, OSPF 110, RIP 120। Pattern: CCNA + RPSC ACP/DD। | AD और metric अलग हैं — AD protocols की तुलना करती है।"], "src": "Practice — original (RPSC Programmer/ACP/DD exam-pattern, textbook-based)", "sec": "Section C — Network Layer: IP, ICMP, ARP & Routing Protocols", "diff": "hard", "stype": "original_practice", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RPSC Programmer", "Practice Set"]}, {"q": ["If the Protocol field of an IPv4 header is 17, the transport-layer protocol carried in the datagram is:", "यदि IPv4 header का Protocol field 17 हो, तो datagram में लिया गया transport-layer protocol है:"], "opts": [["UDP", "UDP"], ["TCP", "TCP"], ["ICMP", "ICMP"], ["IGMP", "IGMP"]], "ans": 0, "exp": ["Protocol numbers: 1 = ICMP, 2 = IGMP, 6 = TCP, 17 = UDP, 89 = OSPF. Ye field fragmentation ke saath-saath next-header ki pehchaan deta hai. | Nukta: 6 TCP, 17 UDP — dono sabse zyada puche jaate hain.", "Protocol numbers: 1=ICMP, 2=IGMP, 6=TCP, 17=UDP, 89=OSPF। | 6 TCP, 17 UDP — सबसे अधिक पूछे जाते हैं।"], "src": "Practice — original (textbook-based)", "sec": "Section C — Network Layer: IP, ICMP, ARP & Routing Protocols", "diff": "medium", "stype": "original_practice", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer", "Practice Set"]}, {"q": ["In IPv4 fragmentation, the LAST fragment has the More Fragments (MF) flag set to:", "IPv4 fragmentation में, अंतिम fragment का More Fragments (MF) flag होता है:"], "opts": [["0", "0"], ["1", "1"], ["Its fragment offset value", "उसका fragment offset मान"], ["The same as the first fragment", "पहले fragment के बराबर"]], "ans": 0, "exp": ["MF = 1 matlab 'aur fragments aane hain'; aakhri fragment par MF = 0. Har fragment ka offset alag hota hai. | Nukta: Dono fields (MF flag + offset) milkar reassembly karte hain.", "MF=1 = 'और fragments आने हैं'; अंतिम पर MF=0। | MF flag + offset मिलकर reassembly करते हैं।"], "src": "Practice — original (textbook-based)", "sec": "Section C — Network Layer: IP, ICMP, ARP & Routing Protocols", "diff": "hard", "stype": "original_practice", "style": "concept", "tags": ["GATE CS", "UGC-NET 087", "RPSC Programmer", "RPSC ACP/DD", "Practice Set"]}, {"q": ["The Fragment Offset field in the IPv4 header is used to:", "IPv4 header का Fragment Offset field प्रयोग होता है:"], "opts": [["Place the fragment at its correct position in the original datagram during reassembly", "Reassembly के दौरान fragment को मूल datagram में सही स्थान पर रखने के लिए"], ["Count the total number of fragments", "कुल fragments गिनने के लिए"], ["Encrypt fragment payloads", "Fragment payloads encrypt करने के लिए"], ["Set the fragment's lifetime", "Fragment का जीवन-काल तय करने के लिए"]], "ans": 0, "exp": ["Offset (8-byte units mein) batata hai fragment original datagram mein kahan baitha hai — destination sirf offset se hi sahi order bana sakta hai. | Nukta: Offset = position; MF = aur aane hain ya nahi.", "Offset (8-byte units में) बताता है fragment का स्थान — इसी से सही क्रम बनता है। | Offset = स्थान; MF = और आने हैं या नहीं।"], "src": "Practice — original (textbook-based)", "sec": "Section C — Network Layer: IP, ICMP, ARP & Routing Protocols", "diff": "hard", "stype": "original_practice", "style": "concept", "tags": ["GATE CS", "UGC-NET 087", "RPSC Programmer", "RPSC ACP/DD", "Practice Set"]}, {"q": ["The data field of an IPv4 datagram can carry:", "IPv4 datagram का data field ले जा सकता है:"], "opts": [["TCP segment, UDP datagram, or ICMP message — all of these", "TCP segment, UDP datagram, या ICMP message — ये सब"], ["Only TCP segments", "सिर्फ TCP segments"], ["Only UDP datagrams", "सिर्फ UDP datagrams"], ["Only application data", "सिर्फ application data"]], "ans": 0, "exp": ["IP ka payload kuch bhi ho sakta hai jo Protocol field bataye — TCP/UDP segments, ICMP/IGMP messages, tunnels mein doosra IP packet bhi. | Nukta: Protocol field = 6/17/1/2/41... isi se pata chalta hai kya andar hai.", "IP का payload कुछ भी हो सकता है — TCP/UDP, ICMP/IGMP, या tunnel में दूसरा IP packet। | Protocol field से पता चलता है क्या अंदर है।"], "src": "Practice — original (textbook-based)", "sec": "Section C — Network Layer: IP, ICMP, ARP & Routing Protocols", "diff": "hard", "stype": "original_practice", "style": "concept", "tags": ["GATE CS", "UGC-NET 087", "RPSC Programmer", "RPSC ACP/DD", "Practice Set"]}, {"q": ["RSVP (Resource ReSerVation Protocol) is used by hosts to:", "RSVP (Resource ReSerVation Protocol) का उपयोग hosts करते हैं:"], "opts": [["Request reservation of network resources (bandwidth) along a path for QoS flows", "QoS flows के लिए रास्ते में network संसाधन (bandwidth) आरक्षित करने के अनुरोध हेतु"], ["Assign IP addresses automatically", "स्वतः IP addresses देने के लिए"], ["Resolve domain names", "Domain names हल करने के लिए"], ["Exchange routing tables between routers", "Routers के बीच routing tables बाँटने के लिए"]], "ans": 0, "exp": ["RSVP = signalling protocol jo routers se kehta hai ki flow ke liye resources reserve karo (IntServ/QoS). IP assignment = DHCP; routing = OSPF/BGP; names = DNS. | Nukta: RSVP 'reservation' ka protocol hai — circuit-switching jaisi guarantee nahi, bas soft-state reservations.", "RSVP = routers से संसाधन आरक्षित करने का संकेत (QoS)। IP=DHCP; routing=OSPF/BGP; names=DNS। | RSVP = soft-state reservations; पूरी guarantee नहीं।"], "src": "Practice — original (textbook-based)", "sec": "Section C — Network Layer: IP, ICMP, ARP & Routing Protocols", "diff": "medium", "stype": "original_practice", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer", "Practice Set"]}, {"q": ["Which of the following is a connectionless transport service?", "निम्न में से कौन-सी connectionless transport service है?"], "opts": [["TCP", "TCP"], ["ARP", "ARP"], ["UDP", "UDP"], ["FTP", "FTP"]], "ans": 2, "exp": ["UDP (User Datagram Protocol) connectionless है — बिना connection बनाए datagrams भेज देता है. TCP connection-oriented है. | Nukta: Transport layer के दो सदस्य: TCP (भरोसेमंद, connection-oriented) और UDP (तेज़, connectionless).", "UDP (User Datagram Protocol) connectionless है — बिना connection बनाए datagrams भेज देता है. TCP connection-oriented है. | Transport layer के दो सदस्य: TCP (भरोसेमंद, connection-oriented) और UDP (तेज़, connectionless)."], "src": "BCI_SCI Subject Test-7.pdf + Oliveboard SSC CGL bank", "sec": "Section D — Transport Layer: TCP/UDP, Ports & Sockets", "diff": "medium", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["SSC Computer Awareness"]}, {"q": ["How many bits are used for port addressing at the transport layer?", "Transport layer पर port addressing के लिए कितने bits उपयोग होते हैं?"], "opts": [["8", "8"], ["10", "10"], ["16", "16"], ["32", "32"]], "ans": 2, "exp": ["Port numbers are 16 bits — that is why ports range from 0 to 65535. | Nukta: Addresses का स्तर: Data link = 48-bit MAC; Network = 32-bit IP; Transport = 16-bit port.", "Port numbers 16 bits के होते हैं — इसीलिए 0 से 65535 तक ports बनते हैं. | Addresses का स्तर: Data link = 48-bit MAC; Network = 32-bit IP; Transport = 16-bit port."], "src": "BCI_SCI Subject Test-7.pdf", "sec": "Section D — Transport Layer: TCP/UDP, Ports & Sockets", "diff": "hard", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["GATE CS", "UGC-NET 087", "RPSC Programmer", "RPSC ACP/DD"]}, {"q": ["What is a socket in networking?", "Networking में socket क्या है?"], "opts": [["IP address + MAC address", "IP address + MAC address"], ["IP address + Port number", "IP address + Port number"], ["MAC address + Port number", "MAC address + Port number"], ["IP address + DNS name", "IP address + DNS name"]], "ans": 1, "exp": ["Socket = IP address + Port number — यही combination एक connection का endpoint पहचानती है. | Nukta: Socket pair = (Source IP:Port, Destination IP:Port) — TCP connection इसी से बनती है.", "Socket = IP address + Port number — यही combination एक connection का endpoint पहचानती है. | Socket pair = (Source IP:Port, Destination IP:Port) — TCP connection इसी से बनती है."], "src": "CN Topic Test 6.pdf", "sec": "Section D — Transport Layer: TCP/UDP, Ports & Sockets", "diff": "medium", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["What term is used for an endpoint in an inter-process communication across a network?", "Network पर inter-process communication में endpoint के लिए कौन-सा term उपयोग होता है?"], "opts": [["Port", "Port"], ["Machine", "Machine"], ["Socket", "Socket"], ["Pipe", "Pipe"]], "ans": 2, "exp": ["IPC endpoint socket कहलाता है — दो processes इन्हीं sockets के ज़रिए बात करती हैं. | Nukta: Port = address का हिस्सा; Socket = पूरा endpoint (IP+Port).", "IPC endpoint socket कहलाता है — दो processes इन्हीं sockets के ज़रिए बात करती हैं. | Port = address का हिस्सा; Socket = पूरा endpoint (IP+Port)."], "src": "CN Topic Test-02.pdf", "sec": "Section D — Transport Layer: TCP/UDP, Ports & Sockets", "diff": "medium", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["A client opens a TCP connection to a web server on port 80 using source port 49152. What is the complete socket pair?", "एक client source port 49152 से port 80 वाले web server को TCP connection खोलता है. पूरा socket pair क्या होगा?"], "opts": [["192.168.1.10:49152 ↔ 172.16.0.5:80", "192.168.1.10:49152 ↔ 172.16.0.5:80"], ["192.168.1.10:80 ↔ 172.16.0.5:49152", "192.168.1.10:80 ↔ 172.16.0.5:49152"], ["49152 ↔ 80", "49152 ↔ 80"], ["80 ↔ 49152", "80 ↔ 49152"]], "ans": 0, "exp": ["Socket pair में पहले जोड़े में client का IP:Port और दूसरे में server का IP:Port होता है — client:49152 ↔ server:80. | Nukta: पहचान: client का port ephemeral (बड़ा number), server का port well-known (80).", "Socket pair में पहले जोड़े में client का IP:Port और दूसरे में server का IP:Port होता है — client:49152 ↔ server:80. | पहचान: client का port ephemeral (बड़ा number), server का port well-known (80)."], "src": "BCI Subject Test-8.pdf", "sec": "Section D — Transport Layer: TCP/UDP, Ports & Sockets", "diff": "easy", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["SSC Computer Awareness", "RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "JNV TAT"]}, {"q": ["What is the purpose of the SYN flag in TCP?", "TCP में SYN flag का उद्देश्य क्या है?"], "opts": [["To end a session", "To end a session"], ["To initiate (open) a connection", "To initiate (open) a connection"], ["To reset a connection", "To reset a connection"], ["For data transmission", "For data transmission"]], "ans": 1, "exp": ["TCP connection शुरू करने के लिए तीन-तरफ़ा handshake (SYN → SYN-ACK → ACK) होता है — SYN यही connection request है. | Nukta: Remember the flags: SYN = start; FIN = end; RST = abort; ACK = confirmation.", "TCP connection शुरू करने के लिए तीन-तरफ़ा handshake (SYN → SYN-ACK → ACK) होता है — SYN यही connection request है. | Flags याद रखो: SYN = शुरुआत; FIN = अंत; RST = रद्द; ACK = पुष्टि."], "src": "CN Topic Test 6.pdf", "sec": "Section D — Transport Layer: TCP/UDP, Ports & Sockets", "diff": "medium", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["The three-way handshake mechanism in TCP aims to:", "TCP का three-way handshake mechanism किस उद्देश्य से होता है?"], "opts": [["Secure the communication", "Secure the communication"], ["Send bits from one device to another", "Send bits from one device to another"], ["Perform error detection and correction", "Perform error detection and correction"], ["Establish a connection and synchronize sequence numbers", "Establish a connection and synchronize sequence numbers"]], "ans": 3, "exp": ["The three-way handshake sets up the connection at both ends and exchanges sequence numbers (synchronisation). | Nukta: RPSC official key (d). SYN, SYN-ACK, ACK — तीन ही संदेश.", "तीन-तरफ़ा handshake से दोनों तरफ़ connection बनती है और sequence numbers का आदान-प्रदान होता है (सिंक्रोनाइज़ेशन). | RPSC official key (d). SYN, SYN-ACK, ACK — तीन ही संदेश."], "src": "RPSC Programmer 2024 Paper-1 (with official key)", "sec": "Section D — Transport Layer: TCP/UDP, Ports & Sockets", "diff": "hard", "stype": "verified_official_pyq", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["In which scenario will TCP's three-way handshake fail?", "किस स्थिति में TCP का three-way handshake विफल होगा?"], "opts": [["Firewall blocks the SYN-ACK", "Firewall blocks the SYN-ACK"], ["High latency", "High latency"], ["ACK is slightly delayed", "ACK is slightly delayed"], ["Server is busy", "Server is busy"]], "ans": 0, "exp": ["If a firewall blocks the SYN-ACK, the handshake never completes and no connection is made. | Nukta: The immediate cause of a failed handshake: the messages are not getting through (firewall/filter).", "यदि firewall SYN-ACK को रोक दे तो handshake पूरा नहीं होता और connection नहीं बनती. | Handshake टूटने का सीधा कारण: संदेशों का न पहुँचना (firewall/filter)."], "src": "CN Topic Test 5.pdf", "sec": "Section D — Transport Layer: TCP/UDP, Ports & Sockets", "diff": "medium", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "scenario", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["In TCP, which state follows the SYN-SENT state in the normal case?", "TCP में सामान्य स्थिति में SYN-SENT के बाद कौन-सी state आती है?"], "opts": [["SYN-RECEIVED", "SYN-RECEIVED"], ["LISTEN", "LISTEN"], ["ESTABLISHED", "ESTABLISHED"], ["CLOSED", "CLOSED"]], "ans": 2, "exp": ["SYN भेजने (SYN-SENT) के बाद जब SYN-ACK आता है और ACK भेजा जाता है, connection ESTABLISHED हो जाती है. | Nukta: सामान्य क्रम: CLOSED → SYN-SENT → ESTABLISHED. (Simultaneous open में SYN-RECEIVED बीच में आती है.)", "SYN भेजने (SYN-SENT) के बाद जब SYN-ACK आता है और ACK भेजा जाता है, connection ESTABLISHED हो जाती है. | सामान्य क्रम: CLOSED → SYN-SENT → ESTABLISHED. (Simultaneous open में SYN-RECEIVED बीच में आती है.)"], "src": "CN Topic Test 6.pdf", "sec": "Section D — Transport Layer: TCP/UDP, Ports & Sockets", "diff": "medium", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "scenario", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["Which one of the following attacks exploits TCP's three-way handshake?", "निम्न में से कौन-सा attack TCP के three-way handshake का फ़ायदा उठाती है?"], "opts": [["SYN Flood", "SYN Flood"], ["DNS Spoofing", "DNS Spoofing"], ["Man in the Middle", "Man in the Middle"], ["ARP Poisoning", "ARP Poisoning"]], "ans": 0, "exp": ["SYN Flood में attacker ढेरों SYN भेजकर half-open connections बना देता है और server के resources खत्म हो जाते हैं. | Nukta: Handshake पर हमला = SYN flood; sequence पर हमला = session hijacking.", "SYN Flood में attacker ढेरों SYN भेजकर half-open connections बना देता है और server के resources खत्म हो जाते हैं. | Handshake पर हमला = SYN flood; sequence पर हमला = session hijacking."], "src": "CN Topic Test 5.pdf", "sec": "Section D — Transport Layer: TCP/UDP, Ports & Sockets", "diff": "medium", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["What type of attack is prevented by using random initial sequence numbers in TCP?", "TCP में random initial sequence numbers उपयोग करने से किस प्रकार की attack रुकती है?"], "opts": [["Smurf attack", "Smurf attack"], ["SYN Flooding", "SYN Flooding"], ["TCP session hijacking", "TCP session hijacking"], ["Ping of Death", "Ping of Death"]], "ans": 2, "exp": ["Random sequence numbers से attacker अगला sequence number अनुमान नहीं लगा पाता और session hijacking (और spoofed ACK) रुकती है. | Nukta: Predictable sequence numbers = session hijacking का दरवाज़ा.", "Random sequence numbers से attacker अगला sequence number अनुमान नहीं लगा पाता और session hijacking (और spoofed ACK) रुकती है. | Predictable sequence numbers = session hijacking का दरवाज़ा."], "src": "CN Topic Test 5.pdf", "sec": "Section D — Transport Layer: TCP/UDP, Ports & Sockets", "diff": "hard", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["GATE CS", "UGC-NET 087", "RPSC Programmer", "RPSC ACP/DD"]}, {"q": ["Which field in the TCP header is used for flow control?", "TCP header में flow control के लिए कौन-सा field उपयोग होता है?"], "opts": [["Window Size", "Window Size"], ["Sequence Number", "Sequence Number"], ["Acknowledgment Number", "Acknowledgment Number"], ["Checksum", "Checksum"]], "ans": 0, "exp": ["Window Size field बताता है कि receiver कितने bytes और ले सकता है — यही TCP का flow control है. | Nukta: TCP के दो घरेलू नियंत्रण: Window (flow control) और cwnd (congestion control).", "Window Size field बताता है कि receiver कितने bytes और ले सकता है — यही TCP का flow control है. | TCP के दो घरेलू नियंत्रण: Window (flow control) और cwnd (congestion control)."], "src": "CN Topic Test 6.pdf", "sec": "Section D — Transport Layer: TCP/UDP, Ports & Sockets", "diff": "hard", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["GATE CS", "UGC-NET 087", "RPSC Programmer", "RPSC ACP/DD"]}, {"q": ["Which TCP header field ensures that data arrives in order?", "TCP header का कौन-सा field सुनिश्चित करता है कि data क्रम में पहुँचे?"], "opts": [["Checksum", "Checksum"], ["Flags", "Flags"], ["Sequence Number", "Sequence Number"], ["Port Number", "Port Number"]], "ans": 2, "exp": ["Every byte has a sequence number — the receiver uses them to put the bytes back in the correct order. | Nukta: UDP has no sequence numbers — that is why it gives no ordering guarantee.", "हर byte का sequence number होता है — receiver इन्हीं से bytes को सही क्रम में जोड़ता है. | UDP में sequence नहीं होता — इसीलिए वहाँ क्रम की guarantee नहीं."], "src": "CN Topic Test 5.pdf", "sec": "Section D — Transport Layer: TCP/UDP, Ports & Sockets", "diff": "hard", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["GATE CS", "UGC-NET 087", "RPSC Programmer", "RPSC ACP/DD"]}, {"q": ["Which field in the TCP header ensures data integrity?", "TCP header का कौन-सा field data integrity सुनिश्चित करता है?"], "opts": [["Urgent Pointer", "Urgent Pointer"], ["Sequence Number", "Sequence Number"], ["Checksum", "Checksum"], ["Acknowledgment Number", "Acknowledgment Number"]], "ans": 2, "exp": ["The checksum sums the whole segment to verify integrity — if anything changed on the way, the packet is dropped. | Nukta: Integrity = Checksum (TCP/UDP/IP); reliability = ACK + retransmission.", "Checksum पूरे segment का जोड़ निकालकर integrity जाँचता है — रास्ते में कुछ बदला तो packet छोड़ दिया जाता है. | Integrity = Checksum (TCP/UDP/IP); reliability = ACK + retransmission."], "src": "CN Topic Test 5.pdf", "sec": "Section D — Transport Layer: TCP/UDP, Ports & Sockets", "diff": "hard", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["GATE CS", "UGC-NET 087", "RPSC Programmer", "RPSC ACP/DD"]}, {"q": ["Which of the following is NOT a property of TCP?", "निम्न में से कौन-सा TCP का गुण नहीं है?"], "opts": [["Reliable", "Reliable"], ["Ordered delivery", "Ordered delivery"], ["Connection-oriented", "Connection-oriented"], ["Broadcast", "Broadcast"]], "ans": 3, "exp": ["TCP point-to-point reliable protocol है — broadcast/multicast नहीं करता. Broadcast का काम UDP/UDP-lite जैसे protocols करते हैं. | Nukta: TCP = reliable + ordered + connection-oriented; बाकी सब (broadcast) UDP की तरफ़ जाता है.", "TCP point-to-point reliable protocol है — broadcast/multicast नहीं करता. Broadcast का काम UDP/UDP-lite जैसे protocols करते हैं. | TCP = reliable + ordered + connection-oriented; बाकी सब (broadcast) UDP की तरफ़ जाता है."], "src": "CN Topic Test 5.pdf", "sec": "Section D — Transport Layer: TCP/UDP, Ports & Sockets", "diff": "hard", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["GATE CS", "UGC-NET 087", "RPSC Programmer", "RPSC ACP/DD"]}, {"q": ["Which of the following provides reliable, connection-oriented communication?", "निम्न में से कौन-सा भरोसेमंद, connection-oriented communication देता है?"], "opts": [["TCP", "TCP"], ["IP", "IP"], ["UDP", "UDP"], ["All of the above", "All of the above"]], "ans": 0, "exp": ["TCP ही reliable और connection-oriented transport protocol है. | Nukta: याद रखो: TCP = phone call (connection + guarantee); UDP = postcard (fast, no promise).", "TCP ही reliable और connection-oriented transport protocol है. | याद रखो: TCP = phone call (connection + guarantee); UDP = postcard (fast, no promise)."], "src": "MQuestions DCN bank + Oliveboard SSC CGL bank", "sec": "Section D — Transport Layer: TCP/UDP, Ports & Sockets", "diff": "hard", "stype": "claimed_pyq_unverified", "style": "concept", "tags": ["SSC Computer Awareness"]}, {"q": ["TCP initially uses which congestion control technique when a connection starts?", "Connection शुरू होने पर TCP शुरू में कौन-सी congestion control technique उपयोग करता है?"], "opts": [["Congestion avoidance", "Congestion avoidance"], ["Fast recovery", "Fast recovery"], ["Slow start", "Slow start"], ["Leaky bucket", "Leaky bucket"]], "ans": 2, "exp": ["At connection start TCP uses Slow Start — the congestion window is kept small and increased gradually. | Nukta: TCP क्रम: Slow start → Congestion avoidance; loss पर → Fast recovery.", "Connection शुरू में TCP Slow start उपयोग करता है — congestion window छोटा रखकर धीरे-धीरे बढ़ाया जाता है. | TCP क्रम: Slow start → Congestion avoidance; loss पर → Fast recovery."], "src": "CN Topic Test 6.pdf", "sec": "Section D — Transport Layer: TCP/UDP, Ports & Sockets", "diff": "medium", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["What is the purpose of TCP's congestion window (cwnd)?", "TCP के congestion window (cwnd) का उद्देश्य क्या है?"], "opts": [["Track unacknowledged packets", "Track unacknowledged packets"], ["Control the sending rate to avoid network congestion", "Control the sending rate to avoid network congestion"], ["Handle encryption", "Handle encryption"], ["Prioritize packets", "Prioritize packets"]], "ans": 1, "exp": ["cwnd controls the sender's speed according to network capacity — it shrinks on loss and grows when all is well. | Nukta: TCP की effective window = min(rwnd, cwnd) — flow और congestion दोनों का संतुलन.", "cwnd network की क्षमता के हिसाब से sender की गति नियंत्रित करता है — ज़्यादा loss हो तो घटता है, सब ठीक हो तो बढ़ता है. | TCP की effective window = min(rwnd, cwnd) — flow और congestion दोनों का संतुलन."], "src": "CN Topic Test 5.pdf", "sec": "Section D — Transport Layer: TCP/UDP, Ports & Sockets", "diff": "medium", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["What kind of delay does TCP's window size help handle on a long, high-bandwidth path?", "लंबी, high-bandwidth path पर TCP का window size किस प्रकार की देर संभालने में मदद करता है?"], "opts": [["Transmission delay", "Transmission delay"], ["Queuing delay", "Queuing delay"], ["Propagation delay", "Propagation delay"], ["Bandwidth-delay product", "Bandwidth-delay product"]], "ans": 3, "exp": ["The bigger the Bandwidth × Delay (BDP), the bigger the window must be — only then is the pipe full and propagation delay hidden. | Nukta: Window ≥ BDP हो तो link बेकार नहीं बैठती — यही high-speed long links का सूत्र है.", "Bandwidth × Delay (BDP) जितना बड़ा हो, window उतनी बड़ी चाहिए — तभी पूरी pipe भरी रहती है और propagation delay छिप जाता है. | Window ≥ BDP हो तो link बेकार नहीं बैठती — यही high-speed long links का सूत्र है."], "src": "CN Topic Test 5.pdf", "sec": "Section D — Transport Layer: TCP/UDP, Ports & Sockets", "diff": "medium", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["In which protocol is 'port knocking' used as a security mechanism?", "किस protocol में 'port knocking' security mechanism के रूप में उपयोग होता है?"], "opts": [["TCP", "TCP"], ["UDP", "UDP"], ["SSH", "SSH"], ["IP", "IP"]], "ans": 2, "exp": ["In port knocking, connection attempts hit closed ports in a fixed sequence, after which the firewall opens a service like SSH — often used with SSH servers. | Nukta: Port knocking = 'secret door knock' — पहचान होते ही असली दरवाज़ा (SSH) खुलता है.", "Port knocking में बंद ports पर तय क्रम से connection attempts किए जाते हैं, जिसके बाद firewall SSH जैसी सेवा खोल देता है — यह अक्सर SSH servers के साथ उपयोग होता है. | Port knocking = 'secret door knock' — पहचान होते ही असली दरवाज़ा (SSH) खुलता है."], "src": "CN Topic Test 6.pdf", "sec": "Section D — Transport Layer: TCP/UDP, Ports & Sockets", "diff": "medium", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["Which of the following supports QoS (Quality of Service) through label switching?", "निम्न में से कौन-सा label switching के ज़रिए QoS (Quality of Service) देता है?"], "opts": [["TCP", "TCP"], ["UDP", "UDP"], ["MPLS", "MPLS"], ["ARP", "ARP"]], "ans": 2, "exp": ["MPLS divides traffic into classes using labels and provides QoS — routers don't repeatedly inspect the full IP header. | Nukta: MPLS = fast path + QoS classes; DiffServ/IntServ भी QoS के तरीके हैं.", "MPLS labels के ज़रिए traffic को classes में बाँटकर QoS देता है — routers बार-बार पूरा IP header नहीं देखते. | MPLS = fast path + QoS classes; DiffServ/IntServ भी QoS के तरीके हैं."], "src": "CN Topic Test 6.pdf", "sec": "Section D — Transport Layer: TCP/UDP, Ports & Sockets", "diff": "medium", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["Virtual circuits are associated with which type of service?", "Virtual circuits किस प्रकार की service से जुड़े हैं?"], "opts": [["Connectionless service", "Connectionless service"], ["Error-free service", "Error-free service"], ["Segmentation", "Segmentation"], ["Connection-oriented service", "Connection-oriented service"]], "ans": 3, "exp": ["Virtual circuit (जैसे X.25, ATM, Frame Relay) में पहले रास्ता तय होता है, फिर सारे packets उसी रास्ते से जाते हैं — यह connection-oriented model है. | Nukta: Virtual circuit = पहले connection, फिर data (connection-oriented); Datagram = हर packet अपने-आप (connectionless).", "Virtual circuit (जैसे X.25, ATM, Frame Relay) में पहले रास्ता तय होता है, फिर सारे packets उसी रास्ते से जाते हैं — यह connection-oriented model है. | Virtual circuit = पहले connection, फिर data (connection-oriented); Datagram = हर packet अपने-आप (connectionless)."], "src": "CN Topic Test-02.pdf", "sec": "Section D — Transport Layer: TCP/UDP, Ports & Sockets", "diff": "medium", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["Transport layer multiplexing allows:", "Transport layer multiplexing की अनुमति देता है:"], "opts": [["Multiple hosts to share one IP", "Multiple hosts to share one IP"], ["Multiple processes to share one network connection", "Multiple processes to share one network connection"], ["Multiple routers to share a routing table", "Multiple routers to share a routing table"], ["Domain name resolution", "Domain name resolution"]], "ans": 1, "exp": ["Transport layer multiplexing/demultiplexing से एक ही IP connection पर कई applications (processes) अपने-अपने ports से चल सकते हैं. | Nukta: Ports ही multiplexing के हथियार हैं — browser 443, mail 25, सब एक साथ.", "Transport layer multiplexing/demultiplexing से एक ही IP connection पर कई applications (processes) अपने-अपने ports से चल सकते हैं. | Ports ही multiplexing के हथियार हैं — browser 443, mail 25, सब एक साथ."], "src": "BCI_SCI Subject Test-7.pdf", "sec": "Section D — Transport Layer: TCP/UDP, Ports & Sockets", "diff": "medium", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["Which protocol must use both TCP and UDP for different operations?", "कौन-सा protocol अलग-अलग कामों के लिए TCP और UDP दोनों उपयोग करता है?"], "opts": [["DNS", "DNS"], ["HTTP", "HTTP"], ["POP3", "POP3"], ["Telnet", "Telnet"]], "ans": 0, "exp": ["DNS queries usually travel on UDP (port 53), but large transfers and zone transfers use TCP — so DNS uses both. | Nukta: DNS = port 53; UDP for small queries, TCP for big/zone transfers.", "DNS queries आमतौर पर UDP (port 53) पर जाती हैं, पर बड़े transfers और zone transfers TCP पर — इसलिए DNS दोनों उपयोग करता है. | DNS = port 53; UDP for small queries, TCP for big/zone transfers."], "src": "BCI Subject Test-8.pdf + CN Topic Test 5.pdf", "sec": "Section D — Transport Layer: TCP/UDP, Ports & Sockets", "diff": "medium", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["Which port is used by a DHCP client when requesting an IP address?", "IP address माँगते समय DHCP client कौन-सा port उपयोग करता है?"], "opts": [["UDP 67", "UDP 67"], ["UDP 68", "UDP 68"], ["TCP 68", "TCP 68"], ["TCP 67", "TCP 67"]], "ans": 1, "exp": ["DHCP client UDP port 68 से request भेजता है और server UDP port 67 से जवाब देता है. | Nukta: जोड़ी याद रखो: server 67, client 68 — DHCP (UDP).", "DHCP client UDP port 68 से request भेजता है और server UDP port 67 से जवाब देता है. | जोड़ी याद रखो: server 67, client 68 — DHCP (UDP)."], "src": "BCI Subject Test-8.pdf", "sec": "Section D — Transport Layer: TCP/UDP, Ports & Sockets", "diff": "easy", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["SSC Computer Awareness", "RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "JNV TAT"]}, {"q": ["Which transport-layer protocol is used to support electronic mail delivery between machines?", "Machines के बीच electronic mail delivery के लिए कौन-सा transport-layer protocol उपयोग होता है?"], "opts": [["SNMP", "SNMP"], ["IP", "IP"], ["SMTP", "SMTP"], ["TCP", "TCP"]], "ans": 3, "exp": ["Mail की सेवा SMTP (application) देती है, पर वह अपना data TCP के ज़रिए ही भेजती है — इसलिए transport layer पर TCP. | Nukta: प्रश्न 'transport-layer protocol' पूछ रहा है — SMTP application layer का है, TCP transport का.", "Mail की सेवा SMTP (application) देती है, पर वह अपना data TCP के ज़रिए ही भेजता है — इसलिए transport layer पर TCP. | प्रश्न 'transport-layer protocol' पूछ रहा है — SMTP application layer का है, TCP transport का."], "src": "CN Topic Test-03.pdf", "sec": "Section D — Transport Layer: TCP/UDP, Ports & Sockets", "diff": "medium", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["Which of the following statements about TCP/IP is INCORRECT?", "TCP/IP के बारे में निम्न में से कौन-सा कथन गलत है?"], "opts": [["TCP/IP has high latency", "TCP/IP has high latency"], ["Data packets sent over TCP/IP are private", "Data packets sent over TCP/IP are private"], ["TCP is used by Secure Shell (SSH)", "TCP is used by Secure Shell (SSH)"], ["TCP/IP uses checksums to check errors", "TCP/IP uses checksums to check errors"]], "ans": 1, "exp": ["Packets on TCP/IP are not private by nature — they can be seen on the way; for confidentiality you must add TLS/SSH/VPN. | Nukta: DSSSB का official key (b). याद रखो: Internet = open postcard, ताला (encryption) खुद लगाओ.", "TCP/IP पर भेजे packets स्वाभाविक रूप से private नहीं होते — रास्ते में देखे जा सकते हैं; गोपनीयता के लिए TLS/SSH/VPN लगाना पड़ता है. | DSSSB का official key (b). याद रखो: Internet = open postcard, ताला (encryption) खुद लगाओ."], "src": "DSSSB TGT CS (via Testbook solved)", "sec": "Section D — Transport Layer: TCP/UDP, Ports & Sockets", "diff": "hard", "stype": "claimed_pyq_unverified", "style": "statement", "tags": ["DSSSB"]}, {"q": ["Why are port numbers included in the TCP header of a segment?", "Segment के TCP header में port numbers क्यों रखे जाते हैं?"], "opts": [["To indicate the correct router interface for forwarding", "To indicate the correct router interface for forwarding"], ["To identify which switch ports should receive the frame", "To identify which switch ports should receive the frame"], ["To determine which Layer 3 protocol encapsulates the data", "To determine which Layer 3 protocol encapsulates the data"], ["To enable a receiving host to forward the data to the appropriate application", "To enable a receiving host to forward the data to the appropriate application"]], "ans": 3, "exp": ["Port numbers बताते हैं कि receiver पर data किस application (process) को देना है — इसीलिए एक ही connection पर कई apps चल सकते हैं. | Nukta: RPSC 2011 official key (4). यही transport-layer multiplexing है.", "Port numbers बताते हैं कि receiver पर data किस application (process) को देना है — इसीलिए एक ही connection पर कई apps चल सकते हैं. | RPSC 2011 official key (4). यही transport-layer multiplexing है."], "src": "RPSC Programmer 2011 Paper-1 (via pyqp.in)", "sec": "Section D — Transport Layer: TCP/UDP, Ports & Sockets", "diff": "hard", "stype": "claimed_pyq_unverified", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["Which one of the following fields of an IP header is NOT modified by a typical IP router?", "IP header का कौन-सा field एक सामान्य IP router द्वारा संशोधित नहीं किया जाता?"], "opts": [["Checksum", "Checksum"], ["Source address", "Source address"], ["Time to Live (TTL)", "Time to Live (TTL)"], ["Length", "Length"]], "ans": 1, "exp": ["Router TTL ko ghatata hai, checksum phir se calculate karta hai, fragmentation par length badal sakti hai — par source address hamesha wahi rehta hai (GATE 2015 key). | Nukta: Checksum aur TTL router ke haath badalte hain; length fragmentation se badal sakti hai.", "Router TTL घटाता है, checksum नया, fragmentation पर length बदल सकती है — source address वही रहता है (GATE 2015 key). | Checksum/TTL बदलते हैं; length fragmentation से बदल सकती है।"], "src": "GATE CS 2015 Set-1", "sec": "Section D — Transport Layer: TCP/UDP, Ports & Sockets", "diff": "hard", "stype": "claimed_pyq_unverified", "style": "concept", "tags": ["GATE CS"]}, {"q": ["Which of the following fields of an IP header is/are ALWAYS modified by any router before it forwards the IP packet?", "IP packet forward करने से पहले हर router IP header के कौन-से fields हमेशा बदलता है?"], "opts": [["TTL only", "केवल TTL"], ["Checksum only", "केवल Checksum"], ["TTL and header checksum", "TTL और header checksum"], ["Source address and TTL", "Source address और TTL"]], "ans": 2, "exp": ["Har hop par TTL ghat-ta hai (1 kam) aur uske kaaran header checksum bhi har router ko phir se lagana hi padta hai — dono always modified hote hain. | Nukta: Checksum ko optional samajhna galti hai — TTL badalne par checksum invalid ho jata hai.", "हर hop पर TTL घटता है और उससे header checksum भी हर router को नया करना पड़ता है — दोनों हमेशा बदलते हैं। | Checksum optional नहीं — TTL बदलते ही checksum अमान्य हो जाता है।"], "src": "GATE CS 2024 Set-2", "sec": "Section D — Transport Layer: TCP/UDP, Ports & Sockets", "diff": "hard", "stype": "claimed_pyq_unverified", "style": "concept", "tags": ["GATE CS"]}, {"q": ["Which of the following fields is/are modified in the IP header of a packet going out of a Network Address Translation (NAT) device from an internal network to an external network?", "NAT device से internal network से external network की तरफ़ जाते packet के IP header में कौन-से fields बदले जाते हैं?"], "opts": [["Source IP address only", "केवल Source IP address"], ["Destination IP address only", "केवल Destination IP address"], ["Source IP address and header checksum", "Source IP address और header checksum"], ["TTL and destination address", "TTL और destination address"]], "ans": 2, "exp": ["NAT bahar jaate packet ka private source IP apne public IP se badalta hai (aur mapping banaata hai); us badalav se header checksum bhi recompute hota hai. | Nukta: Destination address wahi rehta hai (jana to server ko hi hai); TTL alag cheez hai.", "NAT बाहर जाते packet का private source IP अपने public IP से बदलता है; उससे header checksum भी नया होता है। | Destination वही रहता है; TTL अलग चीज़ है।"], "src": "GATE CS 2024 Set-1", "sec": "Section D — Transport Layer: TCP/UDP, Ports & Sockets", "diff": "hard", "stype": "claimed_pyq_unverified", "style": "concept", "tags": ["GATE CS"]}, {"q": ["Consider sending an IP datagram of size 1420 bytes (including a 20-byte IP header) over a path of two links with a router between them. The first link has MTU 542 bytes and the second link has MTU 360 bytes. The number of fragments delivered at the receiver is ______.", "1420 bytes का IP datagram (20-byte header सहित) दो links के रास्ते भेजा जा रहा है, बीच में एक router है। पहले link का MTU 542 bytes और दूसरे का 360 bytes है। Receiver पर कुल कितने fragments पहुँचेंगे?"], "opts": [["4", "4"], ["5", "5"], ["6", "6"], ["8", "8"]], "ans": 2, "exp": ["1400 bytes data पहले link पर 3 fragments (522, 522, 356); दूसरे link (340 bytes data per fragment) पर हर बड़ा fragment 2 में टूटता है — कुल 2+2+2 = 6 fragments. | Nukta: 5/8 fragmentation ko sirf ek baar maante hain; 4 total data ko 360 se seedha bhaag dete hain.", "1400 bytes data पहले link पर 3 (522, 522, 356); दूसरे link पर (340 data) हर बड़ा 2 में — कुल 6. | 5/8 fragmentation एक ही बार मानते हैं; 4 सीधे 360 से भाग देते हैं।"], "src": "GATE CS 2024 Set-1", "sec": "Section D — Transport Layer: TCP/UDP, Ports & Sockets", "diff": "hard", "stype": "claimed_pyq_unverified", "style": "numerical", "tags": ["GATE CS"]}, {"q": ["In an IPv4 datagram, the M bit is 0, the value of HLEN is 10, the value of total length is 400 and the fragment offset value is 300. The position of the datagram, and the sequence numbers of the first and the last bytes of the payload, respectively, are:", "एक IPv4 datagram में M bit = 0, HLEN = 10, total length = 400 और fragment offset = 300 है। इस datagram की स्थिति तथा payload के पहले और आख़िरी bytes के sequence numbers क्रमशः हैं:"], "opts": [["Last fragment, 2400 and 2759", "Last fragment, 2400 और 2759"], ["First fragment, 2400 and 2759", "First fragment, 2400 और 2759"], ["Last fragment, 300 and 659", "Last fragment, 300 और 659"], ["Last fragment, 2400 and 2779", "Last fragment, 2400 और 2779"]], "ans": 0, "exp": ["HLEN 10 → header 40 bytes; offset 300 × 8 = 2400 se payload shuru; payload 400−40 = 360 bytes → aakhri byte 2400+359 = 2759; M = 0 matlab yeh aakhri fragment hai. | Nukta: Offset ko byte nahi 8-byte units mein count karna zaroori hai; 2779 header ko do baar jod deta hai.", "HLEN 10 → header 40 bytes; offset 300×8 = 2400 से payload; 400−40 = 360 bytes → आख़िरी byte 2759; M = 0 = यही अंतिम fragment है। | Offset 8-byte units में होता है; 2779 header दो बार जोड़ता है।"], "src": "GATE CS 2013", "sec": "Section D — Transport Layer: TCP/UDP, Ports & Sockets", "diff": "hard", "stype": "claimed_pyq_unverified", "style": "numerical", "tags": ["GATE CS"]}, {"q": ["Consider the following three statements about link state and distance vector routing protocols for a large network with 500 nodes and 4000 links:\nS1: The computational overhead in link state protocols is higher than in distance vector protocols.\nS2: A distance vector protocol (with split horizon) avoids persistent routing loops, but a link state protocol does not.\nS3: After a topology change, a link state protocol converges faster than a distance vector protocol.\nWhich one is correct?", "500 nodes और 4000 links वाले बड़े network के लिए link state व distance vector routing protocols के बारे में तीन कथन:\nS1: Link state में computational overhead distance vector से अधिक है।\nS2: Distance vector (split horizon सहित) persistent loops से बचता है, पर link state नहीं।\nS3: Topology बदलने पर link state, distance vector से तेज़ converge करता है।\nकौन-सा सही है?"], "opts": [["S1, S2 and S3 are all true", "S1, S2, S3 तीनों सही"], ["S1, S2 and S3 are all false", "S1, S2, S3 तीनों गलत"], ["S1 and S2 are true, S3 is false", "S1 और S2 सही, S3 गलत"], ["S1 and S3 are true, S2 is false", "S1 और S3 सही, S2 गलत"]], "ans": 3, "exp": ["S1 sahi: har node poora SPF/Dijkstra chalata hai. S3 sahi: flooding se LS topology turant jaanti hai. S2 galat: link state shortest-path tree loop-free hota hai — loops ki samasya distance vector ki hai. | Nukta: S2 ulta hai — split horizon count-to-infinity se poora bachata bhi nahi.", "S1 सही: हर node पूरा SPF चलाता है। S3 सही: flooding से तेज़ converge। S2 गलत: link state tree loop-free होता है। | S2 उल्टा — split horizon count-to-infinity से पूरा बचाता भी नहीं।"], "src": "GATE CS 2014 Set-1", "sec": "Section D — Transport Layer: TCP/UDP, Ports & Sockets", "diff": "hard", "stype": "claimed_pyq_unverified", "style": "statement", "tags": ["GATE CS"]}, {"q": ["Which one of the following is TRUE about the interior gateway routing protocols RIP (Routing Information Protocol) and OSPF (Open Shortest Path First)?", "Interior gateway routing protocols RIP (Routing Information Protocol) और OSPF (Open Shortest Path First) के बारे में कौन-सा कथन सही है?"], "opts": [["RIP uses distance vector routing and OSPF uses link state routing", "RIP distance vector और OSPF link state routing प्रयोग करता है"], ["OSPF uses distance vector routing and RIP uses link state routing", "OSPF distance vector और RIP link state routing प्रयोग करता है"], ["Both RIP and OSPF use link state routing", "दोनों link state routing प्रयोग करते हैं"], ["Both RIP and OSPF use distance vector routing", "दोनों distance vector routing प्रयोग करते हैं"]], "ans": 0, "exp": ["RIP neighbours ko apni distance vector bhejta hai (distance vector family); OSPF poora topology map flood kar Dijkstra chalata hai (link state) — yeh standard classification hai. | Nukta: Dono ko ek hi category mein daalna common galti hai.", "RIP अपनी distance vector भेजता है; OSPF topology flood कर Dijkstra चलाता है (link state) — यही मानक भेद है। | दोनों को एक श्रेणी में डालना आम गलती।"], "src": "GATE CS 2014 Set-2", "sec": "Section D — Transport Layer: TCP/UDP, Ports & Sockets", "diff": "hard", "stype": "claimed_pyq_unverified", "style": "concept", "tags": ["GATE CS"]}, {"q": ["Consider the following statements about the functionality of an IP based router:\nI. A router does not modify the IP packets during forwarding.\nII. It is not necessary for a router to implement any routing protocol.\nIII. A router should reassemble IP fragments if the MTU of the outgoing link is larger than the size of the incoming IP packet.\nWhich of the above statement(s) is/are TRUE?", "IP आधारित router की कार्यप्रणाली के बारे में विचार:\nI. Router forwarding के दौरान IP packets को संशोधित नहीं करता।\nII. Router के लिए कोई routing protocol लागू करना आवश्यक नहीं है।\nIII. यदि outgoing link का MTU आने वाले packet से बड़ा हो तो router को fragments जोड़ने चाहिए।\nइनमें कौन-सा कथन सही है?"], "opts": [["I only", "केवल I"], ["II only", "केवल II"], ["I and III only", "केवल I और III"], ["None of the above", "कोई नहीं"]], "ans": 1, "exp": ["I galat: router TTL ghatata hai aur checksum badalta hai. II sahi: static routes se bhi router chal sakta hai. III galat: reassembly sirf destination host karta hai, router kabhi nahi. | Nukta: Fragmentation ke baad re-fragmentation ka kaam router ka hai, jodna nahi.", "I गलत: router TTL/checksum बदलता है। II सही: static routes से भी चलेगा। III गलत: reassembly सिर्फ़ destination करता है। | Router re-fragment कर सकता है, जोड़ता नहीं।"], "src": "GATE CS 2020", "sec": "Section D — Transport Layer: TCP/UDP, Ports & Sockets", "diff": "hard", "stype": "claimed_pyq_unverified", "style": "statement", "tags": ["GATE CS"]}, {"q": ["Host A (on TCP/IPv4 network A) sends an IP datagram D to host B (on TCP/IPv4 network B) with no transmission error. When D reaches B, which of the following IP header field(s) may be different from that of the original datagram D?\nI. TTL    II. Checksum    III. Fragment Offset", "Host A ने (TCP/IPv4 network A से) बिना किसी त्रुटि के IP datagram D, host B को भेजा। D के B पर पहुँचने पर निम्न में से कौन-से IP header fields मूल datagram से भिन्न हो सकते हैं?\nI. TTL    II. Checksum    III. Fragment Offset"], "opts": [["I only", "केवल I"], ["II and III only", "केवल II और III"], ["I and II only", "केवल I और II"], ["I, II and III", "I, II और III तीनों"]], "ans": 3, "exp": ["Har router par TTL ghat-ta hai aur checksum naya hota hai; raaste mein fragmentation hui to fragment offset bhi lag sakta hai — teeno badal sakte hain (GATE 2014 key). | Nukta: Offset ko 'sirf fragmentation ke time' samajh kar chhod dena galti hai — puchha hai 'ho sakta hai'.", "हर router पर TTL घटता है, checksum नया; रास्ते में fragmentation हुई तो offset भी — तीनों बदल सकते हैं। | Offset को छोड़ देना गलती — पूछा है 'हो सकता है'।"], "src": "GATE CS 2014 Set-3", "sec": "Section D — Transport Layer: TCP/UDP, Ports & Sockets", "diff": "hard", "stype": "claimed_pyq_unverified", "style": "concept", "tags": ["GATE CS"]}, {"q": ["The size of the TCP header (without options) is:", "TCP header का size (options बिना) होता है:"], "opts": [["8 bytes", "8 bytes"], ["20 bytes", "20 bytes"], ["24 bytes", "24 bytes"], ["60 bytes", "60 bytes"]], "ans": 1, "exp": ["TCP header = 20 bytes; UDP = 8 bytes; IPv4 = 20 bytes. | Nukta: 8 bytes UDP ka.", "TCP = 20 bytes; UDP = 8; IPv4 = 20। | 8 bytes UDP का।"], "src": "Practice — original (textbook-based)", "sec": "Section D — Transport Layer: TCP/UDP, Ports & Sockets", "diff": "hard", "stype": "original_practice", "style": "concept", "tags": ["GATE CS", "UGC-NET 087", "RPSC Programmer", "RPSC ACP/DD", "Practice Set"]}, {"q": ["During TCP connection termination, after receiving FIN the receiver sends:", "TCP connection समाप्ति में FIN पाने के बाद receiver भेजता है:"], "opts": [["SYN", "SYN"], ["ACK", "ACK"], ["RST", "RST"], ["PSH", "PSH"]], "ans": 1, "exp": ["FIN ka jawab ACK; phir apna FIN bhejta hai. | Nukta: SYN establishment ke liye.", "FIN का जवाब ACK। | SYN establishment के लिए।"], "src": "Practice — original (textbook-based)", "sec": "Section D — Transport Layer: TCP/UDP, Ports & Sockets", "diff": "medium", "stype": "original_practice", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer", "Practice Set"]}, {"q": ["The size of the UDP header is:", "UDP header का size होता है:"], "opts": [["8 bytes", "8 bytes"], ["12 bytes", "12 bytes"], ["20 bytes", "20 bytes"], ["64 bytes", "64 bytes"]], "ans": 0, "exp": ["UDP header = 8 bytes (ports + length + checksum). | Nukta: TCP 20 bytes.", "UDP = 8 bytes। | TCP 20 bytes।"], "src": "Practice — original (textbook-based)", "sec": "Section D — Transport Layer: TCP/UDP, Ports & Sockets", "diff": "hard", "stype": "original_practice", "style": "concept", "tags": ["GATE CS", "UGC-NET 087", "RPSC Programmer", "RPSC ACP/DD", "Practice Set"]}, {"q": ["In TCP slow start, the congestion window size:", "TCP slow start में congestion window size:"], "opts": [["Increases by 1 MSS per RTT", "प्रति RTT 1 MSS बढ़ती है"], ["Doubles approximately every RTT", "हर RTT में लगभग दोगुनी होती है"], ["Remains constant", "स्थिर रहती है"], ["Decreases every ACK", "हर ACK पर घटती है"]], "ans": 1, "exp": ["Slow start exponential growth per RTT. | Nukta: +1 MSS per RTT congestion avoidance hai.", "Slow start per RTT चरम-वृद्धि। | +1 MSS per RTT = congestion avoidance।"], "src": "Practice — original (textbook-based)", "sec": "Section D — Transport Layer: TCP/UDP, Ports & Sockets", "diff": "medium", "stype": "original_practice", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer", "Practice Set"]}, {"q": ["TCP is called a byte-stream protocol because:", "TCP को byte-stream protocol कहते हैं क्योंकि:"], "opts": [["It sends only bytes", "यह सिर्फ़ bytes भेजता है"], ["It does not preserve message boundaries", "यह message सीमाएँ नहीं रखता"], ["It cannot send text", "यह text नहीं भेज सकता"], ["It works only with bytes files", "यह सिर्फ़ byte files के साथ चलता है"]], "ans": 1, "exp": ["TCP data ko byte stream samajhta hai — message boundaries preserve nahi karta. | Nukta: UDP message-oriented hai.", "TCP byte stream — सीमाएँ नहीं रखता। | UDP message-oriented है।"], "src": "Practice — original (textbook-based)", "sec": "Section D — Transport Layer: TCP/UDP, Ports & Sockets", "diff": "hard", "stype": "original_practice", "style": "concept", "tags": ["GATE CS", "UGC-NET 087", "RPSC Programmer", "RPSC ACP/DD", "Practice Set"]}, {"q": ["Which of the following uses UDP?", "निम्न में से कौन UDP प्रयोग करता है?"], "opts": [["FTP", "FTP"], ["SMTP", "SMTP"], ["DNS query", "DNS query"], ["SSH", "SSH"]], "ans": 2, "exp": ["DNS queries UDP (53) par; FTP/SMTP/SSH TCP. | Nukta: Tez chhoti queries UDP.", "DNS query UDP; बाक़ी TCP। | छोटी queries UDP।"], "src": "Practice — original (textbook-based)", "sec": "Section D — Transport Layer: TCP/UDP, Ports & Sockets", "diff": "medium", "stype": "original_practice", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer", "Practice Set"]}, {"q": ["After a TCP connection is closed, the side performing the active close waits in the TIME-WAIT state for:", "TCP connection बंद होने के बाद active close करने वाला पक्ष TIME-WAIT state में रहता है:"], "opts": [["2 × MSL (Maximum Segment Lifetime)", "2 × MSL (Maximum Segment Lifetime)"], ["1 × RTT", "1 × RTT"], ["3 × RTT", "3 × RTT"], ["One congestion timeout", "एक congestion timeout"]], "ans": 0, "exp": ["2×MSL wait se purane connection ke delayed duplicate segments khatam ho jaate hain, naya connection safe rehta hai (RFC 793). | Nukta: MSL = maximum time ek segment Internet mein reh sakta hai.", "2×MSL के इंतज़ार से पुराने duplicates खत्म होते हैं (RFC 793)। | MSL = segment का अधिकतम जीवनकाल।"], "src": "Practice — original (textbook-based)", "sec": "Section D — Transport Layer: TCP/UDP, Ports & Sockets", "diff": "medium", "stype": "original_practice", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer", "Practice Set"]}, {"q": ["The 8-byte UDP header consists of which fields?", "8-byte UDP header में कौन-से fields होते हैं?"], "opts": [["Source port, destination port, length, checksum", "Source port, destination port, length, checksum"], ["Source port, destination port, sequence number, ack number", "Source port, destination port, sequence number, ack number"], ["Source port, destination port, window, checksum", "Source port, destination port, window, checksum"], ["Ports, length, checksum, urgent pointer", "Ports, length, checksum, urgent pointer"]], "ans": 0, "exp": ["UDP header = 4 fields × 2 bytes = 8 bytes; sequence/ack/window — sab TCP ke fields hain. | Nukta: UDP ka mantra: 'chhota header, koi guarantee nahi'.", "UDP header = 4 fields × 2 bytes = 8; sequence/ack/window — TCP के fields। | UDP: 'छोटा header, कोई guarantee नहीं'।"], "src": "Practice — original (textbook-based)", "sec": "Section D — Transport Layer: TCP/UDP, Ports & Sockets", "diff": "hard", "stype": "original_practice", "style": "numerical", "tags": ["GATE CS", "UGC-NET 087", "RPSC Programmer", "RPSC ACP/DD", "Practice Set"]}, {"q": ["TCP provides a byte-stream service. This means that:", "TCP byte-stream service देता है — इसका अर्थ है कि:"], "opts": [["Message boundaries are NOT preserved — a record may be split across segments or two records merged into one", "Message boundaries नहीं बनतीं — एक record कई segments में बँट सकता है या दो records एक में मिल सकते हैं"], ["Each send() call arrives as one segment", "हर send() एक segment के रूप में पहुँचता है"], ["Bytes arrive in fixed 512-byte blocks", "Bytes 512-byte के तय blocks में आते हैं"], ["The receiver delivers bytes in the order they were received, even if reordered on the way", "Receiver bytes उसी क्रम में देता है जिसमें प्राप्त हुए, भले रास्ते में बदले हों"]], "ans": 0, "exp": ["TCP sirf reliable ordered BYTE stream deta hai — application ki record boundaries TCP ki zimmedari nahi (isliye application khud length/delimiter bhejti hai). Pattern: RPSC Programmer/ACP/DD + GATE. | Nukta: UDP message-oriented hai — wahan ek datagram = ek message.", "TCP सिर्फ विश्वसनीय क्रमबद्ध BYTE stream देता है — record boundaries की ज़िम्मेदारी नहीं। Pattern: RPSC Programmer/ACP/DD। | UDP message-oriented है — एक datagram = एक message।"], "src": "Practice — original (RPSC Programmer/ACP/DD exam-pattern, textbook-based)", "sec": "Section D — Transport Layer: TCP/UDP, Ports & Sockets", "diff": "hard", "stype": "original_practice", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RPSC Programmer", "Practice Set"]}, {"q": ["The TCP Maximum Segment Size (MSS) is typically the path MTU minus ______ bytes of headers:", "TCP Maximum Segment Size (MSS) सामान्यतः path MTU में से ______ bytes के headers घटाने पर मिलती है:"], "opts": [["40", "40"], ["20", "20"], ["64", "64"], ["54", "54"]], "ans": 0, "exp": ["MSS = MTU − (20-byte IP header + 20-byte TCP header) = MTU − 40. Ethernet par 1500 − 40 = 1460 bytes. Pattern: RPSC Programmer/ACP/DD + GATE. | Nukta: MSS sirf TCP data ka size hai — headers alag.", "MSS = MTU − (20 IP + 20 TCP) = MTU − 40; Ethernet पर 1460 bytes। Pattern: RPSC Programmer/ACP/DD। | MSS सिर्फ TCP data का size है।"], "src": "Practice — original (RPSC Programmer/ACP/DD exam-pattern, textbook-based)", "sec": "Section D — Transport Layer: TCP/UDP, Ports & Sockets", "diff": "hard", "stype": "original_practice", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RPSC Programmer", "Practice Set"]}, {"q": ["The functionalities of the presentation layer include:", "Presentation layer के कार्यों में शामिल हैं:"], "opts": [["Data compression", "Data compression"], ["Data encryption", "Data encryption"], ["Data description (translation)", "Data description (translation)"], ["All of the mentioned", "All of the mentioned"]], "ans": 3, "exp": ["Presentation layer data का रूप संभालती है — compression, encryption और translation (जैसे ASCII/EBCDIC) — तीनों. | Nukta: Presentation = data का मेकअप (रूप, रंग, सुरक्षा); Application = सेवाएँ.", "Presentation layer data का रूप संभालती है — compression, encryption और translation (जैसे ASCII/EBCDIC) — तीनों. | Presentation = data का मेकअप (रूप, रंग, सुरक्षा); Application = सेवाएँ."], "src": "CN Topic Test-02.pdf", "sec": "Section E — Session, Presentation & Application Layer", "diff": "hard", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["GATE CS", "UGC-NET 087", "RPSC Programmer", "RPSC ACP/DD"]}, {"q": ["The structure or format of data is called:", "Data का structure या format कहलाता है:"], "opts": [["Syntax", "Syntax"], ["Struct", "Struct"], ["Semantic", "Semantic"], ["None of the above", "None of the above"]], "ans": 0, "exp": ["Forouzan के अनुसार: Syntax = data का structure/format; Semantics = sections का अर्थ. | Nukta: Rule: Syntax = how it looks; Semantics = what it means. Both must be agreed for communication.", "Forouzan के अनुसार: Syntax = data का structure/format; Semantics = sections का अर्थ. | नियम: Syntax = कैसा दिखे; Semantics = क्या अर्थ हो. Communication में दोनों तय होने चाहिए."], "src": "Unit Test-4 Solution.pdf (OCR), p14", "sec": "Section E — Session, Presentation & Application Layer", "diff": "medium", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["Which protocol layer uses protocols such as WWW, HTTP, FTP, SMTP and e-mail?", "कौन-सी protocol layer WWW, HTTP, FTP, SMTP और e-mail जैसे protocols उपयोग करती है?"], "opts": [["Application layer", "Application layer"], ["Transport layer", "Transport layer"], ["Internet layer", "Internet layer"], ["Hardware layer", "Hardware layer"]], "ans": 0, "exp": ["HTTP, FTP, SMTP, e-mail आदि Application layer के protocols हैं — यही उपयोगकर्ता की सेवाएँ देती हैं. | Nukta: याद रखो: Layer 7 = सेवाएँ (HTTP/FTP/SMTP/DNS); Layer 4 = TCP/UDP; Layer 3 = IP.", "HTTP, FTP, SMTP, e-mail आदि Application layer के protocols हैं — यही उपयोगकर्ता की सेवाएँ देती हैं. | याद रखो: Layer 7 = सेवाएँ (HTTP/FTP/SMTP/DNS); Layer 4 = TCP/UDP; Layer 3 = IP."], "src": "CN Topic Test-02.pdf + CN Topic Test-01.pdf", "sec": "Section E — Session, Presentation & Application Layer", "diff": "medium", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["Which layer protocols provide user and application programme support such as passwords, resource sharing and file transfer?", "किस layer के protocols उपयोगकर्ता और application programme को passwords, resource sharing और file transfer जैसी सहायता देते हैं?"], "opts": [["Layer 2 protocols", "Layer 2 protocols"], ["Layer 5 protocols", "Layer 5 protocols"], ["Layer 7 protocols", "Layer 7 protocols"], ["Layer 10 protocols", "Layer 10 protocols"]], "ans": 2, "exp": ["Layer 7 (Application) ही users की सेवाएँ संभालती है — passwords, file transfer, resource sharing आदि. | Nukta: OSI has exactly 7 layers — there can be no 'Layer 10'.", "Layer 7 (Application) ही users की सेवाएँ संभालती है — passwords, file transfer, resource sharing आदि. | OSI में 7 layers ही हैं — 'Layer 10' तो हो ही नहीं सकती."], "src": "CN Topic Test-02.pdf", "sec": "Section E — Session, Presentation & Application Layer", "diff": "medium", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["Which of the following protocols is primarily used for secure web browsing?", "निम्न में से कौन-सा protocol मुख्य रूप से सुरक्षित web browsing के लिए उपयोग होता है?"], "opts": [["FTP", "FTP"], ["HTTP", "HTTP"], ["HTTPS", "HTTPS"], ["SMTP", "SMTP"]], "ans": 2, "exp": ["HTTPS = HTTP + TLS/SSL encryption — browser और server के बीच सारा व्यवहार encrypted रहता है. | Nukta: HTTPS का port 443; HTTP का 80. ताला (lock) वाली site = HTTPS.", "HTTPS = HTTP + TLS/SSL encryption — browser और server के बीच सारा व्यवहार encrypted रहता है. | HTTPS का port 443; HTTP का 80. ताला (lock) वाली site = HTTPS."], "src": "CN Topic Test-01.pdf", "sec": "Section E — Session, Presentation & Application Layer", "diff": "medium", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["A server receives a packet with destination port 443. This implies:", "एक server को destination port 443 वाला packet मिलता है. इसका अर्थ है:"], "opts": [["HTTP request", "HTTP request"], ["HTTPS traffic", "HTTPS traffic"], ["FTP command", "FTP command"], ["Email traffic", "Email traffic"]], "ans": 1, "exp": ["Port 443 HTTPS (सुरक्षित web) का standard port है. | Nukta: Ports: 80=HTTP, 443=HTTPS, 21/20=FTP, 22=SSH, 23=Telnet, 25=SMTP, 53=DNS, 67/68=DHCP.", "Port 443 HTTPS (सुरक्षित web) का standard port है. | Ports: 80=HTTP, 443=HTTPS, 21/20=FTP, 22=SSH, 23=Telnet, 25=SMTP, 53=DNS, 67/68=DHCP."], "src": "BCI Subject Test-8.pdf", "sec": "Section E — Session, Presentation & Application Layer", "diff": "easy", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["SSC Computer Awareness", "RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "JNV TAT"]}, {"q": ["Which protocol is generally used to encrypt data between a web browser and a web server?", "Web browser और web server के बीच data encrypt करने के लिए आमतौर पर कौन-सा protocol उपयोग होता है?"], "opts": [["SSL/TLS", "SSL/TLS"], ["Digital Signature", "Digital Signature"], ["IPSec", "IPSec"], ["TCP", "TCP"]], "ans": 0, "exp": ["SSL/TLS (आजकल TLS) browser-server के बीच encryption देता है — इसी पर HTTPS चलता है. | Nukta: HTTPS = HTTP over SSL/TLS. IPSec network-level VPN के लिए होता है.", "SSL/TLS (आजकल TLS) browser-server के बीच encryption देता है — इसी पर HTTPS चलता है. | HTTPS = HTTP over SSL/TLS. IPSec network-level VPN के लिए होता है."], "src": "CN Topic Test-01.pdf", "sec": "Section E — Session, Presentation & Application Layer", "diff": "medium", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["Which of the following protocols is NOT secure?", "निम्न में से कौन-सा protocol सुरक्षित नहीं है?"], "opts": [["HTTPS", "HTTPS"], ["FTP", "FTP"], ["SSH", "SSH"], ["SFTP", "SFTP"]], "ans": 1, "exp": ["Plain FTP sends data and passwords in cleartext — that is insecure. Its secure forms are SFTP/FTPS. | Nukta: असुरक्षित की सूची: HTTP, FTP, Telnet, SMTP (बिना TLS). सुरक्षित: HTTPS, SFTP, SSH, SMTPS.", "सादा FTP data और passwords सादे रूप में भेजता है — यह असुरक्षित है. इसके सुरक्षित रूप SFTP/FTPS हैं. | असुरक्षित की सूची: HTTP, FTP, Telnet, SMTP (बिना TLS). सुरक्षित: HTTPS, SFTP, SSH, SMTPS."], "src": "CN Topic Test 6.pdf", "sec": "Section E — Session, Presentation & Application Layer", "diff": "hard", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["GATE CS", "UGC-NET 087", "RPSC Programmer", "RPSC ACP/DD"]}, {"q": ["Which protocol is used for secure shell (remote) login?", "Secure shell (remote) login के लिए कौन-सा protocol उपयोग होता है?"], "opts": [["FTP", "FTP"], ["SSH", "SSH"], ["Telnet", "Telnet"], ["SNMP", "SNMP"]], "ans": 1, "exp": ["SSH (Secure Shell) encrypted remote login देता है — Telnet का सुरक्षित विकल्प. | Nukta: SSH = port 22 (encrypted); Telnet = port 23 (सादा, असुरक्षित).", "SSH (Secure Shell) encrypted remote login देता है — Telnet का सुरक्षित विकल्प. | SSH = port 22 (encrypted); Telnet = port 23 (सादा, असुरक्षित)."], "src": "CN Topic Test 6.pdf + Medium 30 CN MCQ bank", "sec": "Section E — Session, Presentation & Application Layer", "diff": "medium", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["A firewall blocks all ports except 22. What service remains accessible?", "एक firewall port 22 को छोड़कर सब बंद कर देता है. कौन-सी सेवा अभी भी खुली है?"], "opts": [["FTP", "FTP"], ["SSH", "SSH"], ["HTTPS", "HTTPS"], ["SMTP", "SMTP"]], "ans": 1, "exp": ["Port 22 belongs to SSH — so the SSH service is the one that will be open. | Nukta: Identify the port, identify the service — that is the trick of this question.", "Port 22 SSH का है — इसलिए SSH सेवा ही खुली रहेगी. | Port पहचानो, सेवा पहचानो — यही इस प्रश्न का खेल है."], "src": "BCI Subject Test-8.pdf", "sec": "Section E — Session, Presentation & Application Layer", "diff": "medium", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["Which port does Telnet use by default?", "Telnet डिफ़ॉल्ट रूप से कौन-सा port उपयोग करता है?"], "opts": [["21", "21"], ["23", "23"], ["22", "22"], ["25", "25"]], "ans": 1, "exp": ["Telnet का default port 23 है (सादा remote login). | Nukta: याद रखो: 22 = SSH, 23 = Telnet, 25 = SMTP, 21 = FTP.", "Telnet का default port 23 है (सादा remote login). | याद रखो: 22 = SSH, 23 = Telnet, 25 = SMTP, 21 = FTP."], "src": "CN Topic Test 6.pdf", "sec": "Section E — Session, Presentation & Application Layer", "diff": "medium", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["Which of the following uses port number 25?", "निम्न में से कौन-सा port number 25 उपयोग करता है?"], "opts": [["FTP", "FTP"], ["HTTP", "HTTP"], ["SMTP", "SMTP"], ["Telnet", "Telnet"]], "ans": 2, "exp": ["SMTP (Simple Mail Transfer Protocol) mail भेजने के लिए port 25 उपयोग करता है. | Nukta: Mail ports: 25 (SMTP), 110 (POP3), 143 (IMAP).", "SMTP (Simple Mail Transfer Protocol) mail भेजने के लिए port 25 उपयोग करता है. | Mail ports: 25 (SMTP), 110 (POP3), 143 (IMAP)."], "src": "CN Topic Test 6.pdf", "sec": "Section E — Session, Presentation & Application Layer", "diff": "medium", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["Which of the following protocols is used for transferring email messages from one machine to another?", "निम्न में से कौन-सा protocol email संदेशों को एक machine से दूसरी में भेजने के लिए उपयोग होता है?"], "opts": [["SNMP", "SNMP"], ["FTP", "FTP"], ["TELNET", "TELNET"], ["SMTP", "SMTP"]], "ans": 3, "exp": ["SMTP ही mail servers के बीच संदेश भेजने का मानक protocol है (port 25). | Nukta: RPSC official key (d). भेजना = SMTP; लेना = POP3/IMAP.", "SMTP ही mail servers के बीच संदेश भेजने का मानक protocol है (port 25). | RPSC official key (d). भेजना = SMTP; लेना = POP3/IMAP."], "src": "RPSC Programmer 2024 Paper-1 (with official key)", "sec": "Section E — Session, Presentation & Application Layer", "diff": "hard", "stype": "verified_official_pyq", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["Which protocol uses different ports for control and data connections?", "कौन-सा protocol control और data connections के लिए अलग-अलग ports उपयोग करता है?"], "opts": [["FTP", "FTP"], ["HTTP", "HTTP"], ["DNS", "DNS"], ["Telnet", "Telnet"]], "ans": 0, "exp": ["FTP दो connections रखता है — control के लिए port 21 और data के लिए port 20. | Nukta: FTP = double connection (control + data); HTTP/SMTP/DNS में ऐसा नहीं.", "FTP दो connections रखता है — control के लिए port 21 और data के लिए port 20. | FTP = double connection (control + data); HTTP/SMTP/DNS में ऐसा नहीं."], "src": "BCI_SCI Subject Test-7.pdf", "sec": "Section E — Session, Presentation & Application Layer", "diff": "medium", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["Which protocol is used for file transfer over a network?", "Network पर file transfer के लिए कौन-सा protocol उपयोग होता है?"], "opts": [["FTP", "FTP"], ["HTTP", "HTTP"], ["DNS", "DNS"], ["ARP", "ARP"]], "ans": 0, "exp": ["FTP (File Transfer Protocol) files भेजने-लाने का मानक protocol है. | Nukta: HTTP से भी files मिलती हैं, पर 'file transfer' का नाम protocol FTP है.", "FTP (File Transfer Protocol) files भेजने-लाने का मानक protocol है. | HTTP से भी files मिलती हैं, पर 'file transfer' का नाम protocol FTP है."], "src": "CN Topic Test 6.pdf + Medium 30 CN MCQ bank", "sec": "Section E — Session, Presentation & Application Layer", "diff": "medium", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["In one of the pairs below, both protocols can use multiple TCP connections between the same client and the same server. Which pair is it?", "नीचे दिए जोड़ों में से किसमें दोनों protocols एक ही client और server के बीच कई TCP connections उपयोग कर सकते हैं?"], "opts": [["HTTP, FTP", "HTTP, FTP"], ["HTTP, TELNET", "HTTP, TELNET"], ["FTP, SMTP", "FTP, SMTP"], ["HTTP, SMTP", "HTTP, SMTP"]], "ans": 0, "exp": ["HTTP non-persistent connections में हर object के लिए अलग connection खोल सकता है; FTP में control के अलावा हर transfer की अलग data connection होती है. | Nukta: दोनों 'multi-connection' protocols हैं — यही जोड़ी पूछी गई है.", "HTTP non-persistent connections में हर object के लिए अलग connection खोल सकता है; FTP में control के अलावा हर transfer की अलग data connection होती है. | दोनों 'multi-connection' protocols हैं — यही जोड़ी पूछी गई है."], "src": "CN Topic Test-02.pdf", "sec": "Section E — Session, Presentation & Application Layer", "diff": "hard", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["GATE CS", "UGC-NET 087", "RPSC Programmer", "RPSC ACP/DD"]}, {"q": ["Identify the true statements: (1) HTTP may use different TCP connections for different objects of a webpage if non-persistent connections are used (2) FTP uses two TCP connections, one for data and another for control (3) TELNET and FTP can only use TWO connections at a time", "सही कथन पहचानें: (1) non-persistent connections में HTTP webpage के अलग-अलग objects के लिए अलग TCP connections उपयोग कर सकता है (2) FTP दो TCP connections उपयोग करता है, एक data के लिए और दूसरा control के लिए (3) TELNET और FTP एक समय में केवल TWO connections ही उपयोग कर सकते हैं"], "opts": [["(1) only", "(1) only"], ["(1) and (2)", "(1) and (2)"], ["(2) and (3)", "(2) and (3)"], ["(1), (2) and (3)", "(1), (2) and (3)"]], "ans": 1, "exp": ["(1) सही — non-persistent HTTP हर object के लिए नया connection; (2) सही — FTP में control + data connections; (3) गलत — ऐसी 'केवल दो' सीमा नहीं. | Nukta: HTTP = multi-connection capable; FTP = दो का जोड़ा; 'only two' का नियम कहीं नहीं.", "(1) सही — non-persistent HTTP हर object के लिए नया connection; (2) सही — FTP में control + data connections; (3) गलत — ऐसी 'केवल दो' सीमा नहीं. | HTTP = multi-connection capable; FTP = दो का जोड़ा; 'only two' का नियम कहीं नहीं."], "src": "CN Topic Test-03.pdf", "sec": "Section E — Session, Presentation & Application Layer", "diff": "hard", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "statement", "tags": ["GATE CS", "UGC-NET 087", "RPSC Programmer", "RPSC ACP/DD"]}, {"q": ["Which application allows a user to access and use remote files without actually transferring them?", "कौन-सा application उपयोगकर्ता को remote files को बिना वास्तव में स्थानांतरित किए उपयोग करने देता है?"], "opts": [["DNS", "DNS"], ["FTP", "FTP"], ["NFS", "NFS"], ["Telnet", "Telnet"]], "ans": 2, "exp": ["NFS (Network File System) remote files को ऐसे दिखाता है जैसे वे आपके अपने computer पर हों — असल transfer नहीं होता. | Nukta: NFS = remote files को local जैसा जोड़ना; FTP = files की असल copy भेजना.", "NFS (Network File System) remote files को ऐसे दिखाता है जैसे वे आपके अपने computer पर हों — असल transfer नहीं होता. | NFS = remote files को local जैसा जोड़ना; FTP = files की असल copy भेजना."], "src": "SSC CGL Internet & Networking (via EduRev bank)", "sec": "Section E — Session, Presentation & Application Layer", "diff": "medium", "stype": "claimed_pyq_unverified", "style": "concept", "tags": ["SSC Computer Awareness"]}, {"q": ["Which of the following is NOT an application layer protocol?", "निम्न में से कौन-सा application layer protocol नहीं है?"], "opts": [["HTTP", "HTTP"], ["IP", "IP"], ["TELNET", "TELNET"], ["FTP", "FTP"]], "ans": 1, "exp": ["IP network layer का protocol है — HTTP, TELNET, FTP सब application layer के हैं. | Nukta: Layer 7 के नाम: HTTP, FTP, SMTP, DNS, Telnet, SNMP, DHCP, TFTP...", "IP network layer का protocol है — HTTP, TELNET, FTP सब application layer के हैं. | Layer 7 के नाम: HTTP, FTP, SMTP, DNS, Telnet, SNMP, DHCP, TFTP..."], "src": "SSC CGL Internet & Networking (via EduRev bank)", "sec": "Section E — Session, Presentation & Application Layer", "diff": "hard", "stype": "claimed_pyq_unverified", "style": "concept", "tags": ["SSC Computer Awareness"]}, {"q": ["Which is the FALSE statement?", "कौन-सा कथन गलत है?"], "opts": [["Telnet is used for remote login", "Telnet is used for remote login"], ["FTP can transfer files between two hosts", "FTP can transfer files between two hosts"], ["TFTP relies on TCP", "TFTP relies on TCP"], ["SMTP is used to send mail messages", "SMTP is used to send mail messages"]], "ans": 2, "exp": ["TFTP (Trivial FTP) runs on UDP, not TCP — this is the statement that is wrong. | Nukta: TFTP = छोटा भाई (UDP, port 69); FTP = बड़ा भाई (TCP, ports 20/21).", "TFTP (Trivial FTP) UDP पर चलता है, TCP पर नहीं — यही कथन गलत है. | TFTP = छोटा भाई (UDP, port 69); FTP = बड़ा भाई (TCP, ports 20/21)."], "src": "SSC CGL Internet & Networking (via EduRev bank)", "sec": "Section E — Session, Presentation & Application Layer", "diff": "hard", "stype": "claimed_pyq_unverified", "style": "statement", "tags": ["SSC Computer Awareness"]}, {"q": ["Which protocol translates domain names to IP addresses?", "कौन-सा protocol domain names को IP addresses में बदलता है?"], "opts": [["DHCP", "DHCP"], ["DNS", "DNS"], ["HTTP", "HTTP"], ["FTP", "FTP"]], "ans": 1, "exp": ["DNS (Domain Name System) नाम → IP address का translation करता है — Internet की phonebook. | Nukta: DNS = name→IP; ARP = IP→MAC; DHCP = IP बाँटना.", "DNS (Domain Name System) नाम → IP address का translation करता है — Internet की phonebook. | DNS = name→IP; ARP = IP→MAC; DHCP = IP बाँटना."], "src": "CN Topic Test 5.pdf + CN Topic Test-01.pdf", "sec": "Section E — Session, Presentation & Application Layer", "diff": "medium", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["What does a 'ping' command test?", "'ping' command क्या जाँचता है?"], "opts": [["IP configuration", "IP configuration"], ["Host reachability", "Host reachability"], ["DNS resolution", "DNS resolution"], ["Port scanning", "Port scanning"]], "ans": 1, "exp": ["Ping checks with ICMP Echo whether the other host is reachable and how long it takes. | Nukta: ping = 'क्या तुम वहाँ हो?' — reachability + round-trip time.", "Ping ICMP Echo भेजकर जाँचता है कि दूसरा host पहुँच में है या नहीं और कितनी देर लगी. | ping = 'क्या तुम वहाँ हो?' — reachability + round-trip time."], "src": "CN Topic Test 6.pdf", "sec": "Section E — Session, Presentation & Application Layer", "diff": "medium", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["Which HTTP status code means 'Forbidden'?", "कौन-सा HTTP status code का अर्थ है 'Forbidden'?"], "opts": [["200", "200"], ["301", "301"], ["403", "403"], ["404", "404"]], "ans": 2, "exp": ["HTTP 403 means the server understood the request but permission for access is denied. | Nukta: याद रखो: 200 OK, 301 Moved, 403 Forbidden, 404 Not Found, 500 Server Error.", "HTTP 403 का अर्थ है server ने request समझी, पर access की अनुमति नहीं है. | याद रखो: 200 OK, 301 Moved, 403 Forbidden, 404 Not Found, 500 Server Error."], "src": "Oliveboard SSC CGL Tier-2 bank", "sec": "Section E — Session, Presentation & Application Layer", "diff": "medium", "stype": "claimed_pyq_unverified", "style": "concept", "tags": ["SSC Computer Awareness"]}, {"q": ["Lightweight Directory Access Protocol (LDAP) is used for:", "Lightweight Directory Access Protocol (LDAP) किस काम आता है?"], "opts": [["Routing the packets", "Routing the packets"], ["Authentication and directory access", "Authentication and directory access"], ["Obtaining an IP address", "Obtaining an IP address"], ["Domain name resolving", "Domain name resolving"]], "ans": 1, "exp": ["LDAP directory services (users, groups, permissions की सूची) तक पहुँच देता है और authentication के लिए उपयोग होता है. | Nukta: LDAP = the network's 'address book + identity-desk counter'.", "LDAP directory services (users, groups, permissions की सूची) तक पहुँच देता है और authentication के लिए उपयोग होता है. | LDAP = network का 'पता-पुस्तिका + पहचान-पत्र काउंटर'."], "src": "Unit Test-4 Solution.pdf (OCR), p29", "sec": "Section E — Session, Presentation & Application Layer", "diff": "medium", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["Match TCP/IP layers and protocols — (P) Transport layer (Q) Network (internet) layer (R) Application layer; (1) ICMP (2) FTP (3) UDP. Which matching is correct?", "TCP/IP layers और protocols मिलाएँ — (P) Transport layer (Q) Network (internet) layer (R) Application layer; (1) ICMP (2) FTP (3) UDP. कौन-सा मिलान सही है?"], "opts": [["P-2, Q-1, R-3", "P-2, Q-1, R-3"], ["P-1, Q-2, R-3", "P-1, Q-2, R-3"], ["P-3, Q-1, R-2", "P-3, Q-1, R-2"], ["P-3, Q-2, R-1", "P-3, Q-2, R-1"]], "ans": 2, "exp": ["UDP Transport का है (P-3), ICMP Network का है (Q-1), FTP Application का है (R-2) — इसलिए P-3, Q-1, R-2. | Nukta: Layers याद रखो: Application = FTP/HTTP/SMTP/DNS; Transport = TCP/UDP; Internet = IP/ICMP/IGMP.", "UDP Transport का है (P-3), ICMP Network का है (Q-1), FTP Application का है (R-2) — इसलिए P-3, Q-1, R-2. | Layers याद रखो: Application = FTP/HTTP/SMTP/DNS; Transport = TCP/UDP; Internet = IP/ICMP/IGMP."], "src": "Random Test- Rajasthan PYQ.pdf (OCR) + answer_keys.py Q23", "sec": "Section E — Session, Presentation & Application Layer", "diff": "hard", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "match", "tags": ["GATE CS", "UGC-NET 087", "RPSC Programmer", "RPSC ACP/DD"]}, {"q": ["Which one of the following is NOT a client-server application?", "निम्न में से कौन-सा client-server application नहीं है?"], "opts": [["Internet Chat", "Internet Chat"], ["Web browsing", "Web browsing"], ["E-mail", "E-mail"], ["Ping", "Ping"]], "ans": 3, "exp": ["Ping एक diagnostic tool है जो ICMP Echo भेजता है — यह client-server application नहीं. बाकी तीनों में client और server होते हैं. | Nukta: RPSC 2011 official key (4). Ping = reachability जाँच, application service नहीं.", "Ping एक diagnostic tool है जो ICMP Echo भेजता है — यह client-server application नहीं. बाकी तीनों में client और server होते हैं. | RPSC 2011 official key (4). Ping = reachability जाँच, application service नहीं."], "src": "RPSC Programmer 2011 Paper-1 (via pyqp.in)", "sec": "Section E — Session, Presentation & Application Layer", "diff": "hard", "stype": "claimed_pyq_unverified", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["Which protocol is used for receiving an email?", "Email प्राप्त करने के लिए कौन-सा protocol उपयोग होता है?"], "opts": [["HTTP", "HTTP"], ["FTP", "FTP"], ["POP3", "POP3"], ["SSH", "SSH"]], "ans": 2, "exp": ["POP3 (Post Office Protocol v3) email लाने के लिए उपयोग होता है; भेजने के लिए SMTP. | Nukta: Mail की जोड़ी: भेजो SMTP (25), लो POP3 (110) या IMAP (143).", "POP3 (Post Office Protocol v3) email लाने के लिए उपयोग होता है; भेजने के लिए SMTP. | Mail की जोड़ी: भेजो SMTP (25), लो POP3 (110) या IMAP (143)."], "src": "RRB NTPC previous-year computer banks (via adda247 50-PYQ PDF)", "sec": "Section E — Session, Presentation & Application Layer", "diff": "medium", "stype": "claimed_pyq_unverified", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RRB Computer Awareness"]}, {"q": ["Which of the following is the odd one out?", "निम्न में से असंगत कौन-सा है?"], "opts": [["IMAP", "IMAP"], ["POP", "POP"], ["SNMP", "SNMP"], ["SMTP", "SMTP"]], "ans": 2, "exp": ["IMAP, POP और SMTP — तीनों email के protocols हैं; SNMP (Simple Network Management Protocol) devices manage करता है. | Nukta: Mail family: SMTP/POP3/IMAP; Management family: SNMP.", "IMAP, POP और SMTP — तीनों email के protocols हैं; SNMP (Simple Network Management Protocol) devices manage करता है. | Mail family: SMTP/POP3/IMAP; Management family: SNMP."], "src": "RRB NTPC previous-year computer banks (via adda247 50-PYQ PDF)", "sec": "Section E — Session, Presentation & Application Layer", "diff": "medium", "stype": "claimed_pyq_unverified", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RRB Computer Awareness"]}, {"q": ["For what application is the HTTP protocol used?", "HTTP protocol किस काम के लिए उपयोग होता है?"], "opts": [["To increase upload speed", "To increase upload speed"], ["To develop a website", "To develop a website"], ["To deliver data on the World Wide Web", "To deliver data on the World Wide Web"], ["To download images only", "To download images only"]], "ans": 2, "exp": ["HTTP (Hypertext Transfer Protocol) WWW पर data — web pages, images आदि — भेजने-लाने का मानक protocol है. | Nukta: SSC MTS official key (3). HTTP = web की धड़कन (port 80).", "HTTP (Hypertext Transfer Protocol) WWW पर data — web pages, images आदि — भेजने-लाने का मानक protocol है. | SSC MTS official key (3). HTTP = web की धड़कन (port 80)."], "src": "SSC MTS computer PYQ (via Testbook solved)", "sec": "Section E — Session, Presentation & Application Layer", "diff": "easy", "stype": "claimed_pyq_unverified", "style": "concept", "tags": ["SSC Computer Awareness"]}, {"q": ["ICMP is a network-layer protocol used by devices to diagnose network issues. ICMP stands for:", "ICMP network-layer protocol है जो devices को network समस्याएँ जाँचने में सहायता करता है. ICMP का पूरा नाम है:"], "opts": [["Internet Control Manage Process", "Internet Control Manage Process"], ["Internet Comfort Mass Protocol", "Internet Comfort Mass Protocol"], ["Information Control Manage Protocol", "Information Control Manage Protocol"], ["Internet Control Message Protocol", "Internet Control Message Protocol"]], "ans": 3, "exp": ["ICMP = Internet Control Message Protocol — ping और error messages इसी से जाते हैं. | Nukta: The other names are made up — the real name contains 'Control Message'.", "ICMP = Internet Control Message Protocol — ping और error messages इसी से जाते हैं. | बाकी नाम बनावटी हैं — असली नाम में 'Control Message' आता है."], "src": "IBPS PO Computer Awareness PYQ (via Testbook solved)", "sec": "Section E — Session, Presentation & Application Layer", "diff": "medium", "stype": "claimed_pyq_unverified", "style": "concept", "tags": ["IBPS Computer Awareness"]}, {"q": ["POP3 stands for:", "POP3 का पूरा नाम है:"], "opts": [["Peer to Peer Protocol", "Peer to Peer Protocol"], ["Peer to Post Protocol", "Peer to Post Protocol"], ["Peer Office Protocol", "Peer Office Protocol"], ["Post Office Protocol", "Post Office Protocol"]], "ans": 3, "exp": ["POP3 = Post Office Protocol (version 3) — यह mail server से आपकी mail लाता है, डाकखाने की तरह. | Nukta: POP = Post Office Protocol. याद रखो: POP3 mail लाता है, SMTP भेजता है.", "POP3 = Post Office Protocol (version 3) — यह mail server से आपकी mail लाता है, डाकखाने की तरह. | POP = Post Office Protocol. याद रखो: POP3 mail लाता है, SMTP भेजता है."], "src": "SBI/IBPS Computer Awareness Capsule 2018 (IBT India)", "sec": "Section E — Session, Presentation & Application Layer", "diff": "medium", "stype": "claimed_pyq_unverified", "style": "concept", "tags": ["IBPS Computer Awareness"]}, {"q": ["SLIP stands for:", "SLIP का पूरा नाम है:"], "opts": [["System Line Internet Protocol", "System Line Internet Protocol"], ["Serial Line Internet Protocol", "Serial Line Internet Protocol"], ["Signal Line Internet Protocol", "Signal Line Internet Protocol"], ["Signal Internet Protocol", "Signal Internet Protocol"]], "ans": 1, "exp": ["SLIP = Serial Line Internet Protocol — serial line (modem) पर IP चलाने का पुराना protocol; आजकल PPP उपयोग होता है. | Nukta: SLIP का उत्तराधिकारी PPP (byte-oriented) है — दोनों point-to-point.", "SLIP = Serial Line Internet Protocol — serial line (modem) पर IP चलाने का पुराना protocol; आजकल PPP उपयोग होता है. | SLIP का उत्तराधिकारी PPP (byte-oriented) है — दोनों point-to-point."], "src": "IBPS/banking computer banks (via tpointtech MCQ)", "sec": "Section E — Session, Presentation & Application Layer", "diff": "medium", "stype": "claimed_pyq_unverified", "style": "concept", "tags": ["IBPS Computer Awareness"]}, {"q": ["Which of the following is/are example(s) of stateful application layer protocols?\nI. HTTP    II. FTP    III. TCP    IV. POP3", "निम्न में से कौन-सा stateful application layer protocol का उदाहरण है?\nI. HTTP    II. FTP    III. TCP    IV. POP3"], "opts": [["I and II only", "केवल I और II"], ["II only", "केवल II"], ["I only", "केवल I"], ["II and III only", "केवल II और III"]], "ans": 1, "exp": ["FTP control connection par session state rakhta hai (stateful); HTTP 1.0 request ke baad bhool jata hai (stateless); TCP application layer ka protocol hi nahi; POP3 independent commands — sirf II (GATE 2016 key). | Nukta: TCP ko application protocol samajhna option jaal hai; HTTP stateful sirf modern keep-alive mein lagta hai.", "FTP control connection पर state रखता है (stateful); HTTP 1.0 भूल जाता है; TCP application का protocol नहीं; POP3 स्वतंत्र — केवल II। | TCP application protocol नहीं; HTTP सिर्फ़ आधुनिक keep-alive में stateful लगता है।"], "src": "GATE CS 2016 Set-1", "sec": "Section E — Session, Presentation & Application Layer", "diff": "hard", "stype": "claimed_pyq_unverified", "style": "concept", "tags": ["GATE CS"]}, {"q": ["Identify the correct sequence in which the following packets are transmitted by a host when a browser requests a web page from a remote server, assuming that the host has just been restarted:", "मान लीजिए host अभी-अभी restart हुआ है और browser एक remote server से web page माँगता है। निम्न packets सही क्रम में transmit होंगे:"], "opts": [["HTTP GET request, DNS query, TCP SYN", "HTTP GET request, DNS query, TCP SYN"], ["DNS query, HTTP GET request, TCP SYN", "DNS query, HTTP GET request, TCP SYN"], ["DNS query, TCP SYN, HTTP GET request", "DNS query, TCP SYN, HTTP GET request"], ["TCP SYN, DNS query, HTTP GET request", "TCP SYN, DNS query, HTTP GET request"]], "ans": 2, "exp": ["Restart ke baad cache khaali: pehle DNS query se server ka IP milta hai, phir TCP three-way handshake (SYN...), tabhi HTTP GET ja sakta hai (GATE 2016 key). | Nukta: GET pehle ja hi nahi sakta — connection bina handshake ke nahi banti; restart yaani DNS cache bhi khaali.", "Restart पर cache ख़ाली: पहले DNS से IP, फिर TCP handshake (SYN...), तब HTTP GET (GATE 2016 key). | GET पहले नहीं जा सकता; restart में DNS cache भी ख़ाली।"], "src": "GATE CS 2016 Set-2", "sec": "Section E — Session, Presentation & Application Layer", "diff": "hard", "stype": "claimed_pyq_unverified", "style": "concept", "tags": ["GATE CS"]}, {"q": ["Which of the following protocol pairs can be used to send and retrieve e-mails (in that order)?", "ई-मेल भेजने और प्राप्त करने (इसी क्रम में) के लिए निम्न में से किस protocol जोड़ी का प्रयोग हो सकता है?"], "opts": [["SMTP and POP3", "SMTP और POP3"], ["POP3 and SMTP", "POP3 और SMTP"], ["IMAP and SMTP", "IMAP और SMTP"], ["SMTP and IMAP only", "केवल SMTP और IMAP"]], "ans": 0, "exp": ["SMTP mail bhejne (push) ke liye; POP3 mail lane (retrieve) ke liye — yeh classic jodi GATE 2019 ka answer hai. | Nukta: Ulti jodi (POP3 and SMTP) order ke against hai; IMAP bhi retrieve karta hai par sabse common jodi SMTP+POP3 hai.", "SMTP भेजने (push) के लिए; POP3 लाने (retrieve) के लिए — यही जोड़ी (GATE 2019)। | उल्टी जोड़ी गलत; IMAP भी retrieve करता है पर सबसे सामान्य जोड़ी SMTP+POP3।"], "src": "GATE CS 2019", "sec": "Section E — Session, Presentation & Application Layer", "diff": "hard", "stype": "claimed_pyq_unverified", "style": "concept", "tags": ["GATE CS"]}, {"q": ["Consider a long-lived TCP session with an end-to-end bandwidth of 1 Gbps (= 10⁹ bits/second). The session starts with a sequence number of 1234. The minimum time (in seconds, rounded to the closest integer) before this sequence number can be used again is ______.", "एक लंबी TCP session की bandwidth 1 Gbps (= 10⁹ bits/second) है और वह sequence number 1234 से शुरू होती है। इस sequence number के पुनः प्रयोग से पहले न्यूनतम समय (seconds में, निकटतम पूर्णांक) कितना है?"], "opts": [["34", "34"], ["35", "35"], ["43", "43"], ["32", "32"]], "ans": 0, "exp": ["TCP sequence numbers bytes count karte hain: 2³² bytes ka space; 1 Gbps = 1.25×10⁸ bytes/sec → 2³² ÷ 1.25×10⁸ = 34.36 s → 34 second. | Nukta: Bits mein hisaab karke 4 s; ya 2³² bits samajh kar galat number — bytes ka chakkar hai.", "TCP sequence numbers bytes गिनते हैं: 2³² bytes; 1 Gbps = 1.25×10⁸ B/s → 34.36 s → 34 second. | Bits में हिसाब लगाना (4 s) या 2³² bits मानना गलत।"], "src": "GATE CS 2018", "sec": "Section E — Session, Presentation & Application Layer", "diff": "hard", "stype": "claimed_pyq_unverified", "style": "numerical", "tags": ["GATE CS"]}, {"q": ["In the TCP three-way handshake, host P sends a connection request to Q with SYN = 1, SEQ = X, ACK = 0. Q accepts the connection. Which of the following represents the information in the TCP segment header sent by Q to P?", "TCP three-way handshake में host P, Q को connection request भेजता है: SYN = 1, SEQ = X, ACK = 0। Q connection स्वीकार करता है। Q द्वारा P को भेजे segment header में क्या होगा?"], "opts": [["SYN = 1, SEQ = Y, ACK = X", "SYN = 1, SEQ = Y, ACK = X"], ["SYN = 1, SEQ = X, ACK = Y", "SYN = 1, SEQ = X, ACK = Y"], ["SYN = 1, SEQ = Y, ACK = X+1", "SYN = 1, SEQ = Y, ACK = X+1"], ["SYN = 0, SEQ = Y, ACK = X+1", "SYN = 0, SEQ = Y, ACK = X+1"]], "ans": 2, "exp": ["Q apna random sequence number Y bhejta hai, SYN=1 rakhta hai (apna SYN), aur acknowledge karta hai X ka — agla byte X+1 (GATE 2021 key: III). | Nukta: ACK = X galat (yeh khud ko X+1 expect karna hua); SYN=0 second segment jaisa hota.", "Q अपना sequence number Y भेजता है, SYN=1, और X का ack = X+1 (GATE 2021 key: III)। | ACK = X गलत (X+1 अपेक्षित); SYN=0 दूसरे जैसा।"], "src": "GATE CS 2021 Set-2", "sec": "Section E — Session, Presentation & Application Layer", "diff": "hard", "stype": "claimed_pyq_unverified", "style": "concept", "tags": ["GATE CS"]}, {"q": ["Consider data transfer using TCP over a 1 Gbps link. Assuming that the maximum segment lifetime (MSL) is set to 60 seconds, the minimum number of bits required for the sequence number field of the TCP header, to prevent the sequence number space from wrapping around during the MSL, is ______.", "1 Gbps link पर TCP से data transfer हो रहा है। Maximum segment lifetime (MSL) 60 seconds है। MSL के दौरान sequence number space के wrap होने से बचने के लिए TCP header के sequence number field में न्यूनतम कितने bits चाहिए?"], "opts": [["32", "32"], ["33", "33"], ["34", "34"], ["36", "36"]], "ans": 1, "exp": ["1 Gbps = 1.25×10⁸ bytes/sec; 60 s में 7.5×10⁹ bytes; 2³² = 4.29×10⁹ < 7.5×10⁹ < 2³³ = 8.59×10⁹ — इसलिए कम से कम 33 bits (GATE 2022 key). | Nukta: 32 bits mein space 60 s के लिए kam padta hai; 34/36 zyada hain (minimum pucha hai).", "1.25×10⁸ B/s × 60 = 7.5×10⁹ bytes; 2³² < 7.5×10⁹ < 2³³ — इसलिए 33 bits। | 32 कम पड़ता; 34/36 ज़्यादा (न्यूनतम पूछा है)।"], "src": "GATE CS 2022", "sec": "Section E — Session, Presentation & Application Layer", "diff": "hard", "stype": "claimed_pyq_unverified", "style": "numerical", "tags": ["GATE CS"]}, {"q": ["A TCP client and server complete data transfer. The client calls close; a FIN segment is sent to the server, which responds with an ACK received by the client. As per the TCP connection state diagram (RFC 793), in which state does the client-side TCP connection wait for the FIN from the server?", "TCP client-server का data transfer पूरा हुआ। Client close करता है; server को FIN जाता है; server का ACK client को मिलता है। RFC 793 की state diagram के अनुसार client-side connection server के FIN की प्रतीक्षा किस state में करती है?"], "opts": [["TIME_WAIT", "TIME_WAIT"], ["FIN_WAIT_2", "FIN_WAIT_2"], ["CLOSE_WAIT", "CLOSE_WAIT"], ["LAST_ACK", "LAST_ACK"]], "ans": 1, "exp": ["Client: FIN_WAIT_1 (FIN bheja) → ACK mila → FIN_WAIT_2 (server ke FIN ka intezar) → phir TIME_WAIT. CLOSE_WAIT server-side hoti hai. | Nukta: TIME_WAIT aakhri state hai (dono FIN ke baad); CLOSE_WAIT server ki hoti hai.", "Client: FIN_WAIT_1 (FIN भेजा) → ACK मिला → FIN_WAIT_2 (server के FIN का इंतज़ार) → फिर TIME_WAIT. CLOSE_WAIT server-side। | TIME_WAIT अंत में; CLOSE_WAIT server की।"], "src": "GATE CS 2017 Set-1", "sec": "Section E — Session, Presentation & Application Layer", "diff": "hard", "stype": "claimed_pyq_unverified", "style": "concept", "tags": ["GATE CS"]}, {"q": ["In the TCP three-way handshake, let the three packets exchanged during connection establishment be P1, P2 and P3 in order. Which of the following is TRUE about the TCP header flags set in these packets?", "TCP three-way handshake में connection establishment के दौरान तीन packets P1, P2 और P3 (इसी क्रम में) बदले जाते हैं। इनमें सेट TCP header flags के बारे में क्या सही है?"], "opts": [["P1: SYN; P2: SYN, ACK; P3: ACK", "P1: SYN; P2: SYN, ACK; P3: ACK"], ["P1: SYN, ACK; P2: ACK; P3: FIN", "P1: SYN, ACK; P2: ACK; P3: FIN"], ["P1: SYN; P2: ACK; P3: FIN", "P1: SYN; P2: ACK; P3: FIN"], ["P1: ACK; P2: SYN; P3: ACK", "P1: ACK; P2: SYN; P3: ACK"]], "ans": 0, "exp": ["Classic handshake: P1 SYN (request), P2 SYN+ACK (server ka SYN + acknowledgement), P3 ACK (final) — flags ka yehi standard pattern hai (GATE 2025). | Nukta: FIN connection release ka flag hai; pehle packet par ACK kabhi nahi hota.", "क्लासिक handshake: P1 SYN, P2 SYN+ACK, P3 ACK — यही मानक पैटर्न (GATE 2025)। | FIN release का flag है; पहले packet पर ACK नहीं होता।"], "src": "GATE CS 2025 Set-1", "sec": "Section E — Session, Presentation & Application Layer", "diff": "hard", "stype": "claimed_pyq_unverified", "style": "concept", "tags": ["GATE CS"]}, {"q": ["The World Wide Web (WWW) is:", "World Wide Web (WWW) क्या है?"], "opts": [["another name for the Internet", "Internet का दूसरा नाम"], ["a worldwide connection of computers", "कंप्यूटरों का विश्वव्यापी जुड़ाव"], ["a worldwide collection of information", "सूचना का विश्वव्यापी संग्रह"], ["a collection of linked information residing on computers connected by the Internet", "Internet से जुड़े कंप्यूटरों पर रखी link की गई सूचनाओं का संग्रह"]], "ans": 3, "exp": ["WWW Internet par hosted linked documents (web pages) ka sangrah hai — Internet khud network infrastructure hai, WWW uspar chalne wali information service. | Nukta: Internet aur WWW ko same bolna sabse common galti hai; 'connection of computers' to network ki paribhasha hai.", "WWW, Internet पर hosted linked documents का संग्रह है — Internet खुद network है, WWW उसकी information service। | Internet और WWW को एक मानना सबसे आम गलती; 'connection' तो network है।"], "src": "EMRS PGT Computer Science", "sec": "Section E — Session, Presentation & Application Layer", "diff": "hard", "stype": "claimed_pyq_unverified", "style": "concept", "tags": ["EMRS PGT CS"]}, {"q": ["Which protocol is used to retrieve e-mails and keep them on the server as well?", "कौन-सा protocol e-mail लाता है और उन्हें server पर भी रखता है?"], "opts": [["SMTP", "SMTP"], ["POP3", "POP3"], ["IMAP", "IMAP"], ["FTP", "FTP"]], "ans": 2, "exp": ["IMAP server par messages manage karta hai; POP3 download karke delete. | Nukta: SMTP bhejne ke liye.", "IMAP server पर रखता है; POP3 download+delete। | SMTP भेजने के लिए।"], "src": "Practice — original (textbook-based)", "sec": "Section E — Session, Presentation & Application Layer", "diff": "medium", "stype": "original_practice", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer", "Practice Set"]}, {"q": ["Translation between ASCII and EBCDIC is performed by the:", "ASCII और EBCDIC के बीच अनुवाद करती है:"], "opts": [["Application layer", "Application layer"], ["Presentation layer", "Presentation layer"], ["Data link layer", "Data link layer"], ["Physical layer", "Physical layer"]], "ans": 1, "exp": ["Presentation = translation, encryption, compression. | Nukta: Application user services deta hai.", "Presentation = translation। | Application services।"], "src": "Practice — original (textbook-based)", "sec": "Section E — Session, Presentation & Application Layer", "diff": "medium", "stype": "original_practice", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer", "Practice Set"]}, {"q": ["HTTPS uses which protocol for security?", "HTTPS सुरक्षा के लिए कौन-सा protocol प्रयोग करता है?"], "opts": [["SSH", "SSH"], ["SSL/TLS", "SSL/TLS"], ["SNMP", "SNMP"], ["ICMP", "ICMP"]], "ans": 1, "exp": ["HTTPS = HTTP + SSL/TLS. | Nukta: SSH remote login ka.", "HTTPS = HTTP + SSL/TLS। | SSH remote login का।"], "src": "Practice — original (textbook-based)", "sec": "Section E — Session, Presentation & Application Layer", "diff": "medium", "stype": "original_practice", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer", "Practice Set"]}, {"q": ["DHCP is used to:", "DHCP प्रयोग होता है:"], "opts": [["Resolve names to IPs", "नामों को IP में बदलने के लिए"], ["Assign IP configuration automatically", "IP configuration स्वतः देने के लिए"], ["Encrypt e-mails", "E-mail encrypt करने के लिए"], ["Route packets", "Packets route करने के लिए"]], "ans": 1, "exp": ["DHCP automatic IP, mask, gateway, DNS deta hai. | Nukta: Naam→IP DNS karta hai.", "DHCP स्वतः IP देता है। | नाम→IP DNS।"], "src": "Practice — original (textbook-based)", "sec": "Section E — Session, Presentation & Application Layer", "diff": "medium", "stype": "original_practice", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer", "Practice Set"]}, {"q": ["In FTP, the control connection uses port number:", "FTP में control connection किस port पर चलती है?"], "opts": [["20", "20"], ["21", "21"], ["25", "25"], ["80", "80"]], "ans": 1, "exp": ["Control = 21; data = 20. | Nukta: 20 data connection.", "Control = 21; data = 20। | 20 data connection।"], "src": "Practice — original (textbook-based)", "sec": "Section E — Session, Presentation & Application Layer", "diff": "medium", "stype": "original_practice", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer", "Practice Set"]}, {"q": ["Which of the following is a stateless protocol?", "निम्न में से कौन stateless protocol है?"], "opts": [["FTP", "FTP"], ["HTTP", "HTTP"], ["Telnet", "Telnet"], ["TCP", "TCP"]], "ans": 1, "exp": ["HTTP har request independent — stateless. | Nukta: FTP control connection stateful.", "HTTP — stateless। | FTP stateful।"], "src": "Practice — original (textbook-based)", "sec": "Section E — Session, Presentation & Application Layer", "diff": "medium", "stype": "original_practice", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer", "Practice Set"]}, {"q": ["DHCP uses which pair of UDP ports (server port, client port)?", "DHCP कौन-सी UDP ports की जोड़ी प्रयोग करता है (server port, client port)?"], "opts": [["67 and 68", "67 और 68"], ["69 and 70", "69 और 70"], ["53 and 54", "53 और 54"], ["20 and 21", "20 और 21"]], "ans": 0, "exp": ["DHCP server = UDP 67, DHCP client = UDP 68 (DORA process in dono ports par). | Nukta: 69 = TFTP; 53 = DNS; 20/21 = FTP data/control.", "DHCP server = UDP 67, client = UDP 68 (DORA इन्हीं पर)। | 69 = TFTP; 53 = DNS; 20/21 = FTP।"], "src": "Practice — original (textbook-based)", "sec": "Section E — Session, Presentation & Application Layer", "diff": "medium", "stype": "original_practice", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer", "Practice Set"]}, {"q": ["In the DHCP DORA process, if two DHCP servers send OFFERs, the client usually accepts:", "DHCP DORA process में यदि दो DHCP servers OFFER भेजें, तो client सामान्यतः स्वीकार करता है:"], "opts": [["The first OFFER received", "सबसे पहले प्राप्त OFFER"], ["The OFFER with the longest lease", "सबसे लंबी lease वाला OFFER"], ["Both and merges them", "दोनों, उन्हें मिलाकर"], ["Neither — it uses a static IP", "कोई नहीं — static IP लेता है"]], "ans": 0, "exp": ["DORA = Discover → Offer → Request → Acknowledge. Client pehli Offer leta hai aur Request broadcast karta hai (baaki servers ko pata chalta hai ki unka offer nahi liya). Pattern: SSC CGL/IBPS + Network+. | Nukta: Do OFFERs ke beech 'race' hoti hai — jo pehle pahunche.", "DORA = Discover → Offer → Request → Ack. Client पहली Offer लेता है। Pattern: SSC CGL + Network+। | दो OFFERs में race — जो पहले पहुँचे।"], "src": "Practice — original (SSC CGL/IBPS exam-pattern, textbook-based)", "sec": "Section E — Session, Presentation & Application Layer", "diff": "hard", "stype": "original_practice", "style": "concept", "tags": ["SSC Computer Awareness", "Practice Set"]}, {"q": ["The first line of an HTTP request message is called the:", "HTTP request message की पहली पंक्ति कहलाती है:"], "opts": [["Request line", "Request line"], ["Header line", "Header line"], ["Status line", "Status line"], ["Body line", "Body line"]], "ans": 0, "exp": ["Request line = METHOD URI HTTP/VERSION (jaise 'GET /index.html HTTP/1.1'). Response message ki pehli line STATUS line hoti hai. | Nukta: Status line sirf RESPONSE mein hoti hai.", "Request line = METHOD URI HTTP/VERSION। Response की पहली line = status line। | Status line सिर्फ RESPONSE में होती है।"], "src": "Practice — original (textbook-based)", "sec": "Section E — Session, Presentation & Application Layer", "diff": "medium", "stype": "original_practice", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer", "Practice Set"]}, {"q": ["By default, HTTP/1.1 connections are:", "डिफ़ॉल्ट रूप से, HTTP/1.1 connections होते हैं:"], "opts": [["Persistent (keep-alive)", "Persistent (keep-alive)"], ["Non-persistent", "Non-persistent"], ["Simplex", "Simplex"], ["Datagram-based", "Datagram-based"]], "ans": 0, "exp": ["HTTP/1.1 default persistent connection: ek TCP connection par kai request/response (Connection: close se band hota hai). HTTP/1.0 default non-persistent tha. | Nukta: Persistent = connection reuse; non-persistent = har object par nayi connection.", "HTTP/1.1 default persistent: एक connection पर कई request/response; HTTP/1.0 non-persistent था। | Persistent = connection reuse; non-persistent = हर object पर नई connection।"], "src": "Practice — original (textbook-based)", "sec": "Section E — Session, Presentation & Application Layer", "diff": "medium", "stype": "original_practice", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer", "Practice Set"]}, {"q": ["In HTTP, a conditional GET (using If-Modified-Since) allows:", "HTTP में conditional GET (If-Modified-Since के साथ) संभव बनाता है:"], "opts": [["Cache validation — the server sends a 304 Not Modified instead of the object if unchanged", "Cache validation — अपरिवर्तित होने पर server वस्तु के बजाय 304 Not Modified भेजे"], ["Automatic language translation", "स्वतः भाषा अनुवाद"], ["Password-free login", "बिना password login"], ["Parallel downloads", "समांतर downloads"]], "ans": 0, "exp": ["Conditional GET: browser poochta hai 'kitne din se badla?'; agar object same hai to sirf 304 header — bandwidth bachti hai. | Nukta: 304 = Not Modified; 200 = OK (poora content).", "Conditional GET: object अपरिवर्तित हो तो सिर्फ 304 Not Modified — bandwidth बचती है। | 304 = Not Modified; 200 = OK।"], "src": "Practice — original (textbook-based)", "sec": "Section E — Session, Presentation & Application Layer", "diff": "medium", "stype": "original_practice", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer", "Practice Set"]}, {"q": ["Which of the following is NOT a valid HTTP status code?", "निम्न में से कौन-सा वैध HTTP status code नहीं है?"], "opts": [["250", "250"], ["200", "200"], ["404", "404"], ["503", "503"]], "ans": 0, "exp": ["200 = OK, 3xx redirection (301/302/304), 4xx client errors (400/403/404), 5xx server errors (500/503). '250' SMTP ka 'mail action ok' code hai, HTTP ka nahi. | Nukta: HTTP 2xx family: 200, 201, 204... 250 nahi.", "200=OK; 3xx=redirection; 4xx=client error; 5xx=server error। 250 SMTP का code है। | HTTP 2xx: 200, 201, 204... 250 नहीं।"], "src": "Practice — original (textbook-based)", "sec": "Section E — Session, Presentation & Application Layer", "diff": "hard", "stype": "original_practice", "style": "concept", "tags": ["GATE CS", "UGC-NET 087", "RPSC Programmer", "RPSC ACP/DD", "Practice Set"]}, {"q": ["The default connection type used by HTTP is _____", ""], "opts": [["Persistent", ""], ["Non-persistent", ""], ["Either of the mentioned", ""], ["None of the mentioned", ""]], "ans": 0, "exp": ["Nukta: ⚠ CAUTION — answer NOT verified: compiled-bank source key = (A). Please verify before relying.", "⚠ सावधान — उत्तर verify नहीं है: source key = (A)। कृपया उपयोग से पहले स्वयं जाँच कर लें।"], "src": "Repo: DCN_MCQ-Ashwini-.pdf (new/ 2026 drop)", "sec": "Section E — Session, Presentation & Application Layer", "diff": "medium", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["RSMSSB Informatics Assistant", "SSC Computer Awareness", "RPSC Programmer"]}, {"q": ["Find the oddly matched HTTP status codes", ""], "opts": [["200 OK", ""], ["400 Bad Request", ""], ["301 Moved permanently", ""], ["304 Not Found", ""]], "ans": 3, "exp": ["Nukta: ⚠ CAUTION — answer NOT verified: compiled-bank source key = (D). Please verify before relying.", "⚠ सावधान — उत्तर verify नहीं है: source key = (D)। कृपया उपयोग से पहले स्वयं जाँच कर लें।"], "src": "Repo: DCN_MCQ-Ashwini-.pdf (new/ 2026 drop)", "sec": "Section E — Session, Presentation & Application Layer", "diff": "hard", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["GATE CS", "UGC-NET 087", "RPSC Programmer", "RPSC ACP/DD"]}, {"q": ["Which of the following is not correct ?", ""], "opts": [["Web cache doesnt has its own disk space", ""], ["Web cache can act both like server and client", ""], ["Web cache might reduce the response time", ""], ["Web cache contains copies of recently requested objects", ""]], "ans": 0, "exp": ["Nukta: ⚠ CAUTION — answer NOT verified: compiled-bank source key = (A). Please verify before relying.", "⚠ सावधान — उत्तर verify नहीं है: source key = (A)। कृपया उपयोग से पहले स्वयं जाँच कर लें।"], "src": "Repo: DCN_MCQ-Ashwini-.pdf (new/ 2026 drop)", "sec": "Section E — Session, Presentation & Application Layer", "diff": "hard", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["GATE CS", "UGC-NET 087", "RPSC Programmer", "RPSC ACP/DD"]}, {"q": ["Which of the following is present in both an HTTP request line and a status line?", ""], "opts": [["HTTP version number", ""], ["URL", ""], ["Method", ""], ["None of the mentioned", ""]], "ans": 0, "exp": ["Nukta: ⚠ CAUTION — answer NOT verified: compiled-bank source key = (A). Please verify before relying.", "⚠ सावधान — उत्तर verify नहीं है: source key = (A)। कृपया उपयोग से पहले स्वयं जाँच कर लें।"], "src": "Repo: DCN_MCQ-Ashwini-.pdf (new/ 2026 drop)", "sec": "Section E — Session, Presentation & Application Layer", "diff": "hard", "stype": "repository_internal", "style": "concept", "tags": ["GATE CS", "UGC-NET 087", "RPSC Programmer", "RPSC ACP/DD"]}, {"q": ["Identify the incorrect statement", ""], "opts": [["FTP stands for File Transfer Protocol", ""], ["FTP uses two parallel TCP connections", ""], ["FTP sends its control information in-band", ""], ["FTP sends exactly one file over the data connection", ""]], "ans": 2, "exp": ["Nukta: ⚠ CAUTION — answer NOT verified: compiled-bank source key = (C). Please verify before relying.", "⚠ सावधान — उत्तर verify नहीं है: source key = (C)। कृपया उपयोग से पहले स्वयं जाँच कर लें।"], "src": "Repo: DCN_MCQ-Ashwini-.pdf (new/ 2026 drop)", "sec": "Section E — Session, Presentation & Application Layer", "diff": "hard", "stype": 